{
	file.0000000000000001.title: "Warbucks Chemistry: The Demigod's Codex"
	chapter_group.2DCF10F76EBF2A74.title: "The Demigod's Path (Main Questline)"
	chapter_group.0BF9E0EEF61D9FC8.title: "The Demigod's Market"
	chapter_group.71F0A542B0668E9D.title: "Tools and Gear"
	chapter_group.65B0C73DACFF2083.title: "Storage"
	chapter_group.78721B1463D42BF6.title: "Logistics"
	chapter_group.22D02A9EFAC9B3FB.title: "Resources"
	chapter_group.1D472E4B7694487A.title: "Tech"
	chapter_group.3B51167C89EBE873.title: "Chemistry"
	chapter_group.3798A6859710A136.title: "Energy"
	chapter_group.517E2EE5EE2E76FF.title: "Magic"
	chapter_group.4045A6EE7751118B.title: "Exploration"
	chapter.4335527ACA7CF750.title: "Welcome"
	chapter.4335527ACA7CF750.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Read this first: who you are, and where to go next."
	]
	quest.54E4F62471779F14.title: "Welcome, Demigod"
	quest.54E4F62471779F14.quest_subtitle: "Your first page of the Demigod's Codex"
	quest.54E4F62471779F14.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember light pouring from your hands. Now there is only dirt under your nails.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Welcome to Warbucks Chemistry. You're a demigod who lost your power, and you win it back by mastering chemistry: taking matter apart into elements and building it up again."
		"&eHow:&r the four signposts around this quest point to the pages that matter most. Read them, then take the road below to Getting Started."
		"&eTip:&r the sleeping bag skips the night without moving your spawn point."
	]
	quest.022F679599389147.title: "The Demigod's Path"
	quest.022F679599389147.quest_subtitle: "The main story, one tier at a time"
	quest.022F679599389147.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Demigod's Path is the spine of the book: eight tiers, each opened by a chemistry milestone. Fire and bronze, then steel, hydrogen, electricity, acids, plastics, the atom and antimatter."
		"&eHow:&r every other page hangs off it. Modern Industrialization's voltages (LV, MV, HV, EV) set the pace, and other mods open alongside."
		"&eTip:&r if a recipe looks different from what you remember, it was changed on purpose. JEI always shows the real one."
	]
	quest.32306651C1085697.title: "The Demigod's Market"
	quest.32306651C1085697.quest_subtitle: "What your Demigod Tokens buy"
	quest.32306651C1085697.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r most quests pay Demigod Tokens. The Market turns them into supplies and comforts, never into shortcuts past a tier."
		"&eHow:&r open the Demigod's Market pages, or search &eDemigod Token&r in JEI and press &eU&r: every trade is a crafting recipe."
		"&eTip:&r the Market sells more of what you have already made yourself, so finishing quests opens new stalls."
	]
	quest.745DBEEE9AE746C7.title: "Tips and Tricks"
	quest.745DBEEE9AE746C7.quest_subtitle: "Keys, shortcuts and how this pack differs"
	quest.745DBEEE9AE746C7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Tips and Tricks page collects short lessons: JEI lookups, Jade, claiming land, Ultimine, waystones, perks and the pack's own changes."
		"&eHow:&r &eR&r / &eU&r over an item for recipes and uses, &eM&r for the claim map, hold &e`&r to vein mine. The page has the rest."
		"&eTip:&r give the game about 8 to 10 GB of memory in your launcher's instance settings."
	]
	quest.5EFC77C0525603E5.title: "Building Tips"
	quest.5EFC77C0525603E5.quest_subtitle: "Make your base look like a god lives there"
	quest.5EFC77C0525603E5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Building Tips pages are a catalogue of the pack's building tools and decoration: gadgets, chisels, framed blocks, stone, wood, glass, light, furniture and a proper laboratory."
		"&eHow:&r everything there is optional. Dip in whenever your base needs a new look."
		"&eTip:&r a construction stick and a stonecutter save more time than anything else on that page."
	]
	quest.61103C80A99526F9.title: "Getting Started"
	quest.61103C80A99526F9.quest_subtitle: "Your first day begins here"
	quest.61103C80A99526F9.quest_desc: [
		"&6The world is waiting to be taken apart and put back together.&r"
		"&eHow:&r open &eGetting Started&r and take your first step: wood, stone, food and a safe first night."
		"&eTip:&r you can come back to this page any time from the top of the chapter list."
	]
	quest.14851AEFE672966D.title: "Who You Were"
	quest.14851AEFE672966D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a god's memory, a chemist's method"
	quest.14851AEFE672966D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Some things you still know without being taught: water is two parts hydrogen to one of oxygen, and fire is a reaction, not a spirit.&r"
		"&eChemistry:&r about 90 elements occur in nature. Rearrange their atoms and you change what a thing is. That's the whole game."
		"&eTip:&r every chapter of this book returns one more piece of what you once were."
	]
	quest.5F462A144226867C.title: "The Periodic Table"
	quest.5F462A144226867C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: 118 known elements"
	quest.5F462A144226867C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r chemists know 118 elements. Each is defined by its number of protons, its &eatomic number&r."
		"&eChemistry:&r Mendeleev ordered the table in 1869 by repeating properties and left gaps for elements nobody had found. Gallium and germanium later filled them almost exactly as he predicted."
		"&eTip:&r the Periodic Table page tracks every element you collect, and whole groups grant permanent perks."
	]
	chapter.29A6965304E1D4DA.title: "The Demigod's Market"
	chapter.29A6965304E1D4DA.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Spend your Demigod Tokens: supplies and comforts, never shortcuts."
	]
	quest.7CD14A8D2BC590A9.title: "The Market"
	quest.7CD14A8D2BC590A9.quest_subtitle: "What Demigod Tokens are for"
	quest.7CD14A8D2BC590A9.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember offerings left at your altar. Now the world pays you in coins instead.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Demigod Tokens are the reward currency of this book. You trade them for supplies by crafting, with no shopkeeper and no server plugin."
		"&eHow:&r every shop trade is a shapeless crafting recipe: put tokens in a crafting grid and the item appears."
		"&eHow:&r the price list is JEI: search &eDemigod Token&r and press &eU&r (uses). Every trade shows as a crafting recipe. Do the same for the Greater Demigod Token."
		"&eTip:&r the crafting shop sells raw supplies and comforts, never anything that skips a tier. Copies of machines you have already built are in the Machine Shop quests."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eWhat tokens never buy:&r the shop skips boring gathering (sand, gravel, string, torches), never learning. If a trade seems missing, it was left out on purpose."
		"&eChemistry:&r a bag of raw ore is not a refinery. Raw tin still needs your crusher, raw titanium still needs your blast furnace."
	]
	quest.2B95087344F45A1D.title: "Where Tokens Come From"
	quest.2B95087344F45A1D.quest_subtitle: "Every quest pays"
	quest.2B95087344F45A1D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r almost every quest pays tokens, scaled by tier: 1 per quest at the start, 2 in the steam and Nether chapters, 3 at LV and MV, 4 at HV, 5 at EV, 8 in space."
		"&eHow:&r milestone quests (the big ones) pay double and also roll that tier's reward table. Optional side quests pay 1 or 2."
		"&eTip:&r on a team, rewards go to each player who claims them, so everyone builds their own purse."
	]
	quest.730D392B8D2C31C6.title: "The Price Bands"
	quest.730D392B8D2C31C6.quest_subtitle: "Small, medium and large trades"
	quest.730D392B8D2C31C6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the shop has three price bands. Small (1 to 3 tokens): cheap stacks of things you'd otherwise spend an afternoon gathering. Medium and large are on the next pages."
		"&eHow:&r 1 token: 32 torches, 16 bread, 8 bottles o' enchanting, 32 bone meal, 64 sand, 64 gravel or 32 clay balls."
		"&eHow:&r 2 tokens: 16 iron ingots, 16 coke, 16 rubber sheets, 16 fire clay dust, 32 salt dust, 16 string, 16 leather or a sleeping bag."
		"&eHow:&r 3 tokens: 8 osmium ingots, 2 backpack upgrade bases, 16 gunpowder, 16 slime balls, 32 redstone or 16 lapis."
		"&eTip:&r sand and gravel are the best early value: concrete, glass and silicon all start there."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eMedium band (4 to 8 tokens):&r raw ores (you still process them yourself) and drops you would otherwise farm."
		"&eHow:&r 4 tokens: a Warp Stone, 32 raw copper, 16 raw tin, 16 raw lead, 16 bauxite dust, 32 quartz or 32 glowstone dust."
		"&eHow:&r 5: 16 raw nickel, 8 ender pearls, 4 phantom membranes, 16 amethyst. 6: 8 blaze rods, 4 ghast tears, 16 certus quartz, 8 source gems."
		"&eHow:&r 7: 8 raw titanium or 2 name tags. 8: 8 raw tungsten or 32 prismarine shards."
		"&eTip:&r raw ore bought here is worth up to 5x once your Mekanism line is running. Buy late, process well."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eLarge band (Greater Tokens):&r the big trades cost Greater Demigod Tokens, not regular ones."
		"&eHow:&r 1 Greater: 4 golden apples, 4 diamonds, 16 emeralds or a saddle. 2: 2 shulker shells, a heart of the sea or a netherite scrap."
		"&eHow:&r 3 Greater: a totem of undying or 4 echo shards. 4 Greater: an enchanted golden apple."
		"&eTip:&r shulker shells mean shulker boxes. Many players find that the best trade in the shop."
	]
	quest.003F5C5CD886D522.title: "The Exchange"
	quest.003F5C5CD886D522.quest_subtitle: "Nine tokens make one Greater Token"
	quest.003F5C5CD886D522.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Greater Demigod Token is worth 9 Demigod Tokens, and the trade works both ways."
		"&eHow:&r 9 tokens in a crafting grid make 1 Greater Token. 1 Greater Token alone in the grid gives the 9 back."
		"&eTip:&r late-tier milestones and boss loot sometimes pay Greater Tokens directly."
	]
	quest.78DBBB51C5B3D742.title: "Market Day: Early"
	quest.78DBBB51C5B3D742.quest_subtitle: "Hold 10 tokens; pick a comfort"
	quest.78DBBB51C5B3D742.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a reward for saving. Hold 10 Demigod Tokens at once and choose one comfort: a sleeping bag, a Warp Stone, backpack upgrade bases or a saddle."
		"&eHow:&r the tokens are only checked, not taken. Spend them afterwards if you like."
		"&eTip:&r the Warp Stone is the pick if you explore a lot."
	]
	quest.410F8D5BAEFB395A.title: "Market Day: Industrial"
	quest.410F8D5BAEFB395A.quest_subtitle: "Hold 30 tokens; pick a feedstock"
	quest.410F8D5BAEFB395A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r hold 30 tokens and choose a stack of raw feedstock: tin, lead, nickel, bauxite or salt."
		"&eHow:&r tokens are checked, not taken."
		"&eTip:&r bauxite is the slow one to find, and aluminium is the gate to MV."
	]
	quest.4F2FD5E25FC1E6FB.title: "Market Day: Divine"
	quest.4F2FD5E25FC1E6FB.quest_subtitle: "Hold 64 tokens; pick a treasure"
	quest.4F2FD5E25FC1E6FB.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember when worshippers brought you treasures. Now you just keep a full stack.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r hold a full stack of 64 tokens and choose a treasure: a totem, shulker shells, a heart of the sea, an enchanted golden apple or 3 Greater Tokens."
		"&eHow:&r tokens are checked, not taken. Exchange Greater Tokens back if you need 64 loose ones."
		"&eTip:&r picking the Greater Tokens is the same as taking 27 regular tokens home."
	]
	quest.5D7536360603F09D.title: "A Dragon's Hoard"
	quest.5D7536360603F09D.quest_subtitle: "81 tokens' worth, unspent"
	quest.5D7536360603F09D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r hold nine Greater Demigod Tokens at once. That's 81 tokens you chose not to spend."
		"&eTip:&r the demigod approves of patience. The demigod also notes that totems exist."
	]
	quest.1331D799C9EDD8D5.title: "The Machine Shop"
	quest.1331D799C9EDD8D5.quest_subtitle: "Build your first, buy the rest"
	quest.1331D799C9EDD8D5.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember forges that worked while you slept. Once you know how a thing is made, its copies come cheap.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r repeatable shop quests that sell copies of machines, boilers, tanks, hulls and cables."
		"&eHow:&r a machine goes on sale only after you finish the quest where you build it yourself. Until then its entry is invisible."
		"&eHow:&r hold the price and click &eSubmit&r: the tokens are taken and the machine is yours. Buy again whenever you like."
		"&eTip:&r counters run Steam, LV, MV, HV, EV. From MV up, prices are in Greater Demigod Tokens (9 tokens each). Multiblock controllers are never sold."
	]
	quest.1C0CF4F66B9C8A31.title: "Counter: Steam"
	quest.1C0CF4F66B9C8A31.quest_subtitle: "Steam machines · 3 to 6 tokens"
	quest.1C0CF4F66B9C8A31.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Steam counter of the Machine Shop."
		"&eHow:&r click to open it. Each machine in this row appears once you finish the quest where you build it yourself."
		"&eTip:&r prices at this counter are 3 to 6 tokens."
	]
	quest.30F6DAC79E6F6E9A.title: "Bronze Tank"
	quest.30F6DAC79E6F6E9A.quest_subtitle: "3 tokens · unlocked by Bronze Tank"
	quest.30F6DAC79E6F6E9A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Holds water, steam or any other fluid. This is a copy of something you already built yourself."
		"&eHow:&r hold 3 tokens and click &eSubmit&r. The tokens are taken and you get one Bronze Tank."
		"&eTip:&r repeatable: buy as many as you need."
	]
	quest.75CC9723C1539BCE.title: "Bronze Machine Casing"
	quest.75CC9723C1539BCE.quest_subtitle: "3 tokens · unlocked by Bronze Machine Casing"
	quest.75CC9723C1539BCE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r The frame of every bronze machine. This is a copy of something you already built yourself."
		"&eHow:&r hold 3 tokens and click &eSubmit&r. The tokens are taken and you get one Bronze Machine Casing."
