	quest.2631C7C30A21F19B.title: "Redstone"
	quest.2631C7C30A21F19B.quest_subtitle: "for the collection"
	quest.2631C7C30A21F19B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r redstone stands in for cinnabar, HgS, the bright red mercury ore once ground into the pigment vermilion."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.149FA8E6EB11F35E.title: "Lapis Lazuli"
	quest.149FA8E6EB11F35E.quest_subtitle: "for the collection"
	quest.149FA8E6EB11F35E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r lapis gets its blue from S₃⁻ radical ions trapped in the mineral lazurite."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.0044AC0903650B96.title: "Iron Ingot"
	quest.0044AC0903650B96.quest_subtitle: "for the collection"
	quest.0044AC0903650B96.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r iron (Fe) is the most-used metal on Earth by far; about 95% of all metal made is iron or steel."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.0EDE5F7B3804166E.title: "Gold Ingot"
	quest.0EDE5F7B3804166E.quest_subtitle: "for the collection"
	quest.0EDE5F7B3804166E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r gold (Au) stays bright because almost nothing oxidises it; only aqua regia and a few cyanide solutions dissolve it."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.0F6EA77E0E8F0585.title: "Copper Ingot"
	quest.0F6EA77E0E8F0585.quest_subtitle: "for the collection"
	quest.0F6EA77E0E8F0585.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r copper (Cu) slowly turns green as its surface becomes basic copper carbonate and sulfate: the patina on old roofs."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.556CA51BBA85BCCA.title: "Emerald"
	quest.556CA51BBA85BCCA.quest_subtitle: "for the collection"
	quest.556CA51BBA85BCCA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r emerald is beryl, Be₃Al₂Si₆O₁₈, tinted green by traces of chromium or vanadium."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.470A1D79EC426BDE.title: "Diamond"
	quest.470A1D79EC426BDE.quest_subtitle: "for the collection"
	quest.470A1D79EC426BDE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r diamond is carbon in a tetrahedral network; it burns in pure oxygen to CO₂ like any other carbon."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.3A8E2FED97BE553C.title: "Netherite Ingot"
	quest.3A8E2FED97BE553C.quest_subtitle: "for the collection"
	quest.3A8E2FED97BE553C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r netherite is fictional: four scrap and four gold make an ingot, an alloy no real metallurgist would recognise."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.033A26647FE625CA.title: "Nether Quartz"
	quest.033A26647FE625CA.quest_subtitle: "for the collection"
	quest.033A26647FE625CA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r quartz is SiO₂. Squeeze a quartz crystal and it makes a voltage (piezoelectricity); that's what keeps time in quartz watches."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.5FFA7B24ACF7212D.title: "Amethyst Shard"
	quest.5FFA7B24ACF7212D.quest_subtitle: "for the collection"
	quest.5FFA7B24ACF7212D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r amethyst is quartz, SiO₂, coloured purple by iron impurities and natural radiation."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.4CFA4F63089D99E3.title: "Allthemodium Ingot"
	quest.4CFA4F63089D99E3.quest_subtitle: "for the collection"
	quest.4CFA4F63089D99E3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r allthemodium is fictional; the Allthemodium page covers where it comes from."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.571F38E3FED6BE4B.title: "Vibranium Ingot"
	quest.571F38E3FED6BE4B.quest_subtitle: "for the collection"
	quest.571F38E3FED6BE4B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r vibranium is fiction borrowed from comics; here it's the Nether's deep metal."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.0ACB7C3995FD9092.title: "Unobtainium Ingot"
	quest.0ACB7C3995FD9092.quest_subtitle: "for the collection"
	quest.0ACB7C3995FD9092.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r 'unobtainium' is an old engineers' joke for a material with perfect properties that doesn't exist."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.6C2652DAEEBD6610.title: "Cloggrum Ingot"
	quest.6C2652DAEEBD6610.quest_subtitle: "Optional: for the collection"
	quest.6C2652DAEEBD6610.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r cloggrum is the Undergarden's iron analogue: a soft, workable metal."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.0C2D1912C44E50E2.title: "Froststeel Ingot"
	quest.0C2D1912C44E50E2.quest_subtitle: "Optional: for the collection"
	quest.0C2D1912C44E50E2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r froststeel is fictional; real 'cold' metals don't exist, but some alloys stay tough at cryogenic temperatures (austenitic stainless steel)."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.5D711EAAB2A8D679.title: "Utherium Crystal"
	quest.5D711EAAB2A8D679.quest_subtitle: "Optional: for the collection"
	quest.5D711EAAB2A8D679.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r utherium is a fictional crystal of the Undergarden's depths."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.1C3B390E4E9E36AD.title: "Regalium Crystal"
	quest.1C3B390E4E9E36AD.quest_subtitle: "Optional: for the collection"
	quest.1C3B390E4E9E36AD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r regalium is the Undergarden's gold analogue, a rare crystal."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.7B04AC979AF594F7.title: "Forgotten Ingot"
	quest.7B04AC979AF594F7.quest_subtitle: "Optional: for the collection"
	quest.7B04AC979AF594F7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r forgotten metal is the Undergarden's endgame material."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.654D766647816205.title: "Ironwood Ingot"
	quest.654D766647816205.quest_subtitle: "Optional: for the collection"
	quest.654D766647816205.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r ironwood mixes iron with living wood; real 'ironwoods' are just very dense timbers that sink in water."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.75A20DAC5105DC02.title: "Steeleaf Ingot"
	quest.75A20DAC5105DC02.quest_subtitle: "Optional: for the collection"
	quest.75A20DAC5105DC02.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r steeleaf is fictional; real leaves are mostly water, cellulose and chlorophyll."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.02948A493A95903C.title: "Knightmetal Ingot"
	quest.02948A493A95903C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: for the collection"
	quest.02948A493A95903C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r knightmetal comes from armour shards; real armourers did recycle broken plate the same way."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.32F11D71F995BEED.title: "Naga Scale"
	quest.32F11D71F995BEED.quest_subtitle: "Optional: for the collection"
	quest.32F11D71F995BEED.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r real reptile scales are keratin, the protein of hair and nails."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.4C6364700FF784EF.title: "Carminite"
	quest.4C6364700FF784EF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: for the collection"
	quest.4C6364700FF784EF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r carminite is fictional. Real carmine red came from crushed cochineal insects (carminic acid)."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	quest.75B0F877784D8549.title: "Fiery Ingot"
	quest.75B0F877784D8549.quest_subtitle: "Optional: for the collection"
	quest.75B0F877784D8549.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a material for the collection. Vanilla ingots and gems colour armour trims; some modded ones do too (try it at a smithing table)."
		"&eChemistry:&r fiery metal is iron quenched in the blood of the Hydra; real quenching uses water, oil or brine."
		"&eHow:&r keep one in your inventory. At a smithing table: trim template + armour piece + material."
	]
	chapter.5BBA2E199EC82256.title: "Apotheosis"
	chapter.5BBA2E199EC82256.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Affix loot, gems, sigils, world tiers, spawners and Gateways."
	]
	quest.1DC1DC4A3FCBAD79.title: "A Gem in the Rough"
	quest.1DC1DC4A3FCBAD79.quest_subtitle: "Find any Apotheosis gem"
	quest.1DC1DC4A3FCBAD79.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember gear that remembered you back. Mortal gear can learn, if you teach it.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Apotheosis gems drop from monsters and chests. Each one carries a bonus that you can set into a socket on your gear."
		"&eHow:&r fight, loot and read the tooltip of anything that glitters. Any gem completes this quest."
		"&eTip:&r gems come in purities, from cracked to perfect. Better purity, bigger bonus."
	]
	quest.0823E0B0B994DD08.title: "Gem Dust"
	quest.0823E0B0B994DD08.quest_subtitle: "The currency of Apotheosis"
	quest.0823E0B0B994DD08.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r gem dust builds almost every Apotheosis table, sigil and rune."
		"&eHow:&r crush spare gems into gem dust (JEI shows how)."
		"&eTip:&r keep good gems for sockets and crush the rest."
	]
	quest.543B38711E08D117.title: "Setting a Gem"
	quest.543B38711E08D117.quest_subtitle: "Sockets are filled at the smithing table"
	quest.543B38711E08D117.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the smithing table is where Apotheosis puts gems into sockets and applies sigils to gear."
		"&eHow:&r 4 planks and 2 iron ingots. Put the gear in, then the gem or sigil."
		"&eTip:&r a socketed gem is locked in until a Sigil of Withdrawal pulls it out."
	]
	quest.629C34B0AC068654.title: "Gem Cutting"
	quest.629C34B0AC068654.quest_subtitle: "Combine gems into higher purities"
	quest.629C34B0AC068654.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Gem Cutting Table upgrades gems to higher purity using matching gems and dust."
		"&eChemistry:&r real gems are cut along cleavage planes, flat directions where the crystal's bonds are weakest."
		"&eHow:&r smooth stone, shears, planks and gem dust."
	]
	quest.5816867DEF0C5DBF.title: "Gem-Fused Slate"
	quest.5816867DEF0C5DBF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the base of every sigil"
	quest.5816867DEF0C5DBF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r gem-fused slate is the backing for sigils and spawner runes."
		"&eChemistry:&r deepslate is metamorphic rock: older stone squeezed and heated deep underground until its minerals recrystallised."
		"&eHow:&r 8 deepslate around 1 gem dust makes 8."
	]
	quest.12EF5F7791329CED.title: "Sigil of Socketing"
	quest.12EF5F7791329CED.quest_subtitle: "Optional: add a socket to any gear"
	quest.12EF5F7791329CED.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r adds a socket to gear in a smithing table, so you can slot in a gem."
		"&eHow:&r gem-fused slate, an amethyst shard, gunpowder and gem dust (makes 3)."
		"&eTip:&r a Sigil of Withdrawal pulls gems back out later."
	]
	quest.026907A8758CF03D.title: "Sigil of Unnaming"
	quest.026907A8758CF03D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: wipe an affix name"
	quest.026907A8758CF03D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r removes the long generated name from an affixed item, so it goes back to its plain name."
		"&eHow:&r 6 slate around 3 flint makes 6. Apply it at the smithing table."
		"&eTip:&r a name tag afterwards lets you call the sword whatever you like."
	]
	quest.0E850BA9288D13B8.title: "Sigil of Withdrawal"
	quest.0E850BA9288D13B8.quest_subtitle: "Optional: get your gems back"
	quest.0E850BA9288D13B8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r pulls every gem out of an item without destroying them, so a good gem can move to new gear."
		"&eHow:&r gem-fused slate, blaze rods, ender pearls, a lava bucket and gem dust (makes 4)."
		"&eTip:&r withdraw gems before salvaging or reforging old gear."
	]
	quest.074EDD3891190AD6.title: "Sigil of Enhancement"
	quest.074EDD3891190AD6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: raise a gem's rarity"
	quest.074EDD3891190AD6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r upgrades a socketed gem to the next rarity at the Reforging Table."
		"&eHow:&r gem-fused slate, gem dust and a godforged pearl (makes 4). Godforged pearls come from salvaging mythic gear."
		"&eTip:&r save these for gems you'll keep: a mythic gem in endgame gear is worth it."
	]
	quest.42B5A285CF0DDEC1.title: "Sigil of Rebirth"
	quest.42B5A285CF0DDEC1.quest_subtitle: "Optional: fuel for reforging"
	quest.42B5A285CF0DDEC1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Sigil of Rebirth is spent at the Reforging Table each time you reroll an item."
		"&eHow:&r 6 slate around 3 gem dust makes 6."
		"&eTip:&r make them in bulk before a long reforging session."
	]
	quest.16D771524FEF380B.title: "Sigil of Malice"
	quest.16D771524FEF380B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: taken from an Apothic Invader"
	quest.16D771524FEF380B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a sigil with no crafting recipe. It feeds the highest gateway and spawner upgrade recipes."
		"&eHow:&r Apothic Invaders (named bosses from World Tier: Frontier on) sometimes drop one. Check JEI for its uses."
		"&eTip:&r invaders hit very hard. Fight them where you can retreat."
	]
	quest.57C95E565D3B2119.title: "Salvaging"
	quest.57C95E565D3B2119.quest_subtitle: "Junk gear into rarity materials"
	quest.57C95E565D3B2119.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Salvaging Table breaks affixed gear into materials of its rarity."
		"&eHow:&r a smithing table, an iron pickaxe and axe, copper, a lava bucket and gem dust."
		"&eTip:&r every affixed sword you don't want is a reforge for one you do."
	]
	quest.679DBEB918F424B7.title: "Mysterious Scrap Metal"
	quest.679DBEB918F424B7.quest_subtitle: "Common: from grey gear"
	quest.679DBEB918F424B7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the salvage of common (grey) affix gear, used in common-tier reforging."
		"&eHow:&r salvage any common affixed item."
		"&eTip:&r common gear drops everywhere, so this piles up first."
	]
	quest.56DD467D6105201B.title: "Timeworn Fabric"
	quest.56DD467D6105201B.quest_subtitle: "Uncommon: from green gear"
	quest.56DD467D6105201B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the salvage of uncommon (green) gear. The Frontiersman's spawner upgrade rune uses it too."
		"&eHow:&r salvage uncommon affixed gear."
		"&eTip:&r sort loot by colour before salvaging; each rarity has its own material."
	]
	quest.645E6EA4F2C67FAB.title: "Luminous Crystal"
	quest.645E6EA4F2C67FAB.quest_subtitle: "Rare: from blue gear"
	quest.645E6EA4F2C67FAB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r luminous crystal shards are the salvage of rare (blue) gear."
		"&eHow:&r salvage rare gear in the Salvaging Table until you have 4 shards."
		"&eTip:&r the Wayfarer's spawner upgrade rune is built on these."
	]
	quest.77F9828DD5BEEC92.title: "Godforged Pearl"
	quest.77F9828DD5BEEC92.quest_subtitle: "Mythic: from orange gear"
	quest.77F9828DD5BEEC92.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the salvage of mythic gear, the rarest material: augmenting, enhancement sigils and the top runes need it."
		"&eHow:&r salvage mythic gear. It drops in high world tiers, from tiered gateways and from the toughest elites."
		"&eTip:&r never salvage a mythic item you would rather wear; check its affixes first."
	]
	quest.0887E36DC2300C66.title: "Arcane Sands"
	quest.0887E36DC2300C66.quest_subtitle: "Epic: from purple gear"
	quest.0887E36DC2300C66.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the salvage of epic (purple) gear. The full Reforging Table needs it."
		"&eHow:&r salvage epic affixed gear."
		"&eTip:&r keep a few stacks; reforging epic gear spends them fast."
	]
	quest.6E58E2BD59CFAE57.title: "Simple Reforging"
	quest.6E58E2BD59CFAE57.quest_subtitle: "Reroll an item's affixes"
	quest.6E58E2BD59CFAE57.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Simple Reforging Table rerolls affixes on gear of lower rarities."
		"&eHow:&r an enchanting table, iron, smooth stone and gem dust."
		"&eTip:&r reforging costs rarity materials; salvage junk gear to get them."
	]
	quest.153E1F2212F6740C.title: "Divine Reforging"
	quest.153E1F2212F6740C.quest_subtitle: "Reforge any rarity, up to mythic"
	quest.153E1F2212F6740C.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember weapons that chose their wielders. These at least choose good affixes.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the full Reforging Table handles every rarity, up to mythic gear."
		"&eHow:&r the Simple Reforging Table, a netherite ingot, nether bricks and arcane sands."
	]
	quest.0C78BE8ECFF1CD59.title: "Augmenting"
	quest.0C78BE8ECFF1CD59.quest_subtitle: "Optional: upgrade and reroll single affixes"
	quest.0C78BE8ECFF1CD59.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Augmenting Table improves or rerolls one affix at a time."
		"&eHow:&r an enchanting table, a Nether Star, 2 godforged pearls and polished blackstone."
		"&eTip:&r save it for gear you plan to keep for the rest of the game."
	]
	quest.350612C6F7C5C839.title: "World Tiers"
	quest.350612C6F7C5C839.quest_subtitle: "Harder world, better loot"
	quest.350612C6F7C5C839.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Apotheosis splits the game into five world tiers: Haven, Frontier, Ascent, Summit and Pinnacle. Higher tiers make monsters stronger and loot better, and raise the cap on enchanting power."
		"&eHow:&r press CTRL+T to open the World Tier screen. Hover a tier to see what unlocks it; activate it once unlocked. Click the checkmark when you've looked."
		"&eTip:&r you can step back down to an easier tier at any time."
	]
	quest.7710DDB527AFC9F4.title: "Haven"
	quest.7710DDB527AFC9F4.quest_subtitle: "Pick up your first affix item"
	quest.7710DDB527AFC9F4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Haven is the starting tier. It unlocks when you pick up any affixed item. Enchanting power is capped at 30 Eterna here."
		"&eHow:&r find an affixed item (a coloured name). Click the checkmark when the advancement pops."
		"&eTip:&r Haven is the tier to learn the systems in."
	]
	quest.482D781F156C2AF7.title: "Frontier"
	quest.482D781F156C2AF7.quest_subtitle: "A full set of affix gear"
	quest.482D781F156C2AF7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Frontier unlocks when you wear affixed armour in all four slots and hold an affixed weapon. Apothic Invaders start to appear, and the Eterna cap rises to 45."
		"&eHow:&r equip any affixed helmet, chestplate, leggings, boots and weapon, then activate Frontier (CTRL+T). Click the checkmark."
		"&eTip:&r 45 Eterna is what the infused shelves need (Apothic Enchanting page)."
	]
	quest.1C24BC11278773FE.title: "Ascent"
	quest.1C24BC11278773FE.quest_subtitle: "Uncommon gear and one Invader"
	quest.1C24BC11278773FE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Ascent needs a full set of uncommon (green) or better gear and one Apothic Invader killed. The Eterna cap rises to 60."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade every slot to uncommon or better, kill an invader, then activate Ascent. Click the checkmark."
		"&eTip:&r invaders announce themselves; fight them near a bed."
	]
	quest.6102946A42F68055.title: "Summit"
	quest.6102946A42F68055.quest_subtitle: "Rare gear and the Wither"
	quest.6102946A42F68055.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Summit needs a full set of rare (blue) or better gear and a dead Wither. The Eterna cap rises to 75."
		"&eHow:&r gear up in rare affixes, summon and kill the Wither, then activate Summit. Click the checkmark."
		"&eTip:&r fight the Wither underground or in a bunker: it breaks most blocks around it."
	]
	quest.1A192A3BD6CC2EFC.title: "Pinnacle"
	quest.1A192A3BD6CC2EFC.quest_subtitle: "Epic gear and a free End"
	quest.1A192A3BD6CC2EFC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Pinnacle, the top tier, needs a full set of epic (purple) gear and the Ender Dragon killed. Enchanting power is uncapped (100 Eterna)."
		"&eHow:&r wear epic or better in every slot, beat the dragon, then activate Pinnacle. Click the checkmark."
		"&eTip:&r this is where mythic gear and godforged pearls start to flow."
	]
	quest.7AC2E1778F2440B5.title: "Tiered Gateways"
	quest.7AC2E1778F2440B5.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a gate that matches your world tier"
	quest.7AC2E1778F2440B5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Apotheosis adds one gateway per world tier (Frontier, Ascent, Summit, Pinnacle). Each opens only in its own tier and pays out affix gear."
		"&eHow:&r the Frontier pearl is spider eyes, iron, bones, an ender pearl and rotten flesh. JEI lists the others. Open and close one, then click the checkmark."
		"&eTip:&r the Pinnacle gate needs Sigils of Malice and a Warden Tendril."
	]
	quest.3E15AAB987CD907C.title: "The Endless Gateway"
	quest.3E15AAB987CD907C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: invaders that never stop"
	quest.3E15AAB987CD907C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Endless Gateway of Apothic Invaders sends wave after wave of invaders until you fall or walk away."
		"&eHow:&r its pearl is a reward from the Pinnacle gateway. Open it, survive as long as you can, then click the checkmark."
		"&eTip:&r the deeper you go, the better the payout. Bring totems."
	]
	quest.30108A1B2EF93956.title: "Sigil of Supremacy"
	quest.30108A1B2EF93956.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the Endless Gateway's prize"
	quest.30108A1B2EF93956.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember standing where nothing could follow. It was lonely, and you liked it.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the rarest sigil, paid out deep in the Endless Gateway. Check JEI for what it unlocks."
		"&eHow:&r keep the endless gate going until it drops."
		"&eTip:&r the gateway's reward list in JEI shows which wave it starts at."
	]
	quest.29B876259D4B5686.title: "Elite Hunting"
	quest.29B876259D4B5686.quest_subtitle: "Kill 50 zombies and watch for affix gear"
	quest.29B876259D4B5686.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Apotheosis gives some monsters affixed gear and makes rare elites with a coloured name. Their drops can roll affixes and sockets."
		"&eHow:&r kill 50 zombies. Pick up any named or glowing item they drop and read its tooltip."
		"&eTip:&r elites hit hard. Gear up before poking one with a stick."
	]
	quest.1F426EE32EDF30C4.title: "Potion Charm"
	quest.1F426EE32EDF30C4.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Unbreakable Charms"
	quest.1F426EE32EDF30C4.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Unbreakable Charms\" on the Apothic Enchanting page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.30908A094F9B094F.title: "Gate Pearl"
	quest.30908A094F9B094F.quest_subtitle: "Gateways to Eternity: a wave-based arena"
	quest.30908A094F9B094F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Gate Pearl opens a Gateway that releases waves of a chosen mob. Beat every wave for rewards."
		"&eHow:&r the Blaze gate is five blaze rods, an ender pearl and three nether bricks. Apotheosis adds tiered gates (Frontier and up); JEI shows them all."
		"&eTip:&r a gate is a controlled mob farm: blaze rods, ender pearls and XP on demand."
	]
	quest.29DC8827585EFBB8.title: "Close a Gateway"
	quest.29DC8827585EFBB8.quest_subtitle: "Survive every wave"
	quest.29DC8827585EFBB8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the gateway closes when every wave is defeated and pays out its reward."
		"&eHow:&r throw the pearl in an open area, stay close (leaving fails the gate) and kill each wave. Click the checkmark when it closes."
		"&eTip:&r tiered Apotheosis gates hand out affix gear and rarity materials."
	]
	quest.4E86CCB805AC4C3A.title: "Gem Case"
	quest.4E86CCB805AC4C3A.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Gem Case"
	quest.4E86CCB805AC4C3A.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Gem Case\" on the Apothic Enchanting page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.107F658AC0B2249C.title: "Every Rarity"
	quest.107F658AC0B2249C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: scrap, fabric, sands and a pearl"
	quest.107F658AC0B2249C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one material of each other rarity: common scrap metal, uncommon timeworn fabric, epic arcane sands and a mythic godforged pearl."
		"&eHow:&r salvage gear of each colour. The pearl only comes from mythic gear: tiered Gateways and the toughest elites."
		"&eTip:&r Divine Reforging, upgrade runes and the strongest sigils all spend these."
	]
	quest.124C0733D11EE060.title: "Bottled Monsters"
	quest.124C0733D11EE060.quest_subtitle: "Optional: mine a spawner with Silk Touch"
	quest.124C0733D11EE060.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember making monsters to order. Today you'll settle for moving one.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r with Apothic Spawners a monster spawner can be picked up with a Silk Touch pickaxe and moved home."
		"&eHow:&r find one in a dungeon or mineshaft, light it up, then mine it with Silk Touch (it costs the pick 100 durability)."
		"&eTip:&r spawners are mob farms for drops you can't make chemically: bones, string, ender pearls, blaze rods."
	]
	quest.115518D0E8FADA52.title: "Spawner Chains"
	quest.115518D0E8FADA52.quest_subtitle: "Optional: blow up a spawner"
	quest.115518D0E8FADA52.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r spawner chains are the binding for spawner runes. They only come from a monster spawner destroyed by an explosion."
		"&eChemistry:&r TNT (C₇H₅N₃O₆) carries its own oxygen in its nitro groups, so it burns in microseconds and makes a shock wave."
		"&eHow:&r find a spawner you don't want to keep and blow it up with TNT. Pick up the chains, and bring a spare TNT for the quest."
		"&eTip:&r keep the good spawners: Silk Touch them home instead."
	]
	quest.4175DD97D428CAF7.title: "Spawner Runes"
	quest.4175DD97D428CAF7.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the blank every rune starts from"
	quest.4175DD97D428CAF7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a blank Spawner Rune. Crafted with one more ingredient it becomes a rune that rewrites a spawner's rules when you right-click the spawner with it."
		"&eHow:&r gem dust, gem-fused slate and spawner chains (makes 2)."
		"&eTip:&r hold Shift over a placed spawner's tooltip, or look at it with Jade, to see its current stats."
	]
	quest.74B5FC08EDE47DD7.title: "Rune of Immolation"
	quest.74B5FC08EDE47DD7.quest_subtitle: "Optional: mobs spawn on fire"
	quest.74B5FC08EDE47DD7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r spawned mobs are set alight, so they drop cooked meat and die faster."
		"&eHow:&r a Spawner Rune with 4 campfires around it."
		"&eTip:&r useless on Nether mobs, which don't burn."
	]
	quest.5B6EBD700BFF7918.title: "Rune of Debilitation"
	quest.5B6EBD700BFF7918.quest_subtitle: "Optional: mobs spawn weakened"
	quest.5B6EBD700BFF7918.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r lowers the starting health of spawned mobs, so one hit finishes them."
		"&eHow:&r a Spawner Rune with 4 pointed dripstone around it."
		"&eTip:&r stack it a few times for a one-punch farm."
	]
	quest.4641F2AAF9EBB5EC.title: "Rune of Youth"
	quest.4641F2AAF9EBB5EC.quest_subtitle: "Optional: baby mobs only"
	quest.4641F2AAF9EBB5EC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r spawned mobs are babies wherever the mob has a baby form."
		"&eHow:&r a Spawner Rune with 4 turtle eggs around it."
		"&eTip:&r baby zombies are fast. You were warned."
	]
	quest.324782A36733BB21.title: "Rune of Spawning Range"
	quest.324782A36733BB21.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a wider spawn area"
	quest.324782A36733BB21.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r widens the area a spawner may place mobs in."
		"&eHow:&r a Spawner Rune with 4 pistons around it."
		"&eTip:&r use quartz in the off hand to shrink it again (see Opposite Day)."
	]
	quest.0076287B01379D21.title: "Rune of Perpetual Twilight"
	quest.0076287B01379D21.quest_subtitle: "Optional: spawns in any light"
	quest.0076287B01379D21.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the spawner ignores light levels, so a well-lit farm still runs."
		"&eHow:&r a Spawner Rune with 4 soul lanterns around it."
		"&eTip:&r light your farm fully: the spawner works, wild mobs don't spawn."
	]
	quest.5B0D311F89A43A46.title: "Rune of Control"
	quest.5B0D311F89A43A46.quest_subtitle: "Optional: an off switch"
	quest.5B0D311F89A43A46.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the spawner only runs while it gets a redstone signal."
		"&eHow:&r a Spawner Rune with 4 comparators around it."
		"&eTip:&r put it on every farm first, so you can switch it off."
	]
	quest.5EE2734CD7054A26.title: "Opposite Day"
	quest.5EE2734CD7054A26.quest_subtitle: "Optional: undo a spawner change"
	quest.5EE2734CD7054A26.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r with nether quartz in your off hand, using a rune or modifier on a spawner reverses its effect (turn Silence off, shrink the range, and so on)."
		"&eChemistry:&r quartz is silicon dioxide, SiO₂: the same compound as most sand and glass."
		"&eHow:&r hold quartz in the off hand and the modifier in the main hand, then right-click the spawner."
		"&eTip:&r JEI's spawner page lists every modifier and its inverse."
	]
	quest.36856B7EC9732BEF.title: "Rune of Silence"
	quest.36856B7EC9732BEF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a quiet farm"
	quest.36856B7EC9732BEF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r spawned mobs make no sound."
		"&eHow:&r a Spawner Rune with 4 wool around it."
		"&eTip:&r your ears will thank you."
	]
	quest.33E489B3C17435FC.title: "Frontiersman's Upgrade"
	quest.33E489B3C17435FC.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a slightly better spawner"
	quest.33E489B3C17435FC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the first of four upgrade runes: faster spawns and more mobs per spawn. The others are Wayfarer's, Mountaineer's and Thundering."
		"&eHow:&r a Spawner Rune with timeworn fabric, clocks and flint."
		"&eTip:&r upgrade runes match the world tiers, so each new tier opens the next rune."
	]
	quest.47478A4865F55A20.title: "Wayfarer's Upgrade"
	quest.47478A4865F55A20.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a better spawner"
	quest.47478A4865F55A20.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the second upgrade rune: a bigger step in spawn speed and count."
		"&eHow:&r a Spawner Rune with luminous crystal shards, quartz, a spawn egg and a Sigil of Socketing (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r spawn eggs come from the Capturing enchantment (Choosing the Mob)."
	]
	quest.0A132D9A963A11B1.title: "Infused Spawner Rune"
	quest.0A132D9A963A11B1.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Infusing Spawner Runes"
	quest.0A132D9A963A11B1.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Infusing Spawner Runes\" on the Apothic Enchanting page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.0B6BC2548932EB47.title: "Mountaineer's Upgrade"
	quest.0B6BC2548932EB47.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a much better spawner"
	quest.0B6BC2548932EB47.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the third upgrade rune: a large boost to the spawner."
		"&eHow:&r an Infused Spawner Rune with arcane sands, phantom membranes, a Sigil of Malice and a Warden Tendril."
		"&eTip:&r the tendril drops from the Warden. Plan that fight."
	]
	quest.5E2F8C4BA2913F62.title: "Thundering Upgrade"
	quest.5E2F8C4BA2913F62.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a spawner at its limit"
	quest.5E2F8C4BA2913F62.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the last upgrade rune: the spawner reaches its maximum."
		"&eHow:&r an Infused Spawner Rune with godforged pearls, Infused Breath, a Nether Star and a perfect Endersurge gem."
		"&eTip:&r save Nether Stars: the Seed of a New World needs them too."
	]
	quest.21B21B2ECAD2E261.title: "Rune of Stupor"
	quest.21B21B2ECAD2E261.quest_subtitle: "Optional: mobs that stand still"
	quest.21B21B2ECAD2E261.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r spawned mobs have no AI: they don't move, attack or flee."
		"&eHow:&r an Infused Spawner Rune with chorus fruit and a Potion of Fatigue."
		"&eTip:&r a farm that can't fight back. Mobs without AI also don't despawn on their own."
	]
	quest.1758CEA4EE803F2C.title: "Rune of Solitude"
	quest.1758CEA4EE803F2C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: runs with nobody near"
	quest.1758CEA4EE803F2C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the spawner no longer needs a player nearby (the chunk still has to be loaded)."
		"&eHow:&r an Infused Spawner Rune with a Nether Star, phantom membranes and an eye of ender."
		"&eTip:&r pair it with FTB Chunks chunk loading for an always-on farm."
	]
	quest.507824C814FD4AFB.title: "Rune of Defiance"
	quest.507824C814FD4AFB.quest_subtitle: "Optional: ignore every spawn rule"
	quest.507824C814FD4AFB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the spawner ignores the mob's spawn conditions entirely (light, block, biome)."
		"&eHow:&r an Infused Spawner Rune with a conduit and ender pearls."
		"&eTip:&r useful for mobs with fussy rules, like slimes or guardians."
	]
	quest.7F4A2678A1294777.title: "Rune of Echoes"
	quest.7F4A2678A1294777.quest_subtitle: "Optional: extra loot per kill"
	quest.7F4A2678A1294777.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r spawned mobs drop extra copies of their loot. It stacks up to three times."
		"&eHow:&r an Infused Spawner Rune ringed with 8 echo shards."
		"&eTip:&r echo shards come from Ancient City chests, or from infusing one into four."
	]
	quest.3755654416ED892C.title: "Choosing the Mob"
	quest.3755654416ED892C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: change what a spawner spawns"
	quest.3755654416ED892C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r right-click a placed spawner with a spawn egg and it spawns that mob from then on."
		"&eHow:&r spawn eggs don't drop by themselves. The quests here show three ways to get one. Click the checkmark."
		"&eTip:&r the egg is used up, so change the mob only when you mean it."
	]
	quest.5A3EADEF20E137EE.title: "Capturing"
	quest.5A3EADEF20E137EE.quest_subtitle: "Optional: an enchantment that drops eggs"
	quest.5A3EADEF20E137EE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Capturing is a weapon enchantment from Apothic Spawners: each kill has a small chance per level to drop the mob's spawn egg."
		"&eHow:&r roll it at an enchanting table or find the book, and put it on a sword. Click the checkmark when you have it."
		"&eTip:&r the chance is low (half a percent per level), so use it on a farm, not on a hunt."
	]
	quest.19FCC58E2126F307.title: "Eggs from Fragments"
	quest.19FCC58E2126F307.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Reliquary"
	quest.19FCC58E2126F307.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Reliquary\" on the Relics page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.7784FA6379DA85F6.title: "Occult Ender Lead"
	quest.7784FA6379DA85F6.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Occult Ender Lead"
	quest.7784FA6379DA85F6.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Occult Ender Lead\" on the Apothic Enchanting page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.05B8DAE04E6B49C7.title: "Other Spawners"
	quest.05B8DAE04E6B49C7.quest_subtitle: "Optional: spawners from other mods"
	quest.05B8DAE04E6B49C7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r two other mods in the pack make their own spawners: Ars Additions and Mystical Agriculture."
		"&eHow:&r read on below. Click the checkmark."
		"&eTip:&r unlike a monster spawner, both are crafted, so you never have to go looking for one."
	]
	quest.4484883EB8EBFA4E.title: "Source Spawner"
	quest.4484883EB8EBFA4E.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Source Spawner"
	quest.4484883EB8EBFA4E.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Source Spawner\" on the Ars Nouveau page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.3E0768975888A688.title: "Soulium Spawner"
	quest.3E0768975888A688.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Soulium Spawner"
	quest.3E0768975888A688.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Soulium Spawner\" on the Mystical Agriculture page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.563D61599C12CF41.title: "Better Bookshelves"
	quest.563D61599C12CF41.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Hellshelves"
	quest.563D61599C12CF41.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Hellshelves\" on the Apothic Enchanting page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.0DA470EE8E63A89F.title: "Infusion"
	quest.0DA470EE8E63A89F.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Infused Hellshelves"
	quest.0DA470EE8E63A89F.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Infused Hellshelves\" on the Apothic Enchanting page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.67476A5068C80199.title: "Enchantment Library"
	quest.67476A5068C80199.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Enchantment Library"
	quest.67476A5068C80199.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Enchantment Library\" on the Apothic Enchanting page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.2103D96D8A9B8008.title: "Endshelves"
	quest.2103D96D8A9B8008.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Endshelves"
	quest.2103D96D8A9B8008.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Endshelves\" on the Apothic Enchanting page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.742D6F656F7BFD9B.title: "Scrap Tome"
	quest.742D6F656F7BFD9B.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Tome of Scrapping"
	quest.742D6F656F7BFD9B.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Tome of Scrapping\" on the Apothic Enchanting page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.3A57E3617E30E375.title: "House Fabergé"
	quest.3A57E3617E30E375.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Gem Case of House Fabergé"
	quest.3A57E3617E30E375.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Gem Case of House Fabergé\" on the Apothic Enchanting page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.3D6835D5C5C226C2.title: "God-Fused Pearl"
	quest.3D6835D5C5C226C2.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see God-Fused Pearl"
	quest.3D6835D5C5C226C2.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"God-Fused Pearl\" on the Apothic Enchanting page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.455E28217ADB7ECE.title: "Enchanting Table of the Raven"
	quest.455E28217ADB7ECE.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Enchanting Table of the Raven"
	quest.455E28217ADB7ECE.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Enchanting Table of the Raven\" on the Apothic Enchanting page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.080F97306DC1EEBE.title: "Curious Shelves"
	quest.080F97306DC1EEBE.quest_subtitle: "Optional: shelves that bend the rules"
	quest.080F97306DC1EEBE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Stoneshelf, Beeshelf, Melonshelf, Geode shelf and Basic Bookshelf each nudge the table's stats in an odd direction."
		"&eChemistry:&r a geode's calcite rind is CaCO₃, the same compound as chalk and limestone."
		"&eHow:&r Stoneshelf: polished andesite and books. Geode shelf: calcite around a bookshelf and a budding amethyst. JEI has the rest."
		"&eTip:&r every shelf's tooltip lists its Eterna, Quanta and Arcana: read them before you build."
	]
	quest.6D427E6087161CE0.title: "Hellshelf Upgrades"
	quest.6D427E6087161CE0.quest_subtitle: "Optional: blazing, glowing or all-seeing"
	quest.6D427E6087161CE0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Infused Hellshelf upgrades into Blazing (fire charges), Glowing (glowstone) or the Hellshelf of Sight, which shows more enchantment clues."
		"&eHow:&r an Infused Hellshelf in the grid with the upgrade items (check JEI). Masterful Sight needs netherite and emerald blocks."
		"&eTip:&r one Sightshelf shows much more of what the table will roll."
	]
	quest.50C2261CC96A09E9.title: "Seashelves"
	quest.50C2261CC96A09E9.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Seashelves"
	quest.50C2261CC96A09E9.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Seashelves\" on the Apothic Enchanting page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.38713E8802C76BD6.title: "Seashelf Upgrades"
	quest.38713E8802C76BD6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: infuse a seashelf"
	quest.38713E8802C76BD6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an Infused Seashelf, then Crystalline, Heart-Forged or the Seashelf of Aquatic Filtration, which keeps chosen enchantments out of the pool."
		"&eHow:&r infuse a seashelf at the table, then craft it with prismarine crystals, a heart of the sea, or prismarine bricks and slabs (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the filtering shelf is how you stop a table rolling the enchantment you never want."
	]
	quest.4E9B6DB7867AE262.title: "Deepshelves"
	quest.4E9B6DB7867AE262.quest_subtitle: "Optional: shelves from the deep dark"
	quest.4E9B6DB7867AE262.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the deepshelf family pushes the stats high. It starts dormant and wakes with infusion."
		"&eHow:&r Dormant Deepshelf: cracked deepslate tiles and books. Infuse it at 60 Eterna (World Tier: Ascent) to wake it."
		"&eTip:&r upgrade it with echo shards or soul lanterns; the Deepshelf of Arcane Treasures allows treasure enchantments."
	]
	quest.624644FE4BB6E32A.title: "Deepshelf Upgrades"
	quest.624644FE4BB6E32A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: echoing, soul-touched or treasure"
	quest.624644FE4BB6E32A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Echoing and Soul-Touched deepshelves raise the stats further; the treasure shelf lets the table roll treasure enchantments."
		"&eHow:&r a Deepshelf with an echo shard and candles, or a soul lantern and sculk. Treasure: 2 deepshelves, gold blocks, diamonds and an emerald block."
		"&eTip:&r echo shards come from Ancient City chests."
	]
	quest.20558B1364FA3529.title: "Sculkshelves"
	quest.20558B1364FA3529.quest_subtitle: "Optional: take a tendril from the Warden"
	quest.20558B1364FA3529.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the strongest deepshelves need a Warden Tendril, which drops from a Warden."
		"&eHow:&r kill a Warden (Ancient City; don't make a sound), then craft the tendril over an upgraded deepshelf with sculk and a sculk catalyst."
		"&eTip:&r a Warden has 500 health and its sonic boom ignores armor. Plan the fight, or plan the escape."
	]
	quest.64304335E8D6B4B1.title: "Endshelf Upgrades"
	quest.64304335E8D6B4B1.quest_subtitle: "Optional: pearlescent or draconic"
	quest.64304335E8D6B4B1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the top of the shelf ladder. The Pearlescent Endshelf adds end rods; the Draconic one is crowned with a dragon head."
		"&eHow:&r infuse dragon's breath for Infused Breath (3 per bottle), then craft an Endshelf with end rods and ender pearls, or a dragon head and pearls."
		"&eTip:&r dragon heads hang on End Ship bows. Bring the elytra home too."
	]
	quest.6434E76C18D3EA01.title: "Better Tomes"
	quest.6434E76C18D3EA01.quest_subtitle: "Optional: books with a single job"
	quest.6434E76C18D3EA01.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Tome of the Others enchants like a tool no other tome covers; Superior Scrapping and Extraction strip enchantments more gently (Extraction keeps the item)."
		"&eHow:&r Tome of the Others: 6 books and a blaze rod (makes 6). Infuse a Scrap Tome for Superior Scrapping, and that for Extraction."
		"&eTip:&r Extraction tomes are the cleanest way to move a good enchantment to new gear."
	]
	quest.73834033716D42E1.title: "Library of Alexandria"
	quest.73834033716D42E1.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Library of Alexandria"
	quest.73834033716D42E1.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Library of Alexandria\" on the Apothic Enchanting page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.4B9E10E49642FC65.title: "Ender Leads"
	quest.4B9E10E49642FC65.quest_subtitle: "Optional: carry a mob in your pocket"
	quest.4B9E10E49642FC65.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Flimsy Ender Lead captures animals; the infused Ender Lead captures most mobs; the Occult one can bind a mob to a spawner."
		"&eHow:&r flimsy: an ender pearl, a lead and a gold ingot (shapeless). Infuse it for the Ender Lead; infuse that holding a witch for the Occult lead."
		"&eTip:&r the easy way to move a villager across the world."
	]
	quest.2FB8A7CEA97331D2.title: "Inert Trident"
	quest.2FB8A7CEA97331D2.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see A Real Trident"
	quest.2FB8A7CEA97331D2.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"A Real Trident\" on the Apothic Enchanting page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	chapter.37F569BC21D75E5E.title: "Relics"
	chapter.37F569BC21D75E5E.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Found treasures that grow with you: Relics, plus the old Reliquary curios."
	]
	quest.2D88FCCF56BDE46A.title: "Things Mortals Didn't Make"
	quest.2D88FCCF56BDE46A.quest_subtitle: "How relics work"
	quest.2D88FCCF56BDE46A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Relics are curios you find, never craft. Each has abilities that level up as you use them, and a research screen to spend those levels."
		"&eHow:&r open a relic's tooltip for its abilities and the key that opens its upgrade screen. Click the checkmark when you have read it."
		"&eTip:&r relics never drop from the sky: they sit in structure chests, split by dimension as the three hubs below show."
	]
	quest.65639548C2C2E03A.title: "A True Relic"
	quest.65639548C2C2E03A.quest_subtitle: "Find any item from the Relics mod"
	quest.65639548C2C2E03A.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember owning things no mortal smith made. A few of them seem to have survived.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Relics are found, never crafted: mantles, belts, necklaces, boots, a chef's hat, a ring of the seven deadly sins. Each has abilities that grow with use."
		"&eHow:&r loot chests in dungeons, mineshafts, temples, villages and modded structures. Any one relic completes this quest."
		"&eTip:&r read the tooltip: each relic says what it does and how it gains experience."
	]
	quest.07F4A683B49929E8.title: "Overworld Chests"
	quest.07F4A683B49929E8.quest_subtitle: "Villages, mineshafts, temples and ruins"
	quest.07F4A683B49929E8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the relics below come from Overworld loot: village chests, mineshafts, jungle and desert temples, shipwrecks and the odd ruin."
		"&eHow:&r you are already here. Loot every chest you pass; relics are rare rolls, so volume matters."
		"&eTip:&r an Explorer's Compass points to the nearest structure of the kind you pick; JourneyMap marks the ones you've found."
	]
	quest.5E7D0441A6373BB4.title: "Nether Chests"
	quest.5E7D0441A6373BB4.quest_subtitle: "Bastions, fortresses and ruined portals"
	quest.5E7D0441A6373BB4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r bastion remnants, nether fortresses and ruined portals hold the Nether's relics."
		"&eHow:&r light a Nether portal (Chapter II) and raid a bastion. Its treasure room has the best chests and the angriest piglins."
		"&eTip:&r gold armour keeps piglins calm until you open a chest; after that they come anyway."
	]
	quest.6A4C76A74743E1F8.title: "End Chests"
	quest.6A4C76A74743E1F8.quest_subtitle: "End cities and End ships"
	quest.6A4C76A74743E1F8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r End city towers and the ships moored to them carry the rarest relics."
		"&eHow:&r beat the dragon, take the gateway, find a city. Shulkers guard every chest; bring blocks for levitation falls."
		"&eTip:&r the ship's chest sits behind the elytra frame. Take both."
	]
	quest.1E319EDD2549EE5E.title: "Roller Skates"
	quest.1E319EDD2549EE5E.quest_subtitle: "Faster the longer you run"
	quest.1E319EDD2549EE5E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r skates that build up movement speed while you keep running, at the cost of grip: the faster you go, the more you slide."
		"&eHow:&r Overworld chests. Equip them in the feet curio slot and keep sprinting."
		"&eTip:&r stop before corners. Levelled skates reach their top speed sooner."
	]
	quest.62E94826D4B2E5B0.title: "Jellyfish Necklace"
	quest.62E94826D4B2E5B0.quest_subtitle: "Stronger wet, and it stings"
	quest.62E94826D4B2E5B0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a necklace that raises your health and regeneration while you are in water or rain, and stores electric arcs that shock whatever you touch."
		"&eHow:&r Overworld chests, often in shipwrecks and ocean ruins."
		"&eTip:&r pair it with Flippers or Aqua Dashers for ocean monuments."
	]
	quest.2D1ED2489FB98943.title: "Hunting Belt"
	quest.2D1ED2489FB98943.quest_subtitle: "More charms, stronger pets"
	quest.2D1ED2489FB98943.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a belt that adds charm slots and makes your tamed animals hit harder while they fight beside you."
		"&eHow:&r Overworld chests. Wear it in the belt curio slot."
		"&eTip:&r a belt full of charms turns a pack of wolves into a real escort."
	]
	quest.20509264E3951F23.title: "Cut-Glass Boot"
	quest.20509264E3951F23.quest_subtitle: "A boot that holds liquids"
	quest.20509264E3951F23.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r held in hand, this boot works as a bucket that stores several liquids at once; its tooltip shows which one is selected."
		"&eHow:&r Overworld chests."
		"&eTip:&r it fills the gap between buckets and tanks when you're moving lava or water for the chemistry lines."
	]
	quest.47E080F28225EF5A.title: "Chef's Hat"
	quest.47E080F28225EF5A.quest_subtitle: "Every kill might be dinner"
	quest.47E080F28225EF5A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hat whose kills have a chance to drop a meatball, which eats like raw beef and cooks into something better."
		"&eHow:&r Overworld chests, mostly in villages."
		"&eTip:&r its abilities level with your cooking and eating, so wear it while you farm."
	]
	quest.2C8643F79DDEE201.title: "Leafy Mantle"
	quest.2C8643F79DDEE201.quest_subtitle: "At home in the canopy"
	quest.2C8643F79DDEE201.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a cloak that lets you move freely through leaves, land on them without damage and heal while you stand in foliage; it can even absorb leaves to save you from a killing blow."
		"&eHow:&r Overworld chests in forests and jungles."
		"&eTip:&r a jungle treetop is the safest bed in the pack while you wear it."
	]
	quest.6DBAE429686FCE01.title: "Springy Boot"
	quest.6DBAE429686FCE01.quest_subtitle: "Crouch, jump, bounce"
	quest.6DBAE429686FCE01.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a boot that launches you backwards off a crouch-jump and keeps bouncing on every landing until you come to a stop."
		"&eHow:&r Overworld chests."
		"&eTip:&r level the Bounce ability before trying anything near lava."
	]
	quest.0AA056792A0B33B6.title: "Rider's Flute"
	quest.0AA056792A0B33B6.quest_subtitle: "A stable in your pocket"
	quest.0AA056792A0B33B6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a flute that stores a tamed mount and releases it where you stand, so your horse comes with you through portals and across oceans."
		"&eHow:&r Overworld chests. Right-click a tamed mount to store it, right-click again to release it."
		"&eTip:&r the stored animal is safe in the flute; a horse left outside is not."
	]
	quest.33E9A0E88AECAB65.title: "Sphere of Self-Sacrifice"
	quest.33E9A0E88AECAB65.quest_subtitle: "Spend health now, get it back twice"
	quest.33E9A0E88AECAB65.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an orb that burns a third of your maximum health on use and restores twice as much over ten seconds; each active restoration also reduces incoming damage, and crouching fires them off as homing blood bolts."
		"&eHow:&r bastion and fortress chests."
		"&eTip:&r it rewards being hit: resisted damage levels the relic."
	]
	quest.296056A222401744.title: "Piglin Mask"
	quest.296056A222401744.quest_subtitle: "One of the herd"
	quest.296056A222401744.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a mask that stops piglins attacking you first and turns nearby piglins on anyone who attacks you; its looting ability drops golden teeth."
		"&eHow:&r bastion chests. The piglins guarding them don't see the irony."
		"&eTip:&r the golden teeth are the quest below."
	]
	quest.049E798F7D742FA2.title: "Reflective Necklace"
	quest.049E798F7D742FA2.quest_subtitle: "Damage, stored and returned"
	quest.049E798F7D742FA2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a necklace with a chance to turn damage you take into orbs that hold part of it, and release every orb at the next thing you hit."
		"&eHow:&r fortress chests."
		"&eTip:&r take a few hits on purpose, then swing at a wither skeleton."
	]
	quest.6B6097312B8A0A54.title: "Ring of the Seven Deadly Sins"
	quest.6B6097312B8A0A54.quest_subtitle: "A bonus for every vice"
	quest.6B6097312B8A0A54.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a ring whose abilities are named for the sins: Pride adds damage for height above a target, Envy for a target with more health than you, Wrath for a quick follow-up strike, and so on."
		"&eHow:&r bastion chests."
		"&eTip:&r each sin levels on its own, so the ring rewards the way you already fight."
	]
	quest.5FAD2FA223C07DA0.title: "Ghostly Mantle"
	quest.5FAD2FA223C07DA0.quest_subtitle: "Leave a mist behind you"
	quest.5FAD2FA223C07DA0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a cloak that trails a mist which drains the air of anything standing in it, and takes less damage from targets that keep staring at you."
		"&eHow:&r fortress and bastion chests."
		"&eTip:&r run circles around a brute and let the mist do the work."
	]
	quest.6F08847D8060811B.title: "Shield of Retaliation"
	quest.6F08847D8060811B.quest_subtitle: "Parry, then answer"
	quest.6F08847D8060811B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a shield with a short parry window: hold it and damage from in front is blocked, stored, and returned."
		"&eHow:&r bastion chests."
		"&eTip:&r it blocks a blaze volley cleanly if you raise it as the first fireball leaves."
	]
	quest.5E6FBB34947A8DDF.title: "Gold Teeth"
	quest.5E6FBB34947A8DDF.quest_subtitle: "The Piglin Mask's loot"
	quest.5E6FBB34947A8DDF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r with the Piglin Mask's looting ability, kills drop golden teeth: bigger mobs, more teeth. They also feed the mask's rank."
		"&eHow:&r find a Piglin Mask, level its looting ability and fight. Teeth craft into gold ingots, or trade them to piglins."
		"&eTip:&r it's mob-drop gold, like a zombified piglin farm: handy, but not ore."
	]
	quest.6503FE9F86412CC8.title: "Chorus Staff"
	quest.6503FE9F86412CC8.quest_subtitle: "Blink forward"
	quest.6503FE9F86412CC8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a staff that teleports you a few blocks forward from a small buffer of charges that refills on its own."
		"&eHow:&r End city chests."
		"&eTip:&r it crosses the gaps between End islands that an ender pearl would miss."
	]
	quest.2809A587615F97D2.title: "Clot of Time"
	quest.2809A587615F97D2.quest_subtitle: "Rewind your last few seconds"
	quest.2809A587615F97D2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r hold it and you slide back along the path you just walked, several seconds into the past, then it needs a rest."
		"&eHow:&r End city and ship chests."
		"&eTip:&r a shulker bullet lifted you off the edge? Rewind."
	]
	quest.25DB0A6EC17134F5.title: "Kinetic Belt"
	quest.25DB0A6EC17134F5.quest_subtitle: "Glide on momentum"
	quest.25DB0A6EC17134F5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a belt that adds charm slots and, while you hold jump, lowers your gravity and air resistance so your momentum carries you; falls while gliding hurt less."
		"&eHow:&r End city chests."
		"&eTip:&r with Roller Skates for the run-up it is nearly an elytra."
	]
	quest.74D6C23680479343.title: "Midnight Mantle"
	quest.74D6C23680479343.quest_subtitle: "Stronger by the moon"
	quest.74D6C23680479343.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a cloak that boosts damage near a full moon, health and regeneration near a new moon, and hides you in deep darkness."
		"&eHow:&r End city chests."
		"&eTip:&r check the moon phase before a boss fight; the mantle does."
	]
	quest.1758292777E0C7EE.title: "Glitchy Mantle"
	quest.1758292777E0C7EE.quest_subtitle: "Attacks that miss, copies that don't"
	quest.1758292777E0C7EE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a cloak that gives attacks against you a chance to miss and leaves glitchy copies of you behind that detonate on contact."
		"&eHow:&r End ship chests."
		"&eTip:&r wear it into the dragon fight: endermen hit the copies instead."
	]
	quest.13D47274D5B5041E.title: "Experience Disperser"
	quest.13D47274D5B5041E.quest_subtitle: "Share relic experience around"
	quest.13D47274D5B5041E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r when any of your relics gains experience, every other equipped relic receives a share of it."
		"&eHow:&r chests in any dimension; it has no favourite."
		"&eTip:&r it makes a full curio bar level together instead of one relic at a time."
	]
	quest.2CAD2D054CB09ACA.title: "Reliquary"
	quest.2CAD2D054CB09ACA.quest_subtitle: "Curios built from mob parts"
	quest.2CAD2D054CB09ACA.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember a treasury. Most of it is scattered now, in chests and in the hands of monsters.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Reliquary items are crafted from mob parts: hearts, glands, pearls and charm fragments."
		"&eHow:&r mob charm fragments drop from mobs. JEI shows the charm they build."
		"&eTip:&r a Mob Charm stops that mob type attacking you."
	]
	quest.66B6DA99BDA6AD30.title: "Alkahestry Tome"
	quest.66B6DA99BDA6AD30.quest_subtitle: "The alchemists' dream, in book form"
	quest.66B6DA99BDA6AD30.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r charged with redstone, the tome duplicates common items in a crafting grid."
		"&eChemistry:&r alchemists searched for alkahest, a universal solvent. None exists (what would you keep it in?), but aqua regia, HCl + HNO₃, dissolves even gold."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the tome and its recipes. Recharge it with redstone."
	]
	quest.43308A673FF653BF.title: "Relic Hunter"
	quest.43308A673FF653BF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: find a relic or an artifact"
	quest.43308A673FF653BF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r find any Relics or Artifacts item: a cloud in a bottle, running shoes, a leafy mantle, a mimic's treasure."
		"&eHow:&r loot chests in dungeons, mineshafts and towers, and beware chests that bite. Click the checkmark when you have one."
		"&eTip:&r Relics items level up as you use them; check their tooltips."
	]
	quest.08F23BEDD14FD31D.title: "Fortune Coin"
	quest.08F23BEDD14FD31D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a magnet in your pocket"
	quest.08F23BEDD14FD31D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r pulls nearby items and XP toward you while active."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Right-click to toggle it."
		"&eTip:&r turn it off near your sorting system or it'll grab the items."
	]
	quest.1C39B10303C8A4FB.title: "Relic Growth"
	quest.1C39B10303C8A4FB.quest_subtitle: "Optional: level up a relic"
	quest.1C39B10303C8A4FB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r relics earn experience when you use their abilities, and their levels make those abilities stronger."
		"&eHow:&r keep the relic equipped and use it. Open its ability screen (the tooltip names the key) to spend levels. Click the checkmark after your first upgrade."
		"&eTip:&r one well-levelled relic beats a drawer full of new ones."
	]
	quest.155D611580258963.title: "An Artifact"
	quest.155D611580258963.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Artifacts has its own page now"
	quest.155D611580258963.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Artifacts are simple, always-on curios: Running Shoes, Cloud in a Bottle, Digging Claws, a Lucky Scarf and many more."
		"&eHow:&r found in chests underground and in structures, and dropped by Mimics. Any one artifact completes this quest."
		"&eTip:&r the full list, one quest per artifact, is the Artifacts page under Tools and Gear."
	]
	quest.138734AE1F0C3A87.title: "That Chest Has Teeth"
	quest.138734AE1F0C3A87.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Lid and Teeth"
	quest.138734AE1F0C3A87.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Lid and Teeth\" on the Artifacts page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.73D8CBFF0B71205A.title: "Divine Comedy"
	quest.73D8CBFF0B71205A.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Whoopee Cushion"
	quest.73D8CBFF0B71205A.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Whoopee Cushion\" on the Artifacts page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.344B4E30A304E85A.title: "Mob Ingredients"
	quest.344B4E30A304E85A.quest_subtitle: "Hearts, ribs, glands and pearls"
	quest.344B4E30A304E85A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Reliquary items are built from rare mob parts: zombie hearts, rib bones, catalyzing glands, slime pearls, molten cores and more."
		"&eHow:&r they drop from their mobs (zombies drop zombie hearts). In this pack they can also be crafted: a zombie heart is rotten flesh in a ring of iron ingots."
		"&eTip:&r a Looting sword makes the drops much more common than the iron recipe."
	]
	quest.77C7E8214CABA7DB.title: "Mob Charm Belt"
	quest.77C7E8214CABA7DB.quest_subtitle: "Wear all your charms at once"
	quest.77C7E8214CABA7DB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the belt holds Mob Charms, so you can be ignored by several mob types at once."
		"&eHow:&r three leather and five mob charm fragments (check JEI). Each fragment is made from that mob's drops."
		"&eTip:&r creeper and enderman charms are the most valuable around a base."
	]
	quest.1B9288F0EB08F5B2.title: "Void Tear"
	quest.1B9288F0EB08F5B2.quest_subtitle: "A pocket that holds one item type"
	quest.1B9288F0EB08F5B2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Void Tear stores a huge stack of one item, and pulls more of it from your inventory."
		"&eHow:&r a ghast tear, a nebulous heart, a slime pearl and lapis (shapeless)."
		"&eTip:&r it's also an ingredient for the Infernal Tear, Emperor's Chalice and Midas Touchstone."
	]
	quest.7C823E959B36BA96.title: "Lantern of Paranoia"
	quest.7C823E959B36BA96.quest_subtitle: "Optional: it places torches for you"
	quest.7C823E959B36BA96.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the lantern places torches from your inventory wherever it's dark enough for mobs to spawn."
		"&eHow:&r iron ingots, glass, a slime pearl and a molten core (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r carry a stack of torches when caving and let it do the lighting."
	]
	quest.37897CAA67020AFC.title: "The Handgun"
	quest.37897CAA67020AFC.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Reliquary's magic pistol"
	quest.37897CAA67020AFC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a pistol that fires magazines of special bullets: neutral, exorcism, blaze, ender, storm, seeker and more."
		"&eHow:&r barrel, grip and hammer assemblies plus iron and a slime pearl. Bullets and magazines have their own recipes (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r Seeker bullets home in on targets; good against flying mobs."
	]
	quest.064A1813B7F32692.title: "Phoenix Down"
	quest.064A1813B7F32692.quest_subtitle: "Optional: cheat death several times"
	quest.064A1813B7F32692.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r saves you from death, heals you, and gives you a few seconds of protection. It has several charges."
		"&eHow:&r three Angelheart Vials and an Angelic Feather. Vials need milk, glass, fertile essence and an infernal claw (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r keep it in your inventory before boss fights and Nether trips."
	]
	chapter.4CA1BE98C88CC02D.title: "Artifacts"
	chapter.4CA1BE98C88CC02D.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Simple, always-on curios from chests, ruins and Mimics."
	]
	quest.0825592CB940C7A2.title: "Trinkets in the Dirt"
	quest.0825592CB940C7A2.quest_subtitle: "Found, never crafted"
	quest.0825592CB940C7A2.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember leaving little gifts around the world for mortals to find. Some of them are still here.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Artifacts are curios with one or two fixed, always-on effects: no levels, no fuel, no upkeep. Wear them in the matching curio slot."
		"&eHow:&r they turn up in structure chests (mineshafts, dungeons, temples, villages, bastions, End cities), in archaeology loot, on rare mobs that spawn wearing one, and inside Mimics."
		"&eTip:&r a zombie in a cowboy hat is worth chasing: mobs that spawn wearing an artifact can drop it. Click the checkmark when you have read this."
	]
	quest.7A32332D465D9626.title: "Lid and Teeth"
	quest.7A32332D465D9626.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kill a Mimic"
	quest.7A32332D465D9626.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Mimic is a chest that bites. Each one drops a random artifact, so it is the closest thing to an artifact farm."
		"&eHow:&r they hide underground, in mineshafts and in the mod's small campsites. If a chest sits somewhere odd, hit it before you open it."
		"&eTip:&r they jump and hit hard for their size. Bring armour, not a wooden sword."
	]
	quest.5ED19D3EF6D45C87.title: "Strider Shoes"
	quest.5ED19D3EF6D45C87.quest_subtitle: "Lava is just a floor now"
	quest.5ED19D3EF6D45C87.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r shoes that let you walk on lava like a strider, and spare you the burn from magma and other hot floors."
		"&eHow:&r Nether fortress chests, ruined portals, dungeon chests, warm ocean ruins (brushing), or a piglin brute wearing them."
		"&eTip:&r they don't stop fire damage from falling in sideways. Keep a fire-resistance source too."
	]
	quest.3FC8239CBA03A6E9.title: "Rooted Boots"
	quest.3FC8239CBA03A6E9.quest_subtitle: "Grass feeds you"
	quest.3FC8239CBA03A6E9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r boots that slowly refill your hunger while you walk on grass, and make nearby plants grow after you eat."
		"&eHow:&r jungle temples, ancient cities, pillager outposts, strongholds, trail ruins (brushing), or a bogged wearing them."
		"&eTip:&r stand on the grass in your farm while you eat, and the crops get a free bonemeal."
	]
	quest.095234F6DB7A2C0A.title: "Flippers"
	quest.095234F6DB7A2C0A.quest_subtitle: "Swim like you mean it"
	quest.095234F6DB7A2C0A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r flippers that make you much faster and more agile in water."
		"&eHow:&r buried treasure, shipwrecks, big ocean ruins, or a drowned wearing them."
		"&eTip:&r with a Snorkel, an ocean monument becomes an afternoon job."
	]
	quest.792A54947C2F8222.title: "Steadfast Spikes"
	quest.792A54947C2F8222.quest_subtitle: "Nothing knocks you back"
	quest.792A54947C2F8222.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r spiked boots that make you immune to knockback."
		"&eHow:&r bastion treasure, pillager outposts, shipwrecks, armourer chests in villages, trail ruins, or a stray wearing them."
		"&eTip:&r no more being punched off a ledge by a ravager or into lava by a blaze."
	]
	quest.1C4DC8A0C7F2CA6D.title: "Snowshoes"
	quest.1C4DC8A0C7F2CA6D.quest_subtitle: "Snow, ice and powder snow"
	quest.1C4DC8A0C7F2CA6D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r shoes that let you walk on powder snow, move faster on snow and keep your grip on ice."
		"&eHow:&r igloos, snowy and taiga village houses, an ancient city's ice box, trail ruins, or a stray wearing them."
		"&eTip:&r powder snow traps are a classic grave in frozen peaks; these remove the risk."
	]
	quest.7EC263F4D29B2AC4.title: "Running Shoes"
	quest.7EC263F4D29B2AC4.quest_subtitle: "Faster sprint, higher step"
	quest.7EC263F4D29B2AC4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r shoes that boost your sprint speed and let you step up full blocks while sprinting."
		"&eHow:&r village armourers, shipwrecks, Nether fortresses, warm ocean ruins (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r the step-up means you can sprint over rough ground without jumping."
	]
	quest.0EDA7275844F3367.title: "Kitty Slippers"
	quest.0EDA7275844F3367.quest_subtitle: "Creepers keep their distance"
	quest.0EDA7275844F3367.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r slippers that make creepers avoid you and hiss at phantoms that try to swoop on you."
		"&eHow:&r jungle temples, buried treasure, village tanneries, desert pyramids (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r wear them while building: a creeper near a half-finished wall is the worst kind of surprise."
	]
	quest.0F08057A0BF42B8E.title: "Bunny Hoppers"
	quest.0F08057A0BF42B8E.quest_subtitle: "Higher jumps, softer landings"
	quest.0F08057A0BF42B8E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r hoppers that raise your jump height and cut your fall damage."
		"&eHow:&r jungle temples, buried treasure, bastion hoglin stables, village tanneries, warm ocean ruins, or a zombie wearing them."
		"&eTip:&r with a Cloud in a Bottle you can clear most walls in two jumps."
	]
	quest.21414E84473C21A6.title: "Aqua-Dashers"
	quest.21414E84473C21A6.quest_subtitle: "Sprint across water"
	quest.21414E84473C21A6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r shoes that let you run across water and other fluids while sprinting."
		"&eHow:&r mineshafts, ancient cities, strongholds, buried treasure, warm ocean ruins and trail ruins (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r stop sprinting and you sink, so don't try a lake while hungry."
	]
	quest.7876B884362669B5.title: "Withered Bracelet"
	quest.7876B884362669B5.quest_subtitle: "Your hits carry the wither"
	quest.7876B884362669B5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a bracelet whose melee attacks can inflict the wither effect."
		"&eHow:&r dungeon chests, Nether fortresses, bastion hoglin stables, cold ocean ruins (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r wither damage keeps ticking through a mob's regeneration."
	]
	quest.0C03388ADD3AB224.title: "Pickaxe Heater"
	quest.0C03388ADD3AB224.quest_subtitle: "Ores come out smelted"
	quest.0C03388ADD3AB224.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hand curio that smelts the ores you mine as they drop."
		"&eHow:&r mineshafts, ancient cities, strongholds, bastion hoglin stables, trail ruins (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r it saves furnace time only. Raw ore through the processing lines gives more metal per block."
	]
	quest.32F8C0C9134D54ED.title: "Pocket Piston"
	quest.32F8C0C9134D54ED.quest_subtitle: "Punch things further"
	quest.32F8C0C9134D54ED.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a piston on your hand that adds knockback to your attacks."
		"&eHow:&r village toolsmiths, Nether fortresses, pillager outposts, trail ruins (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r great on a ledge, terrible in a cave where the mob lands just out of reach."
	]
	quest.603258D41A4AE814.title: "Power Glove"
	quest.603258D41A4AE814.quest_subtitle: "More damage per swing"
	quest.603258D41A4AE814.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a glove that raises your attack damage."
		"&eHow:&r pillager outposts, ruined portals, strongholds, big ocean ruins, desert pyramids (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r pair it with Feral Claws for more hits that each land harder."
	]
	quest.78B0C00C2324BFEC.title: "Feral Claws"
	quest.78B0C00C2324BFEC.quest_subtitle: "Faster attacks"
	quest.78B0C00C2324BFEC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r claws that raise your attack speed, so your weapon recharges sooner."
		"&eHow:&r buried treasure, shipwrecks, village weaponsmiths, trail ruins (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r a slow heavy weapon gains the most from them."
	]
	quest.450DDA316EAC648C.title: "Onion Ring"
	quest.450DDA316EAC648C.quest_subtitle: "Snack, then dig faster"
	quest.450DDA316EAC648C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a ring you can't eat that gives you Haste for a while after you eat food."
		"&eHow:&r mineshafts, ancient cities, desert pyramids, warm ocean ruins, or a piglin brute wearing it."
		"&eTip:&r eat a cheap snack right before a long mining run."
	]
	quest.7FF7AFBFFB3F0929.title: "Golden Hook"
	quest.7FF7AFBFFB3F0929.quest_subtitle: "More experience from kills"
	quest.7FF7AFBFFB3F0929.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hook that makes creatures drop more experience."
		"&eHow:&r buried treasure, shipwrecks, bastion treasure, or a piglin or zombified piglin wearing it."
		"&eTip:&r wear it at your mob farm; enchanting and repairs cost a lot of levels."
	]
	quest.580FE592F7A6378E.title: "Vampiric Glove"
	quest.580FE592F7A6378E.quest_subtitle: "Hits heal you"
	quest.580FE592F7A6378E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a glove whose melee attacks give you back part of the damage dealt as health."
		"&eHow:&r mineshafts, desert pyramids, village armourers, warm ocean ruins, or a husk wearing it."
		"&eTip:&r it rewards staying in the fight: the more you hit, the less food you burn healing."
	]
	quest.6C9A18BBA7301F99.title: "Fire Gauntlet"
	quest.6C9A18BBA7301F99.quest_subtitle: "Your fists set things alight"
	quest.6C9A18BBA7301F99.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a gauntlet whose melee attacks set the target on fire."
		"&eHow:&r bastion treasure, ruined portals, big ocean ruins, cold ocean ruins (brushing), or a wither skeleton wearing it."
		"&eTip:&r fire-immune Nether mobs shrug it off; it shines in the Overworld."
	]
	quest.7F4CA6C060C4FC92.title: "Digging Claws"
	quest.7F4CA6C060C4FC92.quest_subtitle: "Faster digging, bare-handed or not"
	quest.7F4CA6C060C4FC92.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r claws that raise your mining speed (the tooltip also lists the tool tier your bare hands reach)."
		"&eHow:&r mineshafts, buried treasure, village toolsmiths, cold ocean ruins (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r they stack with your pickaxe's own speed, so they help long after your first tools."
	]
	quest.736D6E4470EED3D2.title: "Warp Drive"
	quest.736D6E4470EED3D2.quest_subtitle: "Ender pearls without the pearls"
	quest.736D6E4470EED3D2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a belt curio that stops ender pearls being used up when thrown (they cost hunger instead) and stops pearl damage."
		"&eHow:&r dungeon chests, ancient cities, End cities, village temples, desert wells (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r one stack of one pearl becomes a teleporter. Carry food."
	]
	quest.0F8D8BB79A9AB308.title: "Chorus Totem"
	quest.0F8D8BB79A9AB308.quest_subtitle: "A fatal hit sends you elsewhere"
	quest.0F8D8BB79A9AB308.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r when a hit would kill you, the totem may teleport you somewhere nearby instead."
		"&eHow:&r End city treasure and woodland mansions."
		"&eTip:&r read its tooltip for the chance and cooldown, and don't count on two saves in one fight."
	]
	quest.5EC8CC9B13F79399.title: "Helium Flamingo"
	quest.5EC8CC9B13F79399.quest_subtitle: "Swim through the air"
	quest.5EC8CC9B13F79399.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a pool float that lets you swim through the air for a short time; press its key while airborne."
		"&eHow:&r ancient cities, strongholds and End city treasure."
		"&eTip:&r helium (He) is about seven times less dense than air, which is why a real float filled with it would rise. This one just bends the rules."
	]
	quest.2334D8CB5B8CAA7E.title: "Crystal Heart"
	quest.2334D8CB5B8CAA7E.quest_subtitle: "More hearts"
	quest.2334D8CB5B8CAA7E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a heart that raises your maximum health."
		"&eHow:&r bastion treasure, pillager outposts and End city treasure."
		"&eTip:&r more health means more room for everything else to go wrong."
	]
	quest.4DDD4FBCCAAE8CA6.title: "Antidote Vessel"
	quest.4DDD4FBCCAAE8CA6.quest_subtitle: "Bad effects wear off fast"
	quest.4DDD4FBCCAAE8CA6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a flask that greatly shortens poison, wither, slowness and other harmful effects on you."
		"&eHow:&r bastion treasure, strongholds, village temples, cold ocean ruins, or a bogged or wither skeleton wearing it."
		"&eTip:&r real antidotes work by binding or neutralising the poison; this one is more polite and just shortens it."
	]
	quest.610C97008B56A838.title: "Universal Attractor"
	quest.610C97008B56A838.quest_subtitle: "Items come to you"
	quest.610C97008B56A838.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a magnet that pulls nearby items towards you (its tooltip names the toggle key)."
		"&eHow:&r desert pyramids, ruined portals, shipwrecks, desert wells (brushing), or a piglin or zombified piglin wearing it."
		"&eTip:&r switch it off near your sorting system, or it pulls items out of the floor and into your pockets."
	]
	quest.786586FBD2B8D453.title: "Obsidian Skull"
	quest.786586FBD2B8D453.quest_subtitle: "Burn once, then resist"
	quest.786586FBD2B8D453.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a skull that gives you fire resistance for a while after you take fire damage."
		"&eHow:&r mineshafts, ruined portals, shipwrecks, desert pyramids (brushing), or a piglin or zombified piglin wearing it."
		"&eTip:&r it reacts to the first burn, so it saves you from the second. Still bring a potion to the Nether."
	]
	quest.2470920CC6F8F1AE.title: "Cloud in a Bottle"
	quest.2470920CC6F8F1AE.quest_subtitle: "Jump again in mid-air"
	quest.2470920CC6F8F1AE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a bottled cloud that lets you double jump."
		"&eHow:&r mineshafts, pillager outposts, big ocean ruins, End city treasure, trail ruins (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r the second jump also resets a fall, so a late double jump can save you from a long drop."
	]
	quest.180547B0C9ED1FEF.title: "Charm of Shrinking"
	quest.180547B0C9ED1FEF.quest_subtitle: "Become small"
	quest.180547B0C9ED1FEF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a charm that shrinks you while worn."
		"&eHow:&r dungeon chests, Nether fortresses, ruined portals, village weaponsmiths, trail ruins (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r small players fit through one-block gaps. Great for sneaking, odd for building."
	]
	quest.03AD18955480DC78.title: "Charm of Sinking"
	quest.03AD18955480DC78.quest_subtitle: "Walk on the sea floor"
	quest.03AD18955480DC78.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a charm that lets you move freely underwater, as if on land."
		"&eHow:&r ancient cities, desert pyramids, shipwrecks, village temples, desert wells (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r you still need air. Bring a Snorkel or water breathing."
	]
	quest.47FD090E98E7B2EB.title: "Thorn Pendant"
	quest.47FD090E98E7B2EB.quest_subtitle: "Hit me, get hurt"
	quest.47FD090E98E7B2EB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a pendant with a chance to damage anything that attacks you."
		"&eHow:&r desert pyramids, ruined portals, trail ruins (brushing), or a husk wearing it."
		"&eTip:&r it stacks with the Thorns enchantment on your armour."
	]
	quest.7952A76D1115064D.title: "Flame Pendant"
	quest.7952A76D1115064D.quest_subtitle: "Burn whoever hits you"
	quest.7952A76D1115064D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a pendant with a chance to set attackers on fire, and to give you fire resistance when it does."
		"&eHow:&r desert pyramids, bastion hoglin stables, trail ruins (brushing), or a skeleton wearing it."
		"&eTip:&r it does nothing to fire-immune Nether mobs; it shines in the Overworld."
	]
	quest.575F275E95582A23.title: "Shock Pendant"
	quest.575F275E95582A23.quest_subtitle: "Lightning for your attackers"
	quest.575F275E95582A23.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a pendant with a chance to strike attackers with lightning, and that protects you from lightning yourself."
		"&eHow:&r ancient cities and desert pyramids (chests and brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r lightning that hits a creeper charges it. Be careful who you anger."
	]
	quest.256DBA9768E9850F.title: "Panic Necklace"
	quest.256DBA9768E9850F.quest_subtitle: "Hurt, then run"
	quest.256DBA9768E9850F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a necklace that gives you a burst of speed after you take damage."
		"&eHow:&r mineshafts, bastion treasure and pillager outposts."
		"&eTip:&r it turns a bad fight into a quick escape; use it."
	]
	quest.69EDCD758F093395.title: "Cross Necklace"
	quest.69EDCD758F093395.quest_subtitle: "Longer safety after a hit"
	quest.69EDCD758F093395.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a necklace that lengthens the short invulnerable moment after you take damage."
		"&eHow:&r bastion treasure, Nether fortresses, pillager outposts, big ocean ruins, village temples."
		"&eTip:&r it shines against many weak hits at once, like a swarm or a skeleton volley."
	]
	quest.0E53A65593A98BB7.title: "Lucky Scarf"
	quest.0E53A65593A98BB7.quest_subtitle: "One more level of Fortune"
	quest.0E53A65593A98BB7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a scarf that adds a level of Fortune to the blocks you mine."
		"&eHow:&r igloos, ruined portals, strongholds, buried treasure, big and cold ocean ruins."
		"&eTip:&r it stacks with a Fortune pickaxe, which makes it best on diamonds, coal and other gem ores."
	]
	quest.67F4640E1F405AFE.title: "Scarf of Invisibility"
	quest.67F4640E1F405AFE.quest_subtitle: "Now you don't see me"
	quest.67F4640E1F405AFE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a scarf that turns you invisible while worn."
		"&eHow:&r desert pyramids, pillager outposts, shipwrecks, village tanneries, or a zombie wearing it."
		"&eTip:&r armour still shows. Take it off for the full effect."
	]
	quest.3A9E24BEE1A48D76.title: "Angler's Hat"
	quest.3A9E24BEE1A48D76.quest_subtitle: "Better fishing"
	quest.3A9E24BEE1A48D76.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hat that adds a level of Luck of the Sea and of Lure to your fishing."
		"&eHow:&r jungle temples, buried treasure, big ocean ruins, village tanneries, cold ocean ruins (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r with a good rod, treasure from fishing becomes a real income."
	]
	quest.2CF0DDD1D47A7899.title: "Cowboy Hat"
	quest.2CF0DDD1D47A7899.quest_subtitle: "Faster mounts"
	quest.2CF0DDD1D47A7899.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hat that makes whatever you ride faster."
		"&eHow:&r Nether fortresses, ruined portals, bastion hoglin stables, desert pyramids (brushing), or a zombie wearing it."
		"&eTip:&r it works on horses, pigs and striders alike."
	]
	quest.337CCFDB8E65D0FF.title: "Superstitious Hat"
	quest.337CCFDB8E65D0FF.quest_subtitle: "One more level of Looting"
	quest.337CCFDB8E65D0FF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hat that adds a level of Looting to your kills."
		"&eHow:&r mineshafts, pillager outposts, strongholds, big ocean ruins, village armourers, desert wells (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r stack it with a Looting sword at your mob farm."
	]
	quest.53AE813B277289B9.title: "Villager Hat"
	quest.53AE813B277289B9.quest_subtitle: "Cheaper trades"
	quest.53AE813B277289B9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hat that lowers the prices villagers ask you."
		"&eHow:&r village houses in every biome, igloos and trail ruins (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r wear it before you open the trade window; prices update as you look."
	]
	quest.2AEA1641BEB5D7BA.title: "Night Vision Goggles"
	quest.2AEA1641BEB5D7BA.quest_subtitle: "See in the dark"
	quest.2AEA1641BEB5D7BA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r goggles that give you night vision while worn."
		"&eHow:&r mineshafts, Nether fortresses, ruined portals, shipwrecks, desert pyramids (brushing), or a skeleton wearing them."
		"&eTip:&r spotting ore in a dark cave gets much easier; mobs still spawn there."
	]
	quest.413E120FD88D3DD5.title: "Snorkel"
	quest.413E120FD88D3DD5.quest_subtitle: "Breathe underwater"
	quest.413E120FD88D3DD5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a snorkel that lets you breathe underwater for a while."
		"&eHow:&r buried treasure, shipwrecks, big ocean ruins, desert pyramids (brushing), or a drowned wearing it."
		"&eTip:&r its tooltip says how long; pair it with the Charm of Sinking for long dives."
	]
	quest.51964465B0FAEE79.title: "Novelty Drinking Hat"
	quest.51964465B0FAEE79.quest_subtitle: "Drink and eat much faster"
	quest.51964465B0FAEE79.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the grand version of the drinking hat: potions and food go down much faster."
		"&eHow:&r the same loot as the plastic hat (mineshafts, buried treasure, Nether fortresses, desert wells), only rarer, or a skeleton wearing it."
		"&eTip:&r a fast potion in a boss fight is worth more than it sounds."
	]
	quest.42454D1D3F212C58.title: "Plastic Drinking Hat"
	quest.42454D1D3F212C58.quest_subtitle: "Drink and eat faster"
	quest.42454D1D3F212C58.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hat with two cans and a straw: potions and food go down faster."
		"&eHow:&r mineshafts, buried treasure, Nether fortresses, desert wells (brushing), or a skeleton wearing it."
		"&eTip:&r real plastic is a polymer: long chains of small molecules such as ethylene, which the pack teaches you to make later."
	]
	quest.46D48F3B764C6FD1.title: "Whoopee Cushion"
	quest.46D48F3B764C6FD1.quest_subtitle: "Secret: it does what you think"
	quest.46D48F3B764C6FD1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a cushion that makes a rude noise when you crouch. That's all it does."
		"&eHow:&r spawn bonus chests, desert pyramids, village tanneries, trail ruins (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r the relics page has a secret for this one too."
	]
	quest.473753002D1A3C2E.title: "Everlasting Beef"
	quest.473753002D1A3C2E.quest_subtitle: "Raw beef that never runs out"
	quest.473753002D1A3C2E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a piece of raw beef you can eat forever: it isn't used up."
		"&eHow:&r rarely dropped by cows and mooshrooms, or from village butchers and bastion hoglin stables."
		"&eTip:&r cook it to get the Eternal Steak, a better meal that also never runs out."
	]
	quest.597130DD51B23733.title: "Eternal Steak"
	quest.597130DD51B23733.quest_subtitle: "Cooked, and still everlasting"
	quest.597130DD51B23733.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the cooked Everlasting Beef: a full steak's food that is never used up."
		"&eHow:&r cook Everlasting Beef in a furnace, smoker or on a campfire."
		"&eTip:&r cooking browns meat by the Maillard reaction: amino acids and sugars react at about 140 °C into hundreds of flavour compounds."
	]
	quest.6A437B019C98256F.title: "Umbrella"
	quest.6A437B019C98256F.quest_subtitle: "A parachute and a shield"
	quest.6A437B019C98256F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r held in your hand, the umbrella slows your fall and can block like a shield."
		"&eHow:&r buried treasure, desert pyramids, village tanneries, desert wells (brushing)."
		"&eTip:&r keep it in hand while building high up: a slip becomes a slow drift."
	]
	chapter.4A9FBEAB7C073748.title: "Silent Gear"
	chapter.4A9FBEAB7C073748.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Gear built part by part: the material decides the stats."
	]
	quest.0A9ABCCB41A350E0.title: "Every Part a Choice"
	quest.0A9ABCCB41A350E0.quest_subtitle: "How Silent Gear works"
	quest.0A9ABCCB41A350E0.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember weapons shaped to the hand that held them. Here you get to shape your own again.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r every Silent Gear item is assembled from parts (head, rod, binding, grip, tip, coating), and each part takes the stats and traits of its material."
		"&eHow:&r make a blueprint or template for a part, craft the part from a material, then put the parts together in a crafting grid. JEI and the Material Book show every material's stats."
		"&eTip:&r click the checkmark when you have read this. The quests below are one per gear type."
	]
	quest.79DC5609AB064578.title: "Metal and Fuel"
	quest.79DC5609AB064578.quest_subtitle: "The two things every smith needs"
	quest.79DC5609AB064578.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r iron is the first good head material for Silent Gear parts, and coal fuels the smelting (and later the Alloy Forge)."
		"&eChemistry:&r in a furnace, coal burns to carbon monoxide, which strips the oxygen from iron oxide: Fe₂O₃ + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO₂."
		"&eHow:&r smelt raw iron with coal. Hold one of each."
		"&eTip:&r every quest on this page hangs from here: pick the gear types you want and ignore the rest until you need them."
	]
	quest.0F5E40E0CA466BAB.title: "Sword"
	quest.0F5E40E0CA466BAB.quest_subtitle: "The classic"
	quest.0F5E40E0CA466BAB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a sword: a blade and a rod, plus optional binding, grip and coating."
		"&eHow:&r sword blueprint (blueprint paper and a stick), a sword blade from your material, then the blade and a rod in a crafting grid."
		"&eTip:&r the blade's material sets damage and durability; the rod mostly adds traits."
	]
	quest.6DB927B193234878.title: "Katana"
	quest.6DB927B193234878.quest_subtitle: "Fast and sharp"
	quest.6DB927B193234878.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a katana: a long single-edged blade that swings faster than a sword."
		"&eHow:&r katana blueprint and a katana blade, then assemble with a rod (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r light, fast weapons suit materials with high attack speed."
	]
	quest.318E3560A6EA7DF2.title: "Machete"
	quest.318E3560A6EA7DF2.quest_subtitle: "Cuts plants as well as mobs"
	quest.318E3560A6EA7DF2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a machete: a heavy blade that also clears leaves and plants quickly."
		"&eHow:&r machete blueprint and blade, then assemble with a rod (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the right tool for clearing a jungle around a base."
	]
	quest.59C13E452BDBD2BB.title: "Knife"
	quest.59C13E452BDBD2BB.quest_subtitle: "A small blade with uses"
	quest.59C13E452BDBD2BB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a knife: a quick little blade, and Silent Gear's tool for cutting logs into template boards."
		"&eHow:&r knife blueprint and blade, then assemble with a rod (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a knife cuts one log into six template boards (a tool action; check JEI)."
	]
	quest.05756882F26D8649.title: "Dagger"
	quest.05756882F26D8649.quest_subtitle: "The fastest blade"
	quest.05756882F26D8649.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a dagger: very fast attacks with low damage per hit."
		"&eHow:&r dagger blueprint and blade, then assemble with a rod (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a dagger built from a material with an on-hit trait triggers that trait often."
	]
	quest.493470027E0A4296.title: "Trident"
	quest.493470027E0A4296.quest_subtitle: "Throw it, call it back"
	quest.493470027E0A4296.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Silent Gear trident built from prongs of your chosen material."
		"&eHow:&r the trident blueprint needs a vanilla trident and a heart of the sea (check JEI); then make the prongs and assemble."
		"&eTip:&r drowned holding a trident are the only source of the vanilla one; fight them in the rain-free shallows."
	]
	quest.3FC332E18FBA8EE1.title: "Mace Blueprint"
	quest.3FC332E18FBA8EE1.quest_subtitle: "Heavy, and better from above"
	quest.3FC332E18FBA8EE1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the blueprint for Silent Gear's mace, a heavy weapon with a mace core of your material."
		"&eHow:&r blueprint paper and a breeze rod (from breezes in trial chambers); check JEI."
		"&eTip:&r like the vanilla mace, it rewards hitting from a height."
	]
	quest.58B2DFBA4BBE5BA9.title: "Spear"
	quest.58B2DFBA4BBE5BA9.quest_subtitle: "Long reach"
	quest.58B2DFBA4BBE5BA9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a spear: a tipped weapon that reaches further than a sword."
		"&eHow:&r spear blueprint and a spear tip, then assemble with a rod (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the extra reach keeps creepers a step further away."
	]
	quest.2B8A3CBDB18111DC.title: "Bow"
	quest.2B8A3CBDB18111DC.quest_subtitle: "Limbs of any material"
	quest.2B8A3CBDB18111DC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a bow whose limbs set draw speed, damage and range."
		"&eHow:&r bow blueprint, bow limbs and a bowstring (cord) of string or flax, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r flax string from Silent Gear's flax plant makes a decent cord."
	]
	quest.5CF44C605A832B61.title: "Crossbow"
	quest.5CF44C605A832B61.quest_subtitle: "Slow to load, hard to stop"
	quest.5CF44C605A832B61.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a crossbow built from crossbow limbs and a cord."
		"&eHow:&r crossbow blueprint, limbs and a cord, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r load it before a fight; the first shot is free."
	]
	quest.0F4C3DF5F57745CE.title: "Slingshot"
	quest.0F4C3DF5F57745CE.quest_subtitle: "Pebbles with purpose"
	quest.0F4C3DF5F57745CE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a slingshot that fires pebbles and other small shot."
		"&eHow:&r slingshot blueprint, limbs and a cord, then assemble (check JEI). It shoots Silent Gear pebbles."
		"&eTip:&r cheap ammunition makes it a good way to pull mobs out of a group."
	]
	quest.54DDB2BA29713C08.title: "Arrows"
	quest.54DDB2BA29713C08.quest_subtitle: "Ammunition from parts"
	quest.54DDB2BA29713C08.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Silent Gear arrows: arrow heads, a shaft and fletching, built as one stack-like item."
		"&eHow:&r arrow blueprint and arrow heads, then assemble with a rod and fletching (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r heads of a heavy material hit harder; fletching changes how straight they fly."
	]
	quest.2E6BF88352A9D27C.title: "Fletching Blueprint"
	quest.2E6BF88352A9D27C.quest_subtitle: "Feathers for the arrows"
	quest.2E6BF88352A9D27C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the blueprint for fletching, the feather part of Silent Gear arrows."
		"&eHow:&r two blueprint paper and a feather (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r Silent Gear's fluffy feathers work as a fletching material too."
	]
	quest.4CDBB054BEC49AE0.title: "Pickaxe"
	quest.4CDBB054BEC49AE0.quest_subtitle: "The one you already have"
	quest.4CDBB054BEC49AE0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Silent Gear pickaxe, the first part-built tool you made."
		"&eHow:&r pickaxe blueprint and head, then assemble with a rod (check JEI). You made one on the main path."
		"&eTip:&r upgrade the head material first; it decides mining tier and speed."
	]
	quest.3DA6777492FCE5B6.title: "Shovel"
	quest.3DA6777492FCE5B6.quest_subtitle: "Dirt, sand and gravel"
	quest.3DA6777492FCE5B6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a shovel built from a shovel head and a rod."
		"&eHow:&r shovel blueprint and head, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a fast shovel makes clay and sand runs for glassmaking painless."
	]
	quest.0C6A6DBB2FFBD20B.title: "Axe"
	quest.0C6A6DBB2FFBD20B.quest_subtitle: "Trees and heavy hits"
	quest.0C6A6DBB2FFBD20B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an axe built from an axe head and a rod: a woodcutter and a slow, heavy weapon."
		"&eHow:&r axe blueprint and head, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r it also strips logs for charcoal and building."
	]
	quest.7D6EFD3C45E08BED.title: "Paxel"
	quest.7D6EFD3C45E08BED.quest_subtitle: "Three tools in one"
	quest.7D6EFD3C45E08BED.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Silent Gear paxel: pickaxe, axe and shovel in one head."
		"&eHow:&r paxel blueprint and a paxel head (it needs more material than a pickaxe), then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r one tool slot freed on long trips."
	]
	quest.3E0B051A62E3E2C5.title: "Hammer"
	quest.3E0B051A62E3E2C5.quest_subtitle: "Mine 3x3"
	quest.3E0B051A62E3E2C5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hammer that breaks a 3x3 area of stone and ore at once."
		"&eHow:&r hammer blueprint and head, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r it also crushes Silent Gear ingots into dust; the dust quests below need it."
	]
	quest.235007F344B83251.title: "Excavator"
	quest.235007F344B83251.quest_subtitle: "Dig 3x3"
	quest.235007F344B83251.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the shovel's version of the hammer: dirt, sand and gravel in 3x3."
		"&eHow:&r excavator blueprint and head, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r perfect for clearing space for a big build."
	]
	quest.16C24E4E2F59A875.title: "Mattock"
	quest.16C24E4E2F59A875.quest_subtitle: "Hoe, axe and shovel"
	quest.16C24E4E2F59A875.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a mattock: a farming tool that tills, chops and digs."
		"&eHow:&r mattock blueprint and head, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r one tool for the whole farm."
	]
	quest.7C63A1656E94A831.title: "Sickle"
	quest.7C63A1656E94A831.quest_subtitle: "Harvest in a sweep"
	quest.7C63A1656E94A831.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a sickle that cuts and harvests plants over an area."
		"&eHow:&r sickle blueprint and blade, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a quick harvest for wide crop fields."
	]
	quest.795639915B305103.title: "Shears"
	quest.795639915B305103.quest_subtitle: "Wool, leaves and string"
	quest.795639915B305103.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Silent Gear shears with stats from their blades."
		"&eHow:&r shears blueprint and shear blades, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r durable shears are worth it for a wool farm."
	]
	quest.7156A7DBA9E430D1.title: "Fishing Rod"
	quest.7156A7DBA9E430D1.quest_subtitle: "A rod with a real hook"
	quest.7156A7DBA9E430D1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a fishing rod with a hook of your chosen material."
		"&eHow:&r fishing rod blueprint, a fishing hook and a cord, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the hook's material sets the rod's durability and traits."
	]
	quest.4B5D62CEFFE2AF1F.title: "Prospector Hammer"
	quest.4B5D62CEFFE2AF1F.quest_subtitle: "Listen for ore"
	quest.4B5D62CEFFE2AF1F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hammer that scans for ores near the block you strike."
		"&eHow:&r prospector hammer blueprint and head, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r pair it with the Spectrometer from the main path to plan a dig before you start."
	]
	quest.4388037159800098.title: "Shield"
	quest.4388037159800098.quest_subtitle: "Block with your best metal"
	quest.4388037159800098.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a shield built from a shield plate of any material."
		"&eHow:&r shield blueprint and plate, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a tough material means fewer repairs between fights."
	]
	quest.65F1E1DD48C12482.title: "Helmet"
	quest.65F1E1DD48C12482.quest_subtitle: "Armour from plates"
	quest.65F1E1DD48C12482.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a helmet built from helmet plates of your material."
		"&eHow:&r helmet blueprint and plates, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r armour from parts can carry traits that vanilla armour never has."
	]
	quest.0308945DEC34C111.title: "Chestplate"
	quest.0308945DEC34C111.quest_subtitle: "The biggest piece"
	quest.0308945DEC34C111.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a chestplate built from chestplate plates."
		"&eHow:&r chestplate blueprint and plates, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r it carries the most armour, so give it your best material."
	]
	quest.644B61AA5A775708.title: "Leggings"
	quest.644B61AA5A775708.quest_subtitle: "Plate for the legs"
	quest.644B61AA5A775708.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r leggings built from legging plates."
		"&eHow:&r leggings blueprint and plates, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a lining (the blueprint below) adds a second material's traits."
	]
	quest.63337FD8FB882597.title: "Boots"
	quest.63337FD8FB882597.quest_subtitle: "Plate for the feet"
	quest.63337FD8FB882597.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r boots built from boot plates."
		"&eHow:&r boots blueprint and plates, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r linings work on boots too; check the Material Book for useful traits."
	]
	quest.0EA0DAB1B70C29C0.title: "Elytra Blueprint"
	quest.0EA0DAB1B70C29C0.quest_subtitle: "Wings with stats"
	quest.0EA0DAB1B70C29C0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the blueprint for Silent Gear's elytra, whose wings take stats from their material."
		"&eHow:&r blueprint paper, gold, phantom membrane and a real elytra from an End ship (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r you need one vanilla elytra to make the blueprint, then can build wings from better materials."
	]
	quest.17452A762CD5274A.title: "Ring"
	quest.17452A762CD5274A.quest_subtitle: "A trait on your finger"
	quest.17452A762CD5274A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a ring: a shank and an optional gem setting, worn as a curio."
		"&eHow:&r ring blueprint and shank, then assemble with a setting (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r jewellery gives you its material's traits while worn, so pick a material for its trait."
	]
	quest.6DADFD5B81C435E8.title: "Bracelet"
	quest.6DADFD5B81C435E8.quest_subtitle: "A trait on your wrist"
	quest.6DADFD5B81C435E8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a bracelet: a band and an optional setting, worn as a curio."
		"&eHow:&r bracelet blueprint and band, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a second jewellery slot for a second trait."
	]
	quest.59223261D2D2CB2D.title: "Necklace"
	quest.59223261D2D2CB2D.quest_subtitle: "A trait at your neck"
	quest.59223261D2D2CB2D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a necklace: a chain and an optional setting, worn as a curio."
		"&eHow:&r necklace blueprint and chain, then assemble (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the third jewellery piece; together they can carry three different traits."
	]
	quest.567A43CFF1ADD79A.title: "Lining Blueprint"
	quest.567A43CFF1ADD79A.quest_subtitle: "Soft layers inside armour"
	quest.567A43CFF1ADD79A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the blueprint for armour linings, an extra material layer inside a piece of armour."
		"&eHow:&r three blueprint paper, two wool and two string (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a lining adds its material's traits without changing the armour plates."
	]
	quest.52354588C5E5AB69.title: "Tips"
	quest.52354588C5E5AB69.quest_subtitle: "A harder edge"
	quest.52354588C5E5AB69.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a tip: an upgrade part that caps a tool or weapon with another material."
		"&eHow:&r tip blueprint (two blueprint paper, paper and stone), then a tip from your material; add it to a tool in a crafting grid."
		"&eTip:&r a diamond or quartz tip is a cheap upgrade for an iron tool."
	]
	quest.576EA99057E3A9E4.title: "Coating Blueprint"
	quest.576EA99057E3A9E4.quest_subtitle: "Plate a part in a better material"
	quest.576EA99057E3A9E4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the blueprint for coatings, a layer of a better material over a tool's main part."
		"&eHow:&r four blueprint paper, a diamond and an emerald (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the Coatings quest on the Gear and Comfort page covers the smithing template route."
	]
	quest.742CF58E4ADB7CF4.title: "Grip Blueprint"
	quest.742CF58E4ADB7CF4.quest_subtitle: "Something to hold onto"
	quest.742CF58E4ADB7CF4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the blueprint for grips, a handle wrap that adds its material's traits."
		"&eHow:&r two blueprint paper and a grip material such as leather or wool (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r grips are cheap, so try different ones."
	]
	quest.4FEEF30AEEBEB978.title: "Binding Blueprint"
	quest.4FEEF30AEEBEB978.quest_subtitle: "Tie the head on tight"
	quest.4FEEF30AEEBEB978.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the blueprint for bindings, which tie a head to its rod and add their own traits."
		"&eHow:&r blueprint paper and two binding materials such as string or vines (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the Material Book shows which bindings add which traits."
	]
	quest.293C0C68417EB05D.title: "Rods"
	quest.293C0C68417EB05D.quest_subtitle: "The handle of every tool"
	quest.293C0C68417EB05D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a rod: the handle part of nearly every Silent Gear tool and weapon."
		"&eHow:&r rod blueprint (blueprint paper and sticks), then rods from wood, bone, blaze rods, metal and more."
		"&eTip:&r the rod's material adds traits; a blaze rod handle is a classic."
	]
	quest.637DBDB781211606.title: "Salvager"
	quest.637DBDB781211606.quest_subtitle: "Old gear back into parts"
	quest.637DBDB781211606.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a machine that breaks old Silent Gear items back into their parts."
		"&eHow:&r a piston, crimson iron ingots, an iron block and obsidian (check JEI). Crimson iron ore is in the Nether."
		"&eTip:&r salvage before upgrading; some material is lost, most comes back."
	]
	quest.23CB2F29E36CB3AD.title: "Material Grader"
	quest.23CB2F29E36CB3AD.quest_subtitle: "Better grades, better stats"
	quest.23CB2F29E36CB3AD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a machine that grades materials; a higher grade adds bonus stats to every part made from it."
		"&eHow:&r quartz, iron, three blaze gold ingots and an Advanced Upgrade Base (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r grade the material you use for heads; that's where the stats live."
	]
	quest.16388486D2C83958.title: "Glowing Dust"
	quest.16388486D2C83958.quest_subtitle: "The first grading catalyst"
	quest.16388486D2C83958.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the tier 1 catalyst for the Material Grader, spent on each try."
		"&eHow:&r a stick, two glowstone dust and a quartz make four (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r keep a stack by the grader."
	]
	quest.02E126312998CD8F.title: "Blazing Dust"
	quest.02E126312998CD8F.quest_subtitle: "The second catalyst"
	quest.02E126312998CD8F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the tier 2 Grader catalyst, for higher grades."
		"&eHow:&r blaze gold dust and two glowstone dust make four. Crush blaze gold with a hammer first (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a better catalyst raises the highest grade you can reach."
	]
	quest.7BDB29F06BDAC20A.title: "Glittery Dust"
	quest.7BDB29F06BDAC20A.quest_subtitle: "The third catalyst"
	quest.7BDB29F06BDAC20A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the tier 3 Grader catalyst, for the best grades."
		"&eHow:&r popped chorus fruit, emerald nuggets, glowstone dust and a nether banana make eight (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r chorus grows in the End; nether bananas grow on netherwood trees."
	]
	quest.483F16D41646920A.title: "Recrystallizer"
	quest.483F16D41646920A.quest_subtitle: "Grow hybrid gems"
	quest.483F16D41646920A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a machine that fuses gems into hybrid gem materials with mixed stats."
		"&eHow:&r azure electrum ingots, an emerald, a diamond, purpur blocks and a gold block (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r experiment with cheap gems before feeding it diamonds."
	]
	quest.06F2A9B0EEB330B3.title: "Alloy Forge"
	quest.06F2A9B0EEB330B3.quest_subtitle: "Silent Gear's alloy furnace"
	quest.06F2A9B0EEB330B3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the forge that makes Silent Gear's alloys: blaze gold, crimson steel, azure electrum and tyrian steel."
		"&eHow:&r crimson steel ingots, blackstone and an iron block (check JEI). Fuel it like a furnace."
		"&eTip:&r the forge gives more ingots per batch than the crafting routes."
	]
	quest.266FBA2011E70916.title: "Starlight Charger"
	quest.266FBA2011E70916.quest_subtitle: "Charge materials at night"
	quest.266FBA2011E70916.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a block that collects starlight at night and charges Silent Gear materials for a bonus."
		"&eHow:&r quartz blocks, glass, polished blackstone and a blaze gold block (check JEI). Place it under open sky."
		"&eTip:&r the catalyst's tier caps how strong the charge gets."
	]
	quest.0AF4392EBBE047D5.title: "Crimson Steel Block"
	quest.0AF4392EBBE047D5.quest_subtitle: "Nine ingots of heat-forged steel"
	quest.0AF4392EBBE047D5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a storage block of crimson steel."
		"&eHow:&r nine crimson steel ingots from the Alloy Forge."
		"&eTip:&r it decorates as well as it stores."
	]
	quest.68CF20B3CCE7E0A4.title: "Azure Electrum Block"
	quest.68CF20B3CCE7E0A4.quest_subtitle: "The End's metal, stacked"
	quest.68CF20B3CCE7E0A4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a storage block of azure electrum."
		"&eHow:&r nine azure electrum ingots; azure silver ore is in the End and needs a netherite-tier pick."
		"&eTip:&r electrum is a real gold-silver alloy; the azure part is Silent Gear's."
	]
	quest.7B1458AEAC6705E8.title: "Tyrian Steel Block"
	quest.7B1458AEAC6705E8.quest_subtitle: "The finest alloy, by the block"
	quest.7B1458AEAC6705E8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a storage block of tyrian steel, Silent Gear's top alloy."
		"&eHow:&r nine tyrian steel ingots from the Alloy Forge (crimson steel, azure electrum, crushed shulker shell, netherite scrap; check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r make sure you have enough ingots for your gear first."
	]
	quest.12F3F34492285A02.title: "Blaze Gold Dust"
	quest.12F3F34492285A02.quest_subtitle: "Crushed for the charger"
	quest.12F3F34492285A02.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r blaze gold crushed into dust: the tier 1 Starlight Charger catalyst and the base of blazing dust."
		"&eHow:&r crush a blaze gold ingot with a hammer (a tool action; check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r crushing a metal hugely increases its surface area, which is why fine powders react so much faster than bars."
	]
	quest.5A16C9F6F3C63D2D.title: "Azure Silver Dust"
	quest.5A16C9F6F3C63D2D.quest_subtitle: "A higher charger catalyst"
	quest.5A16C9F6F3C63D2D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r azure silver crushed into dust, for the charger and for starmetal."
		"&eHow:&r crush an azure silver ingot with a hammer (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r keep two for the starmetal recipe."
	]
	quest.72F86F27B5282950.title: "Starmetal Dust"
	quest.72F86F27B5282950.quest_subtitle: "A piece of a star, as a material"
	quest.72F86F27B5282950.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r starmetal dust, a late Silent Gear material and charger catalyst."
		"&eHow:&r azure electrum dust, two azure silver dust, blaze gold dust and a nether star fragment make three (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r one Nether Star crafts into nine fragments."
	]
	quest.7EADC55FBD29E134.title: "Any Repair Kit"
	quest.7EADC55FBD29E134.quest_subtitle: "Very crude, crude, sturdy, crimson or azure"
	quest.7EADC55FBD29E134.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a repair kit holds repair materials and mends Silent Gear in a crafting grid. Five tiers, each holding more."
		"&eHow:&r very crude (template boards, a stick and stone), crude (iron), sturdy (iron and a diamond), crimson (crimson steel and blaze gold), azure (azure electrum and an emerald). Check JEI."
		"&eTip:&r better kits hold more material and repair more per use (check the tooltip)."
	]
	chapter.58F2F526022035F5.title: "Quality of Life"
	chapter.58F2F526022035F5.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Small things that make a big difference."
	]
	quest.082FF7126C739233.title: "Comfort First"
	quest.082FF7126C739233.quest_subtitle: "A catalogue of small conveniences"
	quest.082FF7126C739233.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember never wasting a motion. These small things feel familiar.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r this page collects the mods that save time and clicks: guidebooks, backpacks, waystones, maps, keybinds and the Utilitarian shortcuts."
		"&eHow:&r each row is one topic. Nearly everything here is optional, so pick what helps you. Click the checkmark to open the page."
		"&eTip:&r none of this is needed for the main path, but most of it pays for itself within an hour."
	]
	quest.7861E90E0F778D26.title: "One Book to Rule Them All"
	quest.7861E90E0F778D26.quest_subtitle: "Every guidebook in one item"
	quest.7861E90E0F778D26.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Akashic Tome merges every mod's guidebook into one item."
		"&eHow:&r craft it, then right-click it with other guidebooks to add them."
		"&eTip:&r right-click the tome to choose which book to open."
	]
	quest.24E1DFE3C86BAB94.title: "Find Anything"
	quest.24E1DFE3C86BAB94.quest_subtitle: "Compasses for biomes and structures"
	quest.24E1DFE3C86BAB94.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Nature's Compass finds biomes; Explorer's Compass finds structures (Nether Fortresses, Ancient Cities, villages)."
		"&eHow:&r craft both (check JEI), right-click to pick a target, then follow the needle."
		"&eTip:&r the Explorer's Compass is the fastest way to find an Ancient City for the Deeper and Darker quests."
	]
	quest.417C968CF0B6DB90.title: "No More Mob Spawns"
	quest.417C968CF0B6DB90.quest_subtitle: "One torch, a huge safe radius"
	quest.417C968CF0B6DB90.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Mega Torch stops hostile mobs spawning naturally in a huge radius."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the recipe and place it near the middle of your base."
		"&eTip:&r it blocks natural spawns only. Spawners and Simulation Chambers still work."
	]
	quest.2CDD3C38275B155C.title: "Graves"
	quest.2CDD3C38275B155C.quest_subtitle: "Your items wait where you fell"
	quest.2CDD3C38275B155C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r if you die, Corail Tombstone keeps your items in a grave where you fell."
		"&eHow:&r walk back and open the grave to recover everything. Click the checkmark once you've read this."
		"&eTip:&r JourneyMap drops a waypoint where you died, so the grave is easy to find."
	]
	quest.6DE92B29EF0F35A9.title: "Backups"
	quest.6DE92B29EF0F35A9.quest_subtitle: "Optional: automatic world saves"
	quest.6DE92B29EF0F35A9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Simple Backups saves your world automatically."
		"&eHow:&r on a server, backups live in the server's backups folder. In single player, look in your instance folder."
		"&eTip:&r copy a backup somewhere else before trying risky reactor builds."
	]
	quest.604BDD9A6947B39B.title: "Dread Lamp"
	quest.604BDD9A6947B39B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the Mega Torch for Nether mobs"
	quest.604BDD9A6947B39B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Dread Lamp blocks Nether mob spawns in a large radius, the way the Mega Torch does for Overworld mobs."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Place it at your Nether base or portal hub."
		"&eTip:&r place it before building in the Nether so your base stays quiet."
	]
	quest.168A3AC3F1C50464.title: "Rest Anywhere"
	quest.168A3AC3F1C50464.quest_subtitle: "Skip the night, keep your spawn"
	quest.168A3AC3F1C50464.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r A &esleeping bag&r from Comforts skips the night without moving your spawn point, so it's ideal while exploring."
		"&eHow:&r 3 wool of one colour in a vertical column. Any colour of sleeping bag counts."
		"&eTip:&r Hammocks skip the day instead (Gear and Comfort page)."
	]
	quest.7B910D75AE5CB5BE.title: "Crafting on a Stick"
	quest.7B910D75AE5CB5BE.quest_subtitle: "A crafting table that fits in your pocket"
	quest.7B910D75AE5CB5BE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a crafting table you carry around. Right-click it to open a 3x3 grid anywhere: in a mine, out exploring, mid-build."
		"&eHow:&r craft it from a crafting table and a stick (check JEI). The same mod makes pocket versions of the stonecutter, smithing table, anvil, grindstone, loom and cartography table."
		"&eTip:&r it saves a hotbar slot over placing and breaking tables. The pocket stonecutter is great for building with Create Deco and Rechiseled blocks."
	]
	quest.0168A13FA2435F4D.title: "A Whole Workshop"
	quest.0168A13FA2435F4D.quest_subtitle: "Pocket stonecutter and smithing table"
	quest.0168A13FA2435F4D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r optional: the pocket stonecutter and smithing table."
		"&eHow:&r each one is its block plus a stick (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the smithing table is how netherite and Apotheosis upgrades are applied, so it's handy to carry."
	]
	quest.4BC3CD31C26ED641.title: "Backpack Upgrades"
	quest.4BC3CD31C26ED641.quest_subtitle: "Pickup and magnet upgrades"
	quest.4BC3CD31C26ED641.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r pickup and magnet upgrades pull items straight into your backpack."
		"&eHow:&r craft an Upgrade Base, then the upgrades (check JEI). Put them in the backpack's upgrade slots."
		"&eTip:&r set a filter on the pickup upgrade so it only grabs ores and drops you actually want."
	]
	quest.288CF747C2D939F7.title: "Iron Backpack"
	quest.288CF747C2D939F7.quest_subtitle: "More slots and more upgrade space"
	quest.288CF747C2D939F7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each backpack tier adds inventory rows and upgrade slots: iron, gold, diamond, netherite."
		"&eHow:&r surround your backpack with iron ingots (check JEI). It keeps everything inside."
		"&eTip:&r stack upgrades multiply how many items fit in each slot."
	]
	quest.087BBFFCDB2D5BBE.title: "Feeding Upgrade"
	quest.087BBFFCDB2D5BBE.quest_subtitle: "Optional: never stop to eat again"
	quest.087BBFFCDB2D5BBE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r eats food from the backpack automatically when you're hungry."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Farmer's Delight meals restore a lot per bite."
		"&eTip:&r set a filter so it doesn't eat your golden apples."
	]
	quest.667CA6C7D1391223.title: "Netherite Backpack"
	quest.667CA6C7D1391223.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the biggest backpack"
	quest.667CA6C7D1391223.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the top tier: the most inventory slots and upgrade space."
		"&eHow:&r ring the backpack with gold, then diamonds, then smith in a netherite ingot with a netherite upgrade template."
		"&eTip:&r a netherite backpack has room for several stack upgrades at once."
	]
	quest.5B094C907C8047AF.title: "Waystones"
	quest.5B094C907C8047AF.quest_subtitle: "Teleport between your places"
	quest.5B094C907C8047AF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r waystones are teleport points. Activate one by right-clicking it, then warp between any you've activated."
		"&eHow:&r found in villages, or craft one (check JEI). Place them at your base, mines and portals."
		"&eTip:&r warping costs a little XP depending on distance; check the config if it seems steep."
	]
	quest.491A989F2FB877C8.title: "Warp Scrolls"
	quest.491A989F2FB877C8.quest_subtitle: "Optional: one-use trips to any waystone"
	quest.491A989F2FB877C8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a single-use warp to any activated waystone, handy before you can afford a Warp Stone."
		"&eHow:&r paper, an ender pearl, gold nuggets and an ink sac (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r keep one in your backpack for emergencies."
	]
	quest.17EB435344732ED5.title: "Maps"
	quest.17EB435344732ED5.quest_subtitle: "JourneyMap and FTB Chunks"
	quest.17EB435344732ED5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r JourneyMap draws a minimap and a full world map as you explore, with waypoints."
		"&eHow:&r press &eJ&r for the full JourneyMap. FTB Chunks has its own map for claims (check Controls for its key). Click the checkmark when you've tried them."
		"&eTip:&r drop a waypoint at every rich ore deposit you find. Deposits are rare, so note the depth too."
	]
	quest.697F3B912ADA9643.title: "Inventory Tricks"
	quest.697F3B912ADA9643.quest_subtitle: "Sorting, dragging and a trash slot"
	quest.697F3B912ADA9643.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r small mods that save hours: Mouse Tweaks (drag and scroll to move stacks), Inventory Tweaks (sorting) and TrashSlot (a trash can in your inventory)."
		"&eHow:&r try a scroll-wheel drag over stacks, the sort button, and the trash slot by your hotbar. Click the checkmark when done."
		"&eTip:&r Polymorph shows a button when two recipes share a grid; click it to pick the one you want."
	]
	quest.1F2CF66554D65C93.title: "Feral Flare Lantern"
	quest.1F2CF66554D65C93.quest_subtitle: "Optional: light a whole cave at once"
	quest.1F2CF66554D65C93.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the lantern places invisible light sources in the dark spots around it, so a cave or a big hall lights up without a single torch."
		"&eHow:&r gold ingots, glass and glowstone dust (check JEI). Place it in the middle of the room."
		"&eTip:&r great for a clean-looking factory floor. It still lets mobs spawn in spots it can't reach."
	]
	quest.5B9CAB5D9BAADF57.title: "Grave Tricks"
	quest.5B9CAB5D9BAADF57.quest_subtitle: "Optional: more from Corail Tombstone"
	quest.5B9CAB5D9BAADF57.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Corail Tombstone does more than store your items: it adds scrolls, tablets and the Ankh of Prayer, plus a book that makes items soulbound."
		"&eHow:&r search 'tombstone' in JEI to browse them. Click the checkmark when you've had a look."
		"&eTip:&r by default only you can open your grave, so a death on a server doesn't mean losing your gear to someone else."
	]
	quest.7A2E8D54084A7224.title: "Loot for Everyone"
	quest.7A2E8D54084A7224.quest_subtitle: "Optional: every player gets their own chest loot"
	quest.7A2E8D54084A7224.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r with Lootr, structure chests (dungeons, temples, villages, mineshafts) hold separate loot for each player."
		"&eHow:&r open any generated chest. You get your own roll; your friends still get theirs. Click the checkmark when you've seen one."
		"&eTip:&r on a server, nobody has to race to a dungeon first."
	]
	quest.014F5E0E68AA6574.title: "Stack Upgrade"
	quest.014F5E0E68AA6574.quest_subtitle: "Optional: more items per slot"
	quest.014F5E0E68AA6574.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a stack upgrade multiplies how many items each backpack slot holds. Higher tiers multiply more."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI; each tier is built from the one before it."
		"&eTip:&r stack upgrades make a backpack the best place to carry dust and ingots between machines."
	]
	quest.74B98B27BE564EAD.title: "Tool Swapper"
	quest.74B98B27BE564EAD.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the right tool, automatically"
	quest.74B98B27BE564EAD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r swaps the tool in your hand for the best one in your backpack when you start mining a block or hitting a mob."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI, then put it in an upgrade slot and fill the backpack with tools."
		"&eTip:&r pairs well with a paxel; it switches to shears or a sword only when needed."
	]
	quest.1572A9CFC13F6605.title: "Refill Upgrade"
	quest.1572A9CFC13F6605.quest_subtitle: "Optional: never run out of torches"
	quest.1572A9CFC13F6605.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r keeps chosen hotbar items topped up from the backpack: torches, blocks, food."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Set the items to refill in the upgrade's tab."
		"&eTip:&r refill building blocks while bridging and you'll never stop to open your inventory."
	]
	quest.32CFD45D94EE955E.title: "Pocket Anvil"
	quest.32CFD45D94EE955E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: repair and disenchant anywhere"
	quest.32CFD45D94EE955E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r pocket versions of the anvil and grindstone, opened with right-click."
		"&eHow:&r each one is its block plus a stick (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the pocket anvil wears down like a placed one, so carry a spare for long trips."
	]
	quest.295E46752750C4C1.title: "FTB Ultimine"
	quest.295E46752750C4C1.quest_subtitle: "Break a whole vein in one swing"
	quest.295E46752750C4C1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Ultimine breaks every connected matching block at once: a full ore vein, a tree, a strip of stone."
		"&eHow:&r hold the Ultimine key (default &e`&r, the key left of 1) and break a block. Arrow keys up and down change the shape. Click the checkmark when you've tried it."
		"&eTip:&r it can cost extra hunger, so eat first. Shapes include tunnels and flat planes for clearing space."
	]
	quest.24582FFEF0C9CA48.title: "Form a Team"
	quest.24582FFEF0C9CA48.quest_subtitle: "Share quests, claims and loot"
	quest.24582FFEF0C9CA48.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r FTB Teams groups players into a party. Teammates share quest progress and claimed chunks."
		"&eHow:&r open the Teams screen from the button on your inventory screen (or use /ftbteams) and create a party, then invite friends. Click the checkmark when done."
		"&eTip:&r playing alone? A solo party still lets you set chunk permissions for visitors."
	]
	quest.0A6808C7A052CA16.title: "Homes and /back"
	quest.0A6808C7A052CA16.quest_subtitle: "FTB Essentials teleport commands"
	quest.0A6808C7A052CA16.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r FTB Essentials adds /sethome and /home (one home by default), /back to return to where you died or last teleported, /spawn, and /tpa to ask to teleport to a friend."
		"&eHow:&r stand at your base and type /sethome, then try /home from somewhere else. Click the checkmark when done."
		"&eTip:&r each command has a short cooldown. /back after a death walks you straight to your grave."
	]
	quest.3419EC047902045A.title: "Just Zoom"
	quest.3419EC047902045A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a spyglass without the spyglass"
	quest.3419EC047902045A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Just Zoom lets you zoom in on the distance with a key, no item needed."
		"&eHow:&r find its key under Options → Controls, and hold it to zoom (its options are in the Mods menu). Click the checkmark when you've tried it."
		"&eTip:&r handy for spotting structures, meteorites and villages from a hilltop."
	]
	quest.213AD19CC7D30A37.title: "Ping Wheel"
	quest.213AD19CC7D30A37.quest_subtitle: "Optional: point things out to friends"
	quest.213AD19CC7D30A37.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Ping Wheel puts a marker on the spot you look at, visible to the other players nearby."
		"&eHow:&r find its keys under Options → Controls. Look at something and ping it. Click the checkmark when done."
		"&eTip:&r ping an ore deposit or a dangerous mob instead of typing coordinates."
	]
	quest.1E27CF7DD38A14C8.title: "Chat Heads"
	quest.1E27CF7DD38A14C8.quest_subtitle: "Optional: see who's talking"
	quest.1E27CF7DD38A14C8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Chat Heads shows each player's face next to their messages in chat."
		"&eHow:&r nothing to set up; it works as soon as someone talks. Click the checkmark when you've seen it."
		"&eTip:&r its options are in the Mods menu if you want to change how heads are shown."
	]
	quest.69F41022F3C27254.title: "Trade Cycling"
	quest.69F41022F3C27254.quest_subtitle: "Reroll a villager's offers"
	quest.69F41022F3C27254.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Trade Cycling adds a button to the villager trade screen that rerolls the offers of a villager nobody has traded with yet."
		"&eHow:&r give a villager a job block, open its trades and press the cycle button until the offer you want appears. Earn 16 emeralds by trading."
		"&eTip:&r once you trade, the offers lock. Cycle a librarian until it sells the enchanted book you need."
	]
	quest.370448FDEA00C30C.title: "Merchant Prince"
	quest.370448FDEA00C30C.quest_subtitle: "Secret: a demigod with a market stall"
	quest.370448FDEA00C30C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r four emerald blocks: 36 emeralds. The villagers have noticed you."
		"&eChemistry:&r emerald is beryl, Be₃Al₂Si₆O₁₈, coloured green by traces of chromium."
		"&eTip:&r every Warp Stone needs an emerald, so a good trading hall pays for your travel network."
	]
	quest.2570EB0A8AF93C47.title: "Tool Belt"
	quest.2570EB0A8AF93C47.quest_subtitle: "Optional: tools on a quick wheel"
	quest.2570EB0A8AF93C47.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Tool Belt holds tools outside your hotbar and opens as a radial menu so you can swap fast."
		"&eHow:&r leather and string (check JEI). Keep it in your inventory; find its key under Options → Controls."
		"&eTip:&r put the wrench, the config card and your paxel on the belt."
	]
	quest.7DAD39B76BA322EE.title: "Belt Pouches"
	quest.7DAD39B76BA322EE.quest_subtitle: "Optional: more slots on the belt"
	quest.7DAD39B76BA322EE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each pouch adds a slot to your tool belt."
		"&eHow:&r craft pouches, then craft them together with the belt (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a full belt keeps your hotbar free for blocks and food."
	]
	quest.7966EBF899C9AB72.title: "A Waystone Network"
	quest.7966EBF899C9AB72.quest_subtitle: "Optional: four more waystones"
	quest.7966EBF899C9AB72.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one waystone is a landmark; four make a network. Base, mine, Nether portal and a far-off biome."
		"&eHow:&r any four waystones of any style (check JEI for the variants), or bring back ones found in villages."
		"&eTip:&r name each one clearly ('Bauxite Mine -40') so the list stays readable."
	]
	quest.2367545F51E52EA0.title: "Warp Stone"
	quest.2367545F51E52EA0.quest_subtitle: "Optional: warp from anywhere"
	quest.2367545F51E52EA0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a reusable item that opens the waystone menu wherever you stand. It recharges after each use."
		"&eHow:&r amethyst shards, ender pearls and an emerald (check JEI). It's also in the Demigod Token shop."
		"&eTip:&r with a Warp Stone, warp scrolls become backup only."
	]
	quest.4C714AF8B234F7FB.title: "Waypoints"
	quest.4C714AF8B234F7FB.quest_subtitle: "Optional: never lose a deposit again"
	quest.4C714AF8B234F7FB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r JourneyMap waypoints mark places on the minimap and in the world, with distance shown on screen."
		"&eHow:&r open the full map (&eJ&r) and right-click a spot to add a waypoint, or use JourneyMap's waypoint key (see Controls). Click the checkmark when you've made one."
		"&eTip:&r JourneyMap makes a death waypoint for you; share waypoints with teammates in chat."
	]
	quest.3DA42EF9B1B6EE05.title: "Utilitarian Shortcuts"
	quest.3DA42EF9B1B6EE05.quest_subtitle: "Logs straight to sticks, chests and ladders"
	quest.3DA42EF9B1B6EE05.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Utilitarian mod adds bulk recipes that skip the planks step (two logs in a column make 16 sticks), plus small handy blocks: tiny coal, the Trowel, the Angel Block, Snad and more. This row is its catalogue."
		"&eHow:&r press U on any log in JEI to see every log shortcut. Click the checkmark when you've had a look."
		"&eTip:&r the bulk recipes give the same items as the vanilla ones, just with fewer clicks and no waste."
	]
	quest.16303011EEFFC500.title: "Chests and Ladders"
	quest.16303011EEFFC500.quest_subtitle: "Optional: eight logs, four chests"
	quest.16303011EEFFC500.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r logs in a chest ring make 4 chests at once. Seven logs in a ladder shape make 24 ladders."
		"&eHow:&r the same shapes as the plank recipes, but with logs (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r three logs in a V make 12 bowls, and logs between iron make a hopper without a chest."
	]
	quest.1B37259868EBFB82.title: "Slabs and Stairs"
	quest.1B37259868EBFB82.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a row of logs, a stack of slabs"
	quest.1B37259868EBFB82.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r three logs in a row make 24 slabs; six logs in a stair shape make 16 stairs."
		"&eHow:&r use logs of one wood type in the usual slab or stair shape (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r two slabs placed diagonally in the grid turn back into a plank, so leftover slabs are never wasted."
	]
	quest.4A660108C8D617E5.title: "Doors and Trapdoors"
	quest.4A660108C8D617E5.quest_subtitle: "Optional: six logs, a dozen doors"
	quest.4A660108C8D617E5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r six logs in a door shape make 12 doors; six logs in a trapdoor shape make 12 trapdoors."
		"&eHow:&r one wood type per craft (check JEI). Two logs side by side also make 4 pressure plates."
		"&eTip:&r doors placed side by side open together, so a double door needs only one click."
	]
	quest.49F02D49AA5F5138.title: "Re-Dyeing"
	quest.49F02D49AA5F5138.quest_subtitle: "Optional: wrong colour? Dye it again"
	quest.49F02D49AA5F5138.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Utilitarian lets you re-dye concrete, concrete powder, terracotta, stained glass, glass panes and candles that already have a colour."
		"&eChemistry:&r real pigments are chemicals too: concrete's colours come from metal oxides, like iron oxide (Fe₂O₃) for red and brown."
		"&eHow:&r eight coloured blocks around one dye re-colours all eight, or one block plus one dye does a single block (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r it also mixes blue and yellow dye into green, so cactus isn't the only green."
	]
	quest.413856DB1BFD433B.title: "Tiny Coal"
	quest.413856DB1BFD433B.quest_subtitle: "One coal split eight ways"
	quest.413856DB1BFD433B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one coal or charcoal makes 8 tiny pieces. Each burns for 10 seconds, so you don't waste a whole coal on one item."
		"&eChemistry:&r charcoal is wood heated without air (pyrolysis): water and volatile compounds are driven off, leaving mostly carbon."
		"&eHow:&r put one coal or charcoal in the crafting grid. Eight tiny pieces craft back into one."
		"&eTip:&r this pack's furnaces cook faster than vanilla, so one tiny coal covers more than one item."
	]
	quest.0305F783E15AF8E3.title: "The Trowel"
	quest.0305F783E15AF8E3.quest_subtitle: "Places random blocks from your hotbar"
	quest.0305F783E15AF8E3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Trowel places a random block from your hotbar each time you use it. Great for natural-looking walls and paths."
		"&eHow:&r two iron ingots and a stick (check JEI). Sneak-use it to switch between hotbar only and your whole inventory."
		"&eTip:&r fill the hotbar with stone, cobblestone, andesite and tuff, and a plain wall looks weathered in seconds."
	]
	quest.5EA632BBE18FF255.title: "Angel Block"
	quest.5EA632BBE18FF255.quest_subtitle: "A block you can place in mid-air"
	quest.5EA632BBE18FF255.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Angel Block can be placed in empty air, with nothing next to it. It's the start of any sky bridge or floating build."
		"&eHow:&r two feathers, two gold ingots and obsidian (check JEI). Use it while looking at empty air."
		"&eTip:&r it's a building block, not flight. Flying in this pack is a chemistry milestone (see the Nether chapter)."
	]
	quest.0E218EF0FD4FB53C.title: "Snad"
	quest.0E218EF0FD4FB53C.quest_subtitle: "Sand that makes plants grow taller"
	quest.0E218EF0FD4FB53C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r cactus, sugar cane, kelp and bamboo grow taller and faster on Snad. Soul Snad does the same for nether wart."
		"&eChemistry:&r sand is mostly quartz grains, SiO₂, the same compound as the Nether quartz and certus you'll meet later."
		"&eHow:&r two sand make one Snad (red sand makes Red Snad, soul sand makes Soul Snad)."
		"&eTip:&r a column of sugar cane on Snad is the fastest paper source for Sophisticated upgrades and Iron Furnace augments."
	]
	quest.0E3B330A8C3FACC9.title: "Block Magnet"
	quest.0E3B330A8C3FACC9.quest_subtitle: "Optional: powered magnet that lifts iron blocks"
	quest.0E3B330A8C3FACC9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r with a redstone signal, the Block Magnet pulls iron blocks, steel blocks and anvils below it up towards it."
		"&eChemistry:&r iron is ferromagnetic: its atoms' tiny magnetic moments line up in domains. The recipe is an electromagnet, an iron core with copper on each side."
		"&eHow:&r copper ingot, iron block, copper ingot in a row. Place it, put an iron block somewhere below, and power the magnet."
		"&eTip:&r a magnet and a lever make a simple lift for iron blocks: power it to pull them up, cut the power to let them fall."
	]
	quest.353EE527E64311F7.title: "Fluid Hopper"
	quest.353EE527E64311F7.quest_subtitle: "A hopper for liquids"
	quest.353EE527E64311F7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Fluid Hopper moves fluids the way a hopper moves items: it collects fluid from above and passes it on, the way a hopper does with items (check its JEI page)."
		"&eHow:&r iron ingots around a bucket, with white dye on top (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r under an infinite water source it fills a tank for your first steam boiler without any pump."
	]
	quest.351E30D6FCEA7716.title: "Well Behaved Dropper"
	quest.351E30D6FCEA7716.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a dropper that doesn't spray"
	quest.351E30D6FCEA7716.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a dropper that drops items neatly in front of itself instead of flinging them in random directions."
		"&eHow:&r a dropper with a gold nugget on each side (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r drop items onto a pressure plate or into water streams and they land exactly where you planned."
	]
	quest.113DE402B609A554.title: "Redstone Clock"
	quest.113DE402B609A554.quest_subtitle: "A pulse generator in one block"
	quest.113DE402B609A554.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Redstone Clock pulses a redstone signal on its own, with no repeater loop."
		"&eHow:&r chiseled stone bricks with redstone on four sides (check JEI). Right-click it with an empty hand to change the speed; sneak to change it faster."
		"&eTip:&r a slow clock on a dispenser or a Well Behaved Dropper makes a simple timed feeder."
	]
	quest.4311BF3C2BF76AB0.title: "TPS Meter"
	quest.4311BF3C2BF76AB0.quest_subtitle: "Optional: how hard is the server working?"
	quest.4311BF3C2BF76AB0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the TPS Meter gives a redstone signal based on the dimension's ticks per second. A healthy server runs at 20."
		"&eHow:&r four comparators around obsidian (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r wire it to a lamp in your factory: if it dims, something you built is lagging the server."
	]
	quest.17EAFFEB5D84D60A.title: "Sound Muffler"
	quest.17EAFFEB5D84D60A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: silence a noisy machine room"
	quest.17EAFFEB5D84D60A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Sound Muffler mutes sounds in a radius around it. Your crushers, pumps and boilers go quiet."
		"&eChemistry:&r real soundproofing works the same way: soft, porous fibres like wool turn sound energy into a tiny amount of heat."
		"&eHow:&r any wool plus a note block, shapeless."
		"&eTip:&r one in the middle of a machine row is usually enough. Its tooltip shows the radius."
	]
	quest.2CFCE0972D469BBF.title: "Trader Carpet"
	quest.2CFCE0972D469BBF.quest_subtitle: "Wandering traders land here, not on you"
	quest.2CFCE0972D469BBF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a wandering trader arriving nearby appears on a Trader Carpet instead of right in your face."
		"&eHow:&r any carpet plus a small flower, shapeless. Each colour has its own carpet."
		"&eTip:&r put it in a little market stall by your base. JEI also shows a trapped version, if you're feeling unkind."
	]
	quest.73682D8FDFE7FA97.title: "No Soliciting"
	quest.73682D8FDFE7FA97.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a banner that keeps traders away"
	quest.73682D8FDFE7FA97.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the No Soliciting Banner stops wandering traders from spawning in the chunks around it."
		"&eHow:&r wool, a lead and a stick, in a banner shape (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r use either the carpet or the banner: carpet if you like the trader's goods, banner if you don't."
	]
	quest.1343276077F459D5.title: "Outpost Claim"
	quest.1343276077F459D5.quest_subtitle: "Optional: stop pillagers returning to an outpost"
	quest.1343276077F459D5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r place the Raider Outpost Claim Block inside a pillager outpost and raiders stop coming back to it."
		"&eHow:&r the recipe uses an ominous (illager) banner, which a pillager captain drops (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r claim the outpost before building there; it makes a fine tower base."
	]
	quest.0B8BA71400FB1E48.title: "Un-Name Tag"
	quest.0B8BA71400FB1E48.quest_subtitle: "Optional: undo a name tag"
	quest.0B8BA71400FB1E48.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Un-Name Tag removes a mob's custom name."
		"&eHow:&r a name tag plus white dye, shapeless. Use it on the named mob."
		"&eTip:&r useful when a pet name typo has been bothering you for weeks."
	]
	quest.5B9605EFADDFC54D.title: "Slime in a Bucket"
	quest.5B9605EFADDFC54D.quest_subtitle: "Secret: it gets excited near its friends"
	quest.5B9605EFADDFC54D.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember finding hidden things by feel. The slime remembers too.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r you scooped a small slime into a bucket. It gets visibly excited when you carry it into a slime chunk."
		"&eHow:&r use an empty bucket on a small slime. Place it again by using the bucket on the ground."
		"&eTip:&r slime chunks spawn slimes underground at any light level, which makes them the best spot for a slime farm."
	]
	quest.3698C36E49E28F11.title: "The Enchanting Table"
	quest.3698C36E49E28F11.quest_subtitle: "Optional: books, obsidian and a diamond or two"
	quest.3698C36E49E28F11.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the enchanting table, with the 15 bookshelves it needs for level 30 enchantments. Apotheosis makes it much deeper (Magic group)."
		"&eChemistry:&r paper is pressed cellulose fibre; old books yellow because acids left in the paper slowly break those chains (and lignin oxidises)."
		"&eHow:&r table: a book, 2 diamonds and 4 obsidian. Bookshelf: 6 planks and 3 books. Book: 3 paper and a leather."
		"&eTip:&r leave one block of air between the table and the shelves, or they don't count."
	]
	quest.28ED4E6CDA9DEBA2.title: "Anvil"
	quest.28ED4E6CDA9DEBA2.quest_subtitle: "Optional: repair, rename, combine"
	quest.28ED4E6CDA9DEBA2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the anvil joins enchanted books to tools, repairs gear with its own material, and renames items."
		"&eChemistry:&r a real anvil is a block of hardened steel on a softer body: the hard face doesn't dent, the soft body doesn't crack."
		"&eHow:&r 3 iron blocks and 4 iron ingots: 31 iron in all."
		"&eTip:&r every repair raises the 'too expensive' cost. Combine books first, then put them on the tool in one go."
	]
	quest.0507C4360C804E7C.title: "Map, Compass and Clock"
	quest.0507C4360C804E7C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the vanilla navigator's kit"
	quest.0507C4360C804E7C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a map draws the land as you walk; a compass points to world spawn (or a lodestone); a clock shows the time of day, even underground."
		"&eChemistry:&r a real compass needle is magnetised iron. The first ones (China, about 1,000 years ago) used lodestone, naturally magnetic magnetite, Fe₃O₄."
		"&eHow:&r map: paper around a compass. Compass: 4 iron around redstone. Clock: 4 gold around redstone."
		"&eTip:&r JourneyMap does the mapping for you; a framed map on the wall is still a nice trophy."
	]
	quest.44D2755744253F5A.title: "Redstone Basics"
	quest.44D2755744253F5A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: switches, inverters and delays"
	quest.44D2755744253F5A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the three parts of most redstone builds: a lever (a switch), a redstone torch (a NOT gate) and a repeater (a delay and a booster)."
		"&eChemistry:&r redstone is fiction, but the logic is real: a torch is an inverter, exactly like a transistor wired as a NOT gate in every chip you own."
		"&eHow:&r lever: a stick on cobblestone. Torch: redstone on a stick. Repeater: 2 torches and redstone on stone."
		"&eTip:&r MI and Mekanism machines can be switched off with redstone; a lever by your machines saves power at night."
	]
	quest.50AAFA04623459C4.title: "Daylight Detector"
	quest.50AAFA04623459C4.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a switch that knows the time"
	quest.50AAFA04623459C4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r it outputs a signal that follows the sun. Right-click it to invert, so it fires at night instead."
		"&eChemistry:&r a real light sensor is a photodiode: light knocks electrons loose in a semiconductor and a current flows. Same physics as a solar panel, just smaller."
		"&eHow:&r glass, Nether quartz and wooden slabs (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r inverted, it switches on street lamps at dusk."
	]
	quest.6F16D17B0B750F06.title: "Conduit Power"
	quest.6F16D17B0B750F06.quest_subtitle: "Optional: breathe and see underwater"
	quest.6F16D17B0B750F06.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an activated conduit gives Conduit Power to players in the water nearby: no drowning, night vision underwater and faster mining. A bigger frame also attacks hostile mobs."
		"&eChemistry:&r nautilus shells are aragonite, a form of calcium carbonate (CaCO₃) with a different crystal packing from calcite. The pearly sheen is layers of it thinner than a wavelength of light."
		"&eHow:&r a heart of the sea (buried treasure) in 8 nautilus shells (drowned and fishing). Place it in water inside a frame of prismarine (check the wiki shape in JEI's info tab)."
		"&eTip:&r perfect for an underwater base, or for clearing an ocean monument."
	]
	quest.288987F76E925D85.title: "Harvester Pylon"
	quest.288987F76E925D85.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Harvester Pylon"
	quest.288987F76E925D85.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Harvester Pylon\" on the Pylons page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.71E9A9731852D77E.title: "Interdiction Pylon"
	quest.71E9A9731852D77E.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Interdiction Pylon"
	quest.71E9A9731852D77E.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Interdiction Pylon\" on the Pylons page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.6C163C76258D2DA7.title: "Guard Pylons"
	quest.6C163C76258D2DA7.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Protection Pylon"
	quest.6C163C76258D2DA7.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Protection Pylon\" on the Pylons page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	chapter.34560F2FAB74139C.title: "Storage and Logistics"
	chapter.34560F2FAB74139C.chapter_subtitle: [
		"A god needs somewhere to keep things."
	]
	quest.4E2D8BFF1BFBD142.title: "Somewhere for Everything"
	quest.4E2D8BFF1BFBD142.quest_subtitle: "Any chest opens the storage chapter"
	quest.4E2D8BFF1BFBD142.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember vaults that held the stars. Today it's a box of planks, and that's fine.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r this page is every way the pack stores things: vanilla containers, Functional Storage drawers, Sophisticated chests and backpacks, and a few extras of our own."
		"&eHow:&r any chest counts: vanilla, Sophisticated, archwood, whatever you have."
		"&eTip:&r the god's archive (AE2) has its own page. Build a drawer wall first; it'll feed the archive later."
	]
	quest.053027477AF19DE6.title: "Note: Items With Data"
	quest.053027477AF19DE6.quest_subtitle: "Why your enchanted books clog a digital system"
	quest.053027477AF19DE6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r some items carry data: enchanted books, damaged tools, filled backpacks, named things. Digital storage (AE2) spends a whole item type on each variant, so a thousand odd books eat a cell's 63 types fast."
		"&eHow:&r keep data-heavy items in plain chests, drawers or a Sophisticated chest. Put only bulk, identical items (ores, dusts, ingots) in cells."
		"&eTip:&r a storage bus on a chest full of books gives AE2 a window into it without wasting cell types."
	]
	quest.38E6420FFDDB1A47.title: "Note: Sort As You Go"
	quest.38E6420FFDDB1A47.quest_subtitle: "A tidy base is a fast base"
	quest.38E6420FFDDB1A47.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a chest named 'stuff' is where ingredients go to be forgotten. Pick a home for each kind of thing early: one wall for ores and metals, one for chemicals, one for building blocks."
		"&eHow:&r drawers for bulk items, chests for odds and ends, a backpack with a void filter for junk."
		"&eTip:&r every mod on this page can feed a controller, and a controller is what AE2 will read later."
	]
	quest.3ED955DE76ED312A.title: "Vanilla Storage"
	quest.3ED955DE76ED312A.quest_subtitle: "The containers Minecraft already gives you"
	quest.3ED955DE76ED312A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r chests, barrels, trapped chests, ender chests, chest boats and minecarts. Simple, cheap, and still useful late game."
		"&eHow:&r a chest from 8 planks, or an archwood chest from Ars Nouveau's archwood."
		"&eTip:&r two chests side by side make a double chest; a barrel opens even with a block on top."
	]
	quest.3906982CF5CE98D2.title: "Trapped Chest"
	quest.3906982CF5CE98D2.quest_subtitle: "A chest that tells on whoever opens it"
	quest.3906982CF5CE98D2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a trapped chest gives a redstone signal while someone has it open."
		"&eHow:&r a chest and a tripwire hook (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a trapped chest next to a door makes a cheap 'is anyone in my lab?' alarm."
	]
	quest.704F5D259ABEEC0C.title: "Barrel"
	quest.704F5D259ABEEC0C.quest_subtitle: "A chest with no lid to block"
	quest.704F5D259ABEEC0C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a barrel holds as much as a chest and opens with any block on top, so you can stack them in a wall."
		"&eHow:&r planks and slabs (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a wall of barrels with item frames is a fine early sorting room."
	]
	quest.76220BE84C524994.title: "Ender Chest"
	quest.76220BE84C524994.quest_subtitle: "One private inventory, everywhere"
	quest.76220BE84C524994.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every Ender Chest you open shows the same 27 slots, and only you can see yours."
		"&eHow:&r 8 obsidian around an eye of ender."
		"&eTip:&r keep spare tools and a water bucket in it; any Ender Chest becomes an emergency kit."
	]
	quest.24D0C566AB0B92AB.title: "Chest Minecart"
	quest.24D0C566AB0B92AB.quest_subtitle: "Haul a chest by rail"
	quest.24D0C566AB0B92AB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a chest on wheels: a minecart that carries 27 stacks along rails. A hopper under the track at home empties it as it rolls by."
		"&eChemistry:&r steel wheels on steel rails have very low rolling resistance, which is why one locomotive can pull thousands of tonnes."
		"&eHow:&r a minecart (5 iron) plus a chest (check JEI). Powered rails keep it moving."
		"&eTip:&r a hopper minecart (also in JEI) loads itself from containers it passes under."
	]
	quest.56FFFA1315770D48.title: "Chest Boat"
	quest.56FFFA1315770D48.quest_subtitle: "Cargo by river"
	quest.56FFFA1315770D48.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a boat with a chest in it. Any wood works."
		"&eHow:&r a boat plus a chest, shapeless (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r rivers run a long way in this pack's biomes; a chest boat is the cheapest long-distance freight before rails."
	]
	quest.5ABF92EBA6B76EAC.title: "Hoppers"
	quest.5ABF92EBA6B76EAC.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the first item mover"
	quest.5ABF92EBA6B76EAC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hopper pulls items from the container above it and pushes them into the one it points at."
		"&eHow:&r 5 iron ingots around a chest (Utilitarian also has a log recipe; check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a redstone signal locks a hopper, which makes simple item gates."
	]
	quest.48F1CD9DC51F826D.title: "Functional Storage"
	quest.48F1CD9DC51F826D.quest_subtitle: "Drawers: one item each, thousands deep"
	quest.48F1CD9DC51F826D.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember shelves that went on forever. Drawers are the closest thing to them.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Functional Storage drawers hold a lot of a single item and show it on the front. They're the backbone of a bulk store: cobblestone, dusts, ingots, salts."
		"&eHow:&r every drawer starts with a chest in the middle of its recipe, so bring one. The first drawer is the next quest."
		"&eTip:&r a drawer wall behind a Storage Controller is one inventory for pipes, and later for AE2."
	]
	quest.34606B92A3A6F57F.title: "Your First Drawer"
	quest.34606B92A3A6F57F.quest_subtitle: "Any drawer of any wood"
	quest.34606B92A3A6F57F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a drawer of any wood with 1, 2 or 4 slots. Right-click to insert, left-click to take one, sneak-left-click for a stack."
		"&eHow:&r planks and a chest in the drawer shape (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r double-right-click with an item to pour in every matching stack from your inventory."
	]
	quest.0E8BBA3A8819F628.title: "Linking Tool"
	quest.0E8BBA3A8819F628.quest_subtitle: "Join far-away drawers to a controller"
	quest.0E8BBA3A8819F628.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Linking Tool adds drawers that aren't touching a Storage Controller to its network, and pairs Ender Drawers."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Right-click the controller to start, then right-click each drawer. Holding the tool shows what's linked."
		"&eTip:&r link a drawer at your mine entrance so ore pours straight into the wall at home."
	]
	quest.129185B0D2C7C75A.title: "Drawer Controller"
	quest.129185B0D2C7C75A.quest_subtitle: "One face for every drawer"
	quest.129185B0D2C7C75A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Storage Controller links nearby drawers into one inventory you (and pipes, hoppers and AE2 storage buses) can use."
		"&eHow:&r place it among your drawers (check JEI). Drawers touching it or linked with the Linking Tool join the network."
		"&eTip:&r one pipe into the controller is a sorting system: each item goes to the drawer that already holds it."
	]
	quest.565F00C582D234E8.title: "Controller Extension"
	quest.565F00C582D234E8.quest_subtitle: "A second door into your drawer wall"
	quest.565F00C582D234E8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an extension works like the controller itself: pipes and players reach the whole drawer network through it."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI, then link it with the Linking Tool."
		"&eTip:&r one by the smelters, one by the crafting bench."
	]
	quest.0B24E672E714DDCB.title: "Simple Compacting Drawer"
	quest.0B24E672E714DDCB.quest_subtitle: "Two forms of one thing"
	quest.0B24E672E714DDCB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r stores two forms of one item (ingot and block, say) as a single pool and hands out whichever you ask for."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Insert the item you want it to track."
		"&eTip:&r good for things with no nugget form, like coal and coal blocks."
	]
	quest.21D03D3F9703DD77.title: "Compacting Drawer"
	quest.21D03D3F9703DD77.quest_subtitle: "Nuggets, ingots and blocks as one stock"
	quest.21D03D3F9703DD77.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a compacting drawer stores nuggets, ingots and blocks of one metal as a single pool."
		"&eChemistry:&r a block holds the same metal atoms as 9 ingots; only the packing changes, so nothing is lost either way."
		"&eHow:&r craft it (check JEI), then insert the item you want to track."
		"&eTip:&r perfect for copper and tin next to your bronze setup."
	]
	quest.4C26E19560FB2C6D.title: "Framed Drawers"
	quest.4C26E19560FB2C6D.quest_subtitle: "Drawers in any block's clothes"
	quest.4C26E19560FB2C6D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r framed drawers and controllers take on the texture of blocks you give them, so a drawer wall can match your lab."
		"&eHow:&r craft the framed version (check JEI), then sneak-right-click it with the blocks you want for its frame and face."
		"&eTip:&r framed drawers work exactly like normal ones, upgrades included."
	]
	quest.1A95C74DB50FB498.title: "Configuration Tool"
	quest.1A95C74DB50FB498.quest_subtitle: "Lock, hide and tidy"
	quest.1A95C74DB50FB498.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Configuration Tool locks drawers to their item, toggles the count and item display, and more."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Sneak-use cycles its mode; the mode shows on the item."
		"&eTip:&r lock every drawer in a sorting wall, so an empty drawer still only accepts its own item."
	]
	quest.46990CC570367505.title: "Fluid Drawers"
	quest.46990CC570367505.quest_subtitle: "Drawers for liquids"
	quest.46990CC570367505.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fluid drawers store a fluid instead of items, and show it on the front."
		"&eChemistry:&r handy for small stocks of acids: one drawer of H₂SO₄, one of HCl, one of HNO₃. A real lab keeps acids in separate, labelled containers too."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the 1, 2 and 4 slot versions. Pipes and MI fluid pipes fill and drain them; storage upgrades work on them."
	]
	quest.6E40C57F90C4FE3B.title: "Ender Drawer"
	quest.6E40C57F90C4FE3B.quest_subtitle: "One drawer, many places"
	quest.6E40C57F90C4FE3B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every Ender Drawer with the same frequency shares one inventory, wherever it is."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Pair drawers with the Linking Tool."
		"&eTip:&r put one at your mine and one at your smelters to send ore home."
	]
	quest.5D2BB64F5D50681D.title: "Collector Upgrade"
	quest.5D2BB64F5D50681D.quest_subtitle: "A drawer that picks up drops"
	quest.5D2BB64F5D50681D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a drawer with a Collector Upgrade pulls in matching items dropped nearby."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Right-click the drawer to open its upgrade slots."
		"&eTip:&r under a cobblestone generator or a mob farm's drop point it replaces a hopper line."
	]
	quest.05B5C16981AE7543.title: "Redstone Upgrade"
	quest.05B5C16981AE7543.quest_subtitle: "A signal that reads the drawer"
	quest.05B5C16981AE7543.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Redstone Upgrade makes a drawer emit a signal based on how full it is (or full / empty, by mode)."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Put it in the drawer's utility slot and cycle its mode."
		"&eTip:&r wire it to a machine so a cobblestone drawer that's full switches the generator off."
	]
	quest.2F46BAEB729FA068.title: "Copper Upgrade"
	quest.2F46BAEB729FA068.quest_subtitle: "The first capacity step"
	quest.2F46BAEB729FA068.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r storage upgrades multiply how much a drawer holds. Copper is the first and cheapest."
		"&eChemistry:&r copper (8.96 g/cm³) is soft and malleable, which is why it was the first metal people worked."
		"&eHow:&r copper ingots and blocks, chests and a drawer (check JEI). Right-click the drawer to open its upgrade slots."
	]
	quest.092C912113F0682E.title: "Gold Upgrade"
	quest.092C912113F0682E.quest_subtitle: "More room again"
	quest.092C912113F0682E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the gold upgrade multiplies a drawer's capacity more than copper."
		"&eChemistry:&r gold is the most malleable metal there is: one gram beats into a square metre of leaf."
		"&eHow:&r builds on the copper upgrade (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.317575EF2934BE98.title: "Diamond Upgrade"
	quest.317575EF2934BE98.quest_subtitle: "A very deep drawer"
	quest.317575EF2934BE98.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the diamond upgrade is the big step: one drawer holds a serious stockpile."
		"&eHow:&r builds on the gold upgrade (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the Iron Downgrade does the reverse, limiting a drawer to a single stack per slot."
	]
	quest.3396BFBDB6C40BF6.title: "Netherite Upgrade"
	quest.3396BFBDB6C40BF6.quest_subtitle: "The biggest drawer there is"
	quest.3396BFBDB6C40BF6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the top drawer upgrade. One drawer holds an absurd amount of a single item."
		"&eHow:&r smithing table: netherite upgrade template + diamond upgrade + netherite ingot."
		"&eTip:&r save it for cobblestone, raw ore or dust, the things you have tens of thousands of."
	]
	quest.004B7E61E7A5F186.title: "Iron Downgrade"
	quest.004B7E61E7A5F186.quest_subtitle: "Hold less, on purpose"
	quest.004B7E61E7A5F186.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Iron Downgrade limits a drawer to one stack per slot."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI."
		"&eTip:&r useful for a drawer that feeds a machine: it keeps a small buffer instead of swallowing your whole stock."
	]
	quest.0E6E523DE8427EBF.title: "Void Upgrade"
	quest.0E6E523DE8427EBF.quest_subtitle: "Delete the overflow"
	quest.0E6E523DE8427EBF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a drawer with a Void Upgrade destroys whatever doesn't fit, so a full drawer never backs up a pipe."
		"&eChemistry:&r real matter can't vanish (mass is conserved in every chemical reaction). In Minecraft, it can."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI."
		"&eTip:&r a void-upgraded cobblestone drawer at the end of a quarry line keeps everything flowing."
	]
	quest.4D94683496892DE6.title: "Pusher Upgrade"
	quest.4D94683496892DE6.quest_subtitle: "A drawer that feeds a machine"
	quest.4D94683496892DE6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Pusher pushes the drawer's items into the block it faces. No pipes needed."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Put it in the drawer's utility slot and set its direction in the drawer's menu."
		"&eTip:&r a drawer of coal with a Pusher behind a row of furnaces keeps them fuelled."
	]
	quest.6A53B6D2F371F859.title: "Puller Upgrade"
	quest.6A53B6D2F371F859.quest_subtitle: "A drawer that empties a machine"
	quest.6A53B6D2F371F859.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Puller pulls items from the block it faces into the drawer."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Utility slot, set the direction in the drawer's menu."
		"&eTip:&r a drawer with a Puller behind a macerator collects all the dust without a single pipe."
	]
	quest.44D2496540C5F6FE.title: "Sophisticated Storage"
	quest.44D2496540C5F6FE.quest_subtitle: "Chests and barrels that grow with you"
	quest.44D2496540C5F6FE.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember vaults that answered to a word. These answer to upgrade cards, which is nearly as good.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Sophisticated Storage chests, barrels, limited barrels and shulker boxes take upgrade cards (stack, compacting, hopper, filters) and tier upgrades, just like your backpack."
		"&eHow:&r craft any wooden chest or barrel of the mod (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r barrels keep their contents when broken, so moving a full one is easy."
	]
	quest.2478497698299592.title: "Copper Tier"
	quest.2478497698299592.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the first small step up"
	quest.2478497698299592.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the copper tier sits between wood and iron: a few more slots for a little copper."
		"&eChemistry:&r copper tarnishes green: over years it forms a patina of basic copper carbonate, Cu₂CO₃(OH)₂, which then protects the metal underneath."
		"&eHow:&r a copper chest or barrel from JEI, or a basic-to-copper tier upgrade right-clicked on a placed wooden one."
	]
	quest.4C812FEC12C477A4.title: "Iron Tier"
	quest.4C812FEC12C477A4.quest_subtitle: "More slots without emptying anything"
	quest.4C812FEC12C477A4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the iron tier: more slots and more upgrade slots."
		"&eHow:&r craft an iron chest or barrel, or use a tier upgrade (basic → iron skips copper) on the placed container: nothing inside moves."
		"&eTip:&r the Decoration Table re-skins chests and barrels with any wood or block, so your storage room can match your base."
	]
	quest.5CEDE0D09BC9E44B.title: "Gold Tier"
	quest.5CEDE0D09BC9E44B.quest_subtitle: "Climb the ladder one tier at a time"
	quest.5CEDE0D09BC9E44B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the gold tier, with more slots and upgrade slots again."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI, or an iron-to-gold tier upgrade on the placed chest or barrel."
		"&eTip:&r upgrade the barrel your ore line feeds first; it fills fastest."
	]
	quest.290DCB55D825C794.title: "Diamond Tier"
	quest.290DCB55D825C794.quest_subtitle: "The tier before netherite"
	quest.290DCB55D825C794.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the diamond tier. Enough upgrade slots for stack upgrades, a hopper and a filter at once."
		"&eChemistry:&r diamond is pure carbon, the same element as the coal in your furnace, arranged in a lattice where every atom bonds to four others."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI, or a gold-to-diamond tier upgrade on the placed container."
	]
	quest.767BDE1049071494.title: "Netherite Tier"
	quest.767BDE1049071494.quest_subtitle: "The top tier"
	quest.767BDE1049071494.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the netherite tier has the most slots and upgrade slots of any Sophisticated container."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI, or a diamond-to-netherite tier upgrade on a placed diamond chest or barrel."
		"&eTip:&r a netherite barrel full of stack upgrades holds a staggering amount."
	]
	quest.73531F8549FB5D54.title: "Upgrade Base"
	quest.73531F8549FB5D54.quest_subtitle: "The blank every upgrade starts from"
	quest.73531F8549FB5D54.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every Sophisticated Storage upgrade card starts from an upgrade base."
		"&eHow:&r planks and iron ingots in a checker pattern. The backpack mod has its own base; JEI shows both."
		"&eTip:&r make a few at a time; you'll want stack, hopper and compacting upgrades soon."
	]
	quest.4723957D49EEF36E.title: "Storage Controller"
	quest.4723957D49EEF36E.quest_subtitle: "Many containers, one inventory"
	quest.4723957D49EEF36E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Controller joins touching Sophisticated containers into one inventory. Right-click it with an item and it goes to the container that already holds that item."
		"&eHow:&r place it next to your chests and barrels (check JEI). Pipes into the controller reach every connected container."
		"&eTip:&r one pipe into the controller is a sorting system; a storage bus on it later gives AE2 the whole room."
	]
	quest.5DD71B12870D590E.title: "Storage Tool"
	quest.5DD71B12870D590E.quest_subtitle: "Link and lock from a distance"
	quest.5DD71B12870D590E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Storage Tool links containers to a controller without touching it and toggles settings like locks and displays."
		"&eHow:&r an ender pearl, iron, sticks and a redstone torch (check JEI). Its tooltip lists each mode."
		"&eTip:&r locked slots keep their item type even when empty, so a sorting system never fills them with junk."
	]
	quest.2073E19E1FCE7014.title: "Storage Link"
	quest.2073E19E1FCE7014.quest_subtitle: "Reach containers the controller can't touch"
	quest.2073E19E1FCE7014.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Storage Link joins containers that aren't touching the controller's group, within the controller's range."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Place it against the far container (or group) and link it with the Storage Tool."
		"&eTip:&r a link under the floor joins a second storage room without a wall of cables."
	]
	quest.69DDDBCD4E866CB4.title: "Sophisticated Chest"
	quest.69DDDBCD4E866CB4.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the same upgrades, in chest form"
	quest.69DDDBCD4E866CB4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Sophisticated chests take the same tier upgrades and upgrade cards as the barrels, and show their contents in a double-chest layout."
		"&eHow:&r a wooden chest version (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r chests connect to the controller the same way barrels do."
	]
	quest.437BDBF9EB5E0A3A.title: "Limited Barrels"
	quest.437BDBF9EB5E0A3A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: drawer-style barrels with a few huge slots"
	quest.437BDBF9EB5E0A3A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r limited barrels have one to four big slots and show their items on the front, like drawers, but take Sophisticated upgrades."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for each size. They use the same tier upgrades as normal barrels."
		"&eTip:&r a four-slot limited barrel per metal (ore, dust, ingot, block) makes a tidy wall."
	]
	quest.3E872691D5DE867F.title: "Sophisticated Shulker Box"
	quest.3E872691D5DE867F.quest_subtitle: "Optional: upgradeable storage you can carry"
	quest.3E872691D5DE867F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a shulker box that takes tier upgrades and upgrade cards, and keeps everything inside when you pick it up."
		"&eHow:&r a chest, two shulker shells and a lever (check JEI). Shulkers live in End cities."
		"&eTip:&r a shulker box with a compacting upgrade is a portable ore bank for long mining trips."
	]
	quest.4EA79F2D59AD8BFF.title: "Tier Upgrade Kits"
	quest.4EA79F2D59AD8BFF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: upgrade in place instead of crafting anew"
	quest.4EA79F2D59AD8BFF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tier upgrades turn a placed chest or barrel into the next tier without moving a thing. This one is the last step, diamond to netherite."
		"&eHow:&r a lever and a netherite ingot, shapeless (check JEI for the other steps)."
		"&eTip:&r every item and upgrade card inside stays where it was."
	]
	quest.14C4F705E5EB614F.title: "Stack Upgrades"
	quest.14C4F705E5EB614F.quest_subtitle: "Optional: more items in every slot"
	quest.14C4F705E5EB614F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r stack upgrades multiply how many items fit in each slot of a chest or barrel. Higher tiers multiply more."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base and storage blocks (check JEI). Insert it in an upgrade slot."
		"&eTip:&r a barrel with a few stack upgrades holds a whole mine's worth of cobblestone or raw ore."
	]
	quest.45772E69CBC7F59A.title: "Compacting Upgrade"
	quest.45772E69CBC7F59A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: nuggets to ingots to blocks, automatically"
	quest.45772E69CBC7F59A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Compacting Upgrade squeezes 9 nuggets into an ingot and 9 ingots into a block as items arrive."
		"&eChemistry:&r a block holds the same metal atoms as 9 ingots; only the packing changes, so no mass is lost either way."
		"&eHow:&r craft it (check JEI) and put it in an upgrade slot. Add a filter so it only compacts what you choose."
	]
	quest.43161D5C917A2792.title: "Compression Upgrade"
	quest.43161D5C917A2792.quest_subtitle: "Optional: nuggets, ingots and blocks as one stock"
	quest.43161D5C917A2792.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Compression Upgrade links a few slots so nuggets, ingots and blocks of one material count as a single stock."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base, pistons, iron and redstone (check JEI). Choose which slots it uses in the upgrade tab."
		"&eTip:&r take out exactly the form you need: blocks for storage, ingots for crafting, nuggets for small recipes."
	]
	quest.60D0F5C1FAE2D0DD.title: "Hopper Upgrade"
	quest.60D0F5C1FAE2D0DD.quest_subtitle: "Optional: containers that pull and push themselves"
	quest.60D0F5C1FAE2D0DD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Hopper Upgrade pulls items from one side and pushes them out another, with filters."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base, a hopper, iron and redstone (check JEI). Set directions and filters in the container's upgrade tab."
		"&eTip:&r a barrel with a hopper upgrade under a machine's output collects everything without pipes."
	]
	quest.41BFE37C73B3E712.title: "Storage Input and Output"
	quest.41BFE37C73B3E712.quest_subtitle: "Optional: separate doors into your storage"
	quest.41BFE37C73B3E712.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Storage Input only accepts items into the controller's containers; Storage Output only lets them out. Pipes and hoppers use them like any inventory."
		"&eHow:&r a wooden storage block, gold, planks and a repeater (check JEI). Place them touching the controller's group."
		"&eTip:&r put an Input at the end of your ore line and an Output by your crafting area, so the two never mix."
	]
	quest.24A467FAA663A7EF.title: "Storage in Motion"
	quest.24A467FAA663A7EF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Sophisticated chests on rails and water"
	quest.24A467FAA663A7EF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Sophisticated Storage in Motion puts upgradeable chests and barrels on minecarts, boats and rafts, upgrades and all."
		"&eHow:&r combine a minecart with a Sophisticated chest or barrel (check JEI). Boats and rafts work the same way."
		"&eTip:&r a hopper upgrade on a storage minecart makes a simple ore train between your mine and base."
	]
	quest.30347A69744DE975.title: "A Backpack"
	quest.30347A69744DE975.quest_subtitle: "More pockets, upgradeable later"
	quest.30347A69744DE975.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember carrying whole worlds. For now, a leather bag will do.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r more inventory, and it can be upgraded later (pickup, magnet, feeding and more)."
		"&eHow:&r leather, string and a chest (check JEI for the shape). Wear it in the chest slot or keep it in your inventory."
		"&eTip:&r take it on your first mining trip. The upgrade base is also sold in the Demigod Token shop."
	]
	quest.44A83B065B0048B5.title: "Copper Backpack"
	quest.44A83B065B0048B5.quest_subtitle: "Optional: one small step before iron"
	quest.44A83B065B0048B5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the copper backpack sits between leather and iron: a few more slots and an extra upgrade slot."
		"&eHow:&r surround your backpack with copper ingots (check JEI). Everything inside stays put."
		"&eTip:&r copper is plentiful early, so this is the cheapest upgrade in the line."
	]
	quest.3E28F4295DA98B59.title: "Gold Backpack"
	quest.3E28F4295DA98B59.quest_subtitle: "More rows, more upgrade slots"
	quest.3E28F4295DA98B59.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the gold backpack adds inventory rows and upgrade slots over the iron one."
		"&eHow:&r surround an iron backpack with eight gold ingots. Everything inside stays put."
		"&eTip:&r spend the new upgrade slot on a stack upgrade; it multiplies every slot at once."
	]
	quest.38D0C0420E9CD61E.title: "Diamond Backpack"
	quest.38D0C0420E9CD61E.quest_subtitle: "Room for a whole lab's worth of reagents"
	quest.38D0C0420E9CD61E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the diamond backpack is the tier before netherite: even more rows and upgrade slots."
		"&eHow:&r surround a gold backpack with eight diamonds."
		"&eTip:&r netherite comes after it (the Netherite Backpack quest, on the Quality of Life page)."
	]
	quest.5615A7371D54955E.title: "Backpack Upgrade Base"
	quest.5615A7371D54955E.quest_subtitle: "The blank behind every backpack upgrade"
	quest.5615A7371D54955E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every backpack upgrade starts from this base. The upgrades below each add one thing the pack does by itself."
		"&eHow:&r leather, string and iron (check JEI). It's also in the Demigod Token shop."
		"&eTip:&r upgrades go in the slots on the left of the backpack screen; sneak-right-click the slot to open an upgrade's settings."
	]
	quest.1EF5A71CFAD4061B.title: "Tank Upgrade"
	quest.1EF5A71CFAD4061B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: carry fluids in your backpack"
	quest.1EF5A71CFAD4061B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Tank Upgrade stores fluid inside the backpack. Fill and empty it with buckets or tanks from its upgrade tab."
		"&eChemistry:&r a real acid needs the right container: HF eats glass, so it's kept in PTFE; concentrated H₂SO₄ can sit in steel. A backpack tank isn't fussy."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base surrounded by glass (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a tank of water means you're never stuck in a lava cave without a way to cool it into obsidian."
	]
	quest.4BB6003995F45994.title: "Advanced Pickup"
	quest.4BB6003995F45994.quest_subtitle: "Optional: more filter slots, tag and mod filters"
	quest.4BB6003995F45994.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the advanced pickup upgrade has more filter slots and can filter by tag, mod or durability."
		"&eHow:&r the basic pickup upgrade with gold, diamonds and redstone (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a tag filter for 'c:raw_materials' picks up every raw ore in the pack with one entry."
	]
	quest.3AF418BDA378DFE2.title: "Advanced Magnet"
	quest.3AF418BDA378DFE2.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a wider pull and finer filters"
	quest.3AF418BDA378DFE2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the advanced magnet pulls drops from further away, with the advanced filter slots."
		"&eChemistry:&r a real magnet only pulls iron, nickel, cobalt and a few alloys. This one is less picky."
		"&eHow:&r the basic magnet upgrade with gold, diamonds and redstone (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.199FC6B41959C849.title: "Smelting Upgrade"
	quest.199FC6B41959C849.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a furnace in your backpack"
	quest.199FC6B41959C849.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Smelting Upgrade is a furnace in the backpack screen, burning fuel from the backpack."
		"&eChemistry:&r smelting iron ore is a reduction: carbon monoxide strips the oxygen off the ore, Fe₂O₃ + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO₂."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base and a furnace (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r smelt your raw ore on the walk home."
	]
	quest.1351E1675B744204.title: "Auto-Smelting Upgrade"
	quest.1351E1675B744204.quest_subtitle: "Optional: it smelts by itself"
	quest.1351E1675B744204.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Auto-Smelting Upgrade smelts matching items inside the backpack on its own, using fuel from the backpack."
		"&eHow:&r the smelting upgrade with a hopper, gold, redstone and a diamond (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r filter it to raw ores only, or it will smelt your logs into charcoal too."
	]
	quest.746F54C2A600C026.title: "Pump Upgrade"
	quest.746F54C2A600C026.quest_subtitle: "Optional: fill the tank from the world"
	quest.746F54C2A600C026.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Pump Upgrade fills and empties the backpack's tank from blocks in the world or from tanks you click on."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base with buckets, glass, a piston and a sticky piston (check JEI). It needs a Tank Upgrade to work with."
		"&eTip:&r set it to 'fill' on a water source and the tank is never empty."
	]
	quest.2059C2BD4C57C88F.title: "Advanced Pump"
	quest.2059C2BD4C57C88F.quest_subtitle: "Optional: faster, with filters"
	quest.2059C2BD4C57C88F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the advanced pump moves fluid faster and filters which fluids it touches."
		"&eHow:&r the pump upgrade with gold, diamonds and redstone (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.780DFC4D7AF87273.title: "Experience Pump"
	quest.780DFC4D7AF87273.quest_subtitle: "Optional: bank your levels"
	quest.780DFC4D7AF87273.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the XP Pump stores your experience as fluid in the backpack's tank and gives it back on demand."
		"&eHow:&r an advanced pump upgrade with ender eyes, bottles o' enchanting and redstone (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r bank your levels before a risky fight; a grave keeps items, not levels."
	]
	quest.143C1C0C468DEAB2.title: "Battery Upgrade"
	quest.143C1C0C468DEAB2.quest_subtitle: "Optional: FE in your backpack"
	quest.143C1C0C468DEAB2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r stores Forge Energy in the backpack, which other upgrades and charging tools can use."
		"&eChemistry:&r a battery stores energy as chemistry: two electrodes with different appetites for electrons, kept apart by an electrolyte."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base with gold ingots and redstone blocks (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r charge it at home, then top up your jetpack or Mining Gadget in the field."
	]
	quest.30AEB3BE1D760F10.title: "Deposit Upgrade"
	quest.30AEB3BE1D760F10.quest_subtitle: "Optional: empty into a chest in one click"
	quest.30AEB3BE1D760F10.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r with a Deposit Upgrade, sneak-right-clicking a container with the backpack puts matching items into it."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base, a chest, iron, redstone and a piston (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r deposit ores into your processing chest in one click when you get home."
	]
	quest.3CD64620E5534214.title: "Advanced Deposit"
	quest.3CD64620E5534214.quest_subtitle: "Optional: more filter slots"
	quest.3CD64620E5534214.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the advanced version with more filter slots and tag filters."
		"&eHow:&r the deposit upgrade with gold, diamonds and redstone (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.078048039CB21290.title: "Blasting Upgrade"
	quest.078048039CB21290.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a blast furnace in your pack"
	quest.078048039CB21290.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Blasting Upgrade smelts ores and metal at double speed, like a blast furnace, from the backpack screen."
		"&eChemistry:&r a blast furnace forces air through the fuel so it burns hotter: C + O₂ → CO₂, then CO₂ + C → 2CO, and the CO reduces the ore."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base with a blast furnace, iron and redstone (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r one furnace-type upgrade is enough: they share the backpack's fuel."
	]
	quest.5C440F910ECF2D56.title: "Auto-Blasting Upgrade"
	quest.5C440F910ECF2D56.quest_subtitle: "Optional: ores smelt themselves"
	quest.5C440F910ECF2D56.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the automatic version: it blasts matching items inside the backpack by itself."
		"&eHow:&r the blasting upgrade with a hopper, gold, redstone and a diamond (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.71BA808FEAC08882.title: "Stonecutter Upgrade"
	quest.71BA808FEAC08882.quest_subtitle: "Optional: cut stone without a block"
	quest.71BA808FEAC08882.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Stonecutter Upgrade adds a stonecutter to the backpack screen."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base with a stonecutter, iron and redstone (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r perfect for Create Deco, Rechiseled and laboratory blocks on a building trip."
	]
	quest.739A1631FE308482.title: "Filter Upgrade"
	quest.739A1631FE308482.quest_subtitle: "Optional: only what you want gets in or out"
	quest.739A1631FE308482.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Filter Upgrade decides what pipes and hoppers may put into or take out of the backpack."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base with string and redstone (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a backpack in a hopper line with a filter is a cheap sorter."
	]
	quest.7B7C0E8DB419BF4E.title: "Advanced Filter"
	quest.7B7C0E8DB419BF4E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: filter by tag or mod"
	quest.7B7C0E8DB419BF4E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r more filter slots, plus filters by tag, mod or durability."
		"&eHow:&r the filter upgrade with gold, diamonds and redstone (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.1981F6EE5DB4453C.title: "Smoking Upgrade"
	quest.1981F6EE5DB4453C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: cook food twice as fast"
	quest.1981F6EE5DB4453C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Smoking Upgrade is a smoker in the backpack screen: food only, at double speed."
		"&eChemistry:&r smoking preserves meat: phenols and other compounds in wood smoke kill microbes and slow the fats going rancid."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base with a smoker, iron and redstone (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.2B2C202ECD702F6E.title: "Auto-Smoking Upgrade"
	quest.2B2C202ECD702F6E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: dinner cooks itself"
	quest.2B2C202ECD702F6E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the automatic version: raw food in the backpack is smoked by itself."
		"&eHow:&r the smoking upgrade with a hopper, gold, redstone and a diamond (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.0D290B35BC958A75.title: "Mixtape"
	quest.0D290B35BC958A75.quest_subtitle: "Secret: music while you mine"
	quest.0D290B35BC958A75.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember a time when the spheres sang to you. A jukebox in a backpack will have to do.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Jukebox Upgrade plays music discs from inside your backpack, wherever you walk."
		"&eTip:&r it plays to everyone nearby. Choose your disc with care."
	]
	quest.4A5E552053BC2DD0.title: "Advanced Tool Swapper"
	quest.4A5E552053BC2DD0.quest_subtitle: "Optional: swap weapons too"
	quest.4A5E552053BC2DD0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the advanced tool swapper also swaps to the right weapon for the mob in front of you, with more filter slots."
		"&eHow:&r the tool swapper upgrade with gold, diamonds and redstone (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.08E300D23A89C5D9.title: "Stack Upgrade II"
	quest.08E300D23A89C5D9.quest_subtitle: "Optional: every slot holds more"
	quest.08E300D23A89C5D9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each stack tier multiplies how many items fit in every backpack slot. Tier 2 multiplies more than tier 1."
		"&eHow:&r the tier 1 upgrade with better materials (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a backpack full of stacked dust is the cheapest way to move a day's mining to your machines."
	]
	quest.52A9CCAA61BD8179.title: "Stack Upgrade III"
	quest.52A9CCAA61BD8179.quest_subtitle: "Optional: bigger again"
	quest.52A9CCAA61BD8179.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tier 3 of the stack upgrade."
		"&eHow:&r the tier 2 upgrade with diamonds (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.08525D5A6E69A69A.title: "Stack Upgrade IV"
	quest.08525D5A6E69A69A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the top stack tier"
	quest.08525D5A6E69A69A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tier 4, the biggest stack multiplier a backpack takes."
		"&eHow:&r the tier 3 upgrade with netherite (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r two of these in a netherite backpack and you can carry a quarry's output."
	]
	quest.50DE86ADFB0ED44D.title: "Crafting Upgrade"
	quest.50DE86ADFB0ED44D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a crafting grid in your backpack"
	quest.50DE86ADFB0ED44D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r adds a 3x3 crafting grid to the backpack screen that can use the backpack's own items."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base, a crafting table, iron and a chest (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r JEI's + button fills the backpack grid straight from the backpack."
	]
	quest.3EA17776398A680D.title: "Advanced Feeding"
	quest.3EA17776398A680D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: eats only when it's worth it"
	quest.3EA17776398A680D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the advanced feeding upgrade has more food slots and can be set to eat only when no hunger would be wasted."
		"&eHow:&r the feeding upgrade with gold, diamonds and redstone (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.5DDE2A62CC563B43.title: "Void Upgrade"
	quest.5DDE2A62CC563B43.quest_subtitle: "Optional: delete the junk as you pick it up"
	quest.5DDE2A62CC563B43.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Void Upgrade destroys chosen items as they enter the backpack: cobblestone, dirt, gravel, rotten flesh."
		"&eChemistry:&r real matter can't vanish (mass is conserved in every chemical reaction). In Minecraft, it can."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base, ender pearls, obsidian and redstone (check JEI). Set the filter carefully."
		"&eTip:&r keep a stack of cobblestone out of the filter. You'll want it for building and for the Matter Condenser later."
	]
	quest.12053E26676498FA.title: "Advanced Void"
	quest.12053E26676498FA.quest_subtitle: "Optional: void by tag, and only the overflow"
	quest.12053E26676498FA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r more filter slots, tag filters, and an 'overflow only' mode that keeps one stack and deletes the rest."
		"&eHow:&r the void upgrade with gold, diamonds and redstone (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.0A0D6B351BA1796A.title: "Inception"
	quest.0A0D6B351BA1796A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: backpacks within backpacks"
	quest.0A0D6B351BA1796A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r with the Inception Upgrade, backpacks stored inside your backpack keep using their own upgrades, and you can open them from the outer one."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base with ender eyes, diamonds and a Nether Star (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a small 'mining' backpack inside your main one keeps its magnet and void settings separate."
	]
	quest.1C8600E724F1113E.title: "Compacting Upgrade"
	quest.1C8600E724F1113E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: nuggets to ingots as you walk"
	quest.1C8600E724F1113E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Compacting Upgrade squeezes 9 of something into its block as you pick it up."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base with pistons, iron and redstone (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r compact redstone, lapis and coal while mining; whole blocks take a ninth of the space."
	]
	quest.336F79DDC88E987D.title: "Advanced Compacting"
	quest.336F79DDC88E987D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: more slots, uncrafting too"
	quest.336F79DDC88E987D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the advanced version compacts more item types at once and can uncraft blocks back into pieces."
		"&eHow:&r the compacting upgrade with gold, diamonds and redstone (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.0C5521026175E1FD.title: "Restock Upgrade"
	quest.0C5521026175E1FD.quest_subtitle: "Optional: refill from a chest in one click"
	quest.0C5521026175E1FD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Restock Upgrade tops the backpack up from a container you sneak-right-click: torches, food, whatever it already holds."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base, a chest, iron, redstone and a sticky piston (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r restock torches and food from your supply chest on the way out, every time."
	]
	quest.53CFA8761CE1BFCE.title: "Advanced Restock"
	quest.53CFA8761CE1BFCE.quest_subtitle: "Optional: more filter slots"
	quest.53CFA8761CE1BFCE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the advanced version with more filter slots and tag filters."
		"&eHow:&r the restock upgrade with gold, diamonds and redstone (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.5962C913253DCBED.title: "Everlasting"
	quest.5962C913253DCBED.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a backpack that can't be lost"
	quest.5962C913253DCBED.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r with the Everlasting Upgrade, a dropped backpack can't burn, explode or despawn."
		"&eHow:&r an upgrade base, nether stars and end crystals (check JEI). That means beating the Wither and visiting the End."
		"&eTip:&r worth it before reactor work or deep Nether trips, where a lost pack hurts most."
	]
	quest.7A148C70DC9D5A00.title: "Advanced Refill"
	quest.7A148C70DC9D5A00.quest_subtitle: "Optional: keep more hotbar slots topped up"
	quest.7A148C70DC9D5A00.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the advanced refill upgrade keeps more hotbar items topped up from the backpack, with a target slot for each."
		"&eHow:&r the refill upgrade with gold, diamonds and redstone (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.39A06D5C8360B8C7.title: "Fully Advanced"
	quest.39A06D5C8360B8C7.quest_subtitle: "Optional: four advanced upgrades in one pack"
	quest.39A06D5C8360B8C7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a collection: any four advanced upgrades (feeding, refill, restock, deposit, void, tool swapper, compacting, pump)."
		"&eHow:&r each is its basic upgrade plus gold, diamonds and redstone (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a diamond backpack has the slots for all of them at once."
	]
	quest.73F96D08F9DD5275.title: "An Early Network"
	quest.73F96D08F9DD5275.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Tom's Simple Storage, one searchable terminal"
	quest.73F96D08F9DD5275.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Tom's Simple Storage connects your chests into one searchable terminal. It's your network until AE2."
		"&eHow:&r place an Inventory Connector touching your chests (or link them with Inventory Cables), and a Storage Terminal on it."
		"&eTip:&r point it at a drawer controller and every drawer shows up in the terminal."
	]
	quest.36279DAC568E66FC.title: "Crafting Terminal"
	quest.36279DAC568E66FC.quest_subtitle: "Optional: craft straight from storage"
	quest.36279DAC568E66FC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a terminal with a crafting grid that pulls ingredients from the network. JEI's + button fills it for you."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade a Storage Terminal (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a Wireless Terminal (also in JEI) lets you use it from across the base."
	]
	quest.198E6DA2BCC8985F.title: "Inventory Cables"
	quest.198E6DA2BCC8985F.quest_subtitle: "Optional: reach chests across the room"
	quest.198E6DA2BCC8985F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r inventory cables carry the Inventory Connector's reach to chests that aren't touching it."
		"&eHow:&r run cables from the connector and put a Cable Connector on each chest or drawer (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r framed cables can wear any block's texture, so they hide in walls."
	]
	quest.74EA12F84EA1A34D.title: "Wireless Terminal"
	quest.74EA12F84EA1A34D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: your early network, anywhere"
	quest.74EA12F84EA1A34D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Advanced Wireless Terminal opens your Tom's network from a long way off."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI, then right-click it on a Storage Terminal to bind it."
		"&eTip:&r it's the cheapest remote storage access until AE2."
	]
	quest.2AA6E5D8AD92D260.title: "Pipez"
	quest.2AA6E5D8AD92D260.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Item Pipes"
	quest.2AA6E5D8AD92D260.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Item Pipes\" on the Automation and Logic page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.3391DEB52E24862E.title: "LaserIO"
	quest.3391DEB52E24862E.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Laser Nodes"
	quest.3391DEB52E24862E.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Laser Nodes\" on the Automation and Logic page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.01F07AC7CEBA34C1.title: "Entangled"
	quest.01F07AC7CEBA34C1.quest_subtitle: "Optional: one inventory, two places"
	quest.01F07AC7CEBA34C1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an Entangled Block is a window into another inventory: bind it to a chest or machine, and anything put in the Entangled Block goes into the bound block, even across dimensions."
		"&eHow:&r ender pearls, obsidian and a wooden chest (check JEI). Right-click the target with the Entangled Binder (pearls, obsidian and a diamond), then right-click the Entangled Block. Click the checkmark when one is working."
		"&eTip:&r put one next to a remote ore processor and pipe the output straight home. Both chunks must be loaded."
	]
	quest.28340CD18CB88A6E.title: "Faster Furnaces"
	quest.28340CD18CB88A6E.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Iron Furnace"
	quest.28340CD18CB88A6E.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Iron Furnace\" on the Generators page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.34FFD4956363A3AB.title: "Copper Furnace"
	quest.34FFD4956363A3AB.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Copper Furnace"
	quest.34FFD4956363A3AB.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Copper Furnace\" on the Generators page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.3D68B879966847C4.title: "Speed and Fuel Augments"
	quest.3D68B879966847C4.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Speed Augment"
	quest.3D68B879966847C4.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Speed Augment\" on the Generators page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.654A264E4B2127B7.title: "Furnace Generator"
	quest.654A264E4B2127B7.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Generator Augment"
	quest.654A264E4B2127B7.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Generator Augment\" on the Generators page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.10C32F4F5C98A2A3.title: "Factory and Blasting"
	quest.10C32F4F5C98A2A3.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Factory Augment"
	quest.10C32F4F5C98A2A3.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Factory Augment\" on the Generators page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.765C3CFF7AB22005.title: "Smoking Augment"
	quest.765C3CFF7AB22005.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Smoking Augment"
	quest.765C3CFF7AB22005.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Smoking Augment\" on the Generators page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.51B6B34D8378335D.title: "Wireless Heat"
	quest.51B6B34D8378335D.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Wireless Heating"
	quest.51B6B34D8378335D.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Wireless Heating\" on the Generators page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.7714F7B6CE6E8C98.title: "Settings Linker"
	quest.7714F7B6CE6E8C98.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Configuration Copier"
	quest.7714F7B6CE6E8C98.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Configuration Copier\" on the Generators page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.7F7F7AE8FCCD5830.title: "Gold Furnace"
	quest.7F7F7AE8FCCD5830.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Gold Furnace"
	quest.7F7F7AE8FCCD5830.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Gold Furnace\" on the Generators page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.4D47DB0CB8D48178.title: "Silver Furnace"
	quest.4D47DB0CB8D48178.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Silver Furnace"
	quest.4D47DB0CB8D48178.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Silver Furnace\" on the Generators page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.120BEFA94919009C.title: "Diamond Furnace"
	quest.120BEFA94919009C.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Diamond Furnace"
	quest.120BEFA94919009C.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Diamond Furnace\" on the Generators page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.00E5D0622F31D483.title: "Crystal Furnace"
	quest.00E5D0622F31D483.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Crystal Furnace"
	quest.00E5D0622F31D483.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Crystal Furnace\" on the Generators page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.31D9AF350D35865B.title: "Emerald Furnace"
	quest.31D9AF350D35865B.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Emerald Furnace"
	quest.31D9AF350D35865B.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Emerald Furnace\" on the Generators page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.015A0B700439D32C.title: "Obsidian Furnace"
	quest.015A0B700439D32C.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Obsidian Furnace"
	quest.015A0B700439D32C.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Obsidian Furnace\" on the Generators page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.049DBCCC2E53857E.title: "Netherite Furnace"
	quest.049DBCCC2E53857E.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Netherite Furnace"
	quest.049DBCCC2E53857E.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Netherite Furnace\" on the Generators page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.067098268A78E98D.title: "The Rainbow Furnace"
	quest.067098268A78E98D.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see The Rainbow Generator"
	quest.067098268A78E98D.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"The Rainbow Generator\" on the Generators page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	chapter.0995B455F4B29E6B.title: "Applied Energistics"
	chapter.0995B455F4B29E6B.chapter_subtitle: [
		"The archive of a god: every item as data, every recipe on demand."
	]
	quest.318686D5930E7632.title: "Before the Archive"
	quest.318686D5930E7632.quest_subtitle: "Any chest: the last storage that isn't data"
	quest.318686D5930E7632.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember a library with no shelves, where every book answered when you thought of it.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Applied Energistics 2 turns items into data. A network of cables, drives and terminals holds everything you own and can craft on demand."
		"&eHow:&r show any chest to begin. Soon a single terminal will replace rooms of them."
		"&eTip:&r AE2 opens in the HV tier here: the Inscriber needs an MI Turbo hull and the Controller a digital circuit."
	]
	quest.05C7F194A8C0C12A.title: "Note: Read the Guide"
	quest.05C7F194A8C0C12A.quest_subtitle: "AE2 ships its own manual"
	quest.05C7F194A8C0C12A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r AE2's in-game guide explains every block, with pictures. Hold G over an AE2 item in JEI or your inventory to open its page."
		"&eTip:&r the guide's 'Getting Started' pages cover channels better than any quest text could."
	]
	quest.0C632BD4268C9AF0.title: "Note: Channels and Power"
	quest.0C632BD4268C9AF0.quest_subtitle: "The two things that break a network"
	quest.0C632BD4268C9AF0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r almost every AE2 problem is one of two things: the network has no power, or a device has no channel."
		"&eHow:&r a device whose light is off has no channel; a dark terminal means no power. Tick one box for each once you've read it."
		"&eTip:&r the Network Tool (later in this chapter) shows both at a glance."
	]
	quest.3492FAC143ED86DA.title: "Quartz Wrench"
	quest.3492FAC143ED86DA.quest_subtitle: "Turn and pick up AE2 blocks"
	quest.3492FAC143ED86DA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the wrench rotates AE2 blocks and sneak-click picks them up, parts included."
		"&eHow:&r certus or nether quartz with iron (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r it also removes a single cable part without breaking the cable."
	]
	quest.35F3D5EA62AB545F.title: "Charger and Inscriber"
	quest.35F3D5EA62AB545F.quest_subtitle: "The two machines every AE2 part goes through"
	quest.35F3D5EA62AB545F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Charger puts energy into certus crystals; the Inscriber presses processors and grinds crystals into dust."
		"&eChemistry:&r real quartz is piezoelectric: squeeze it and it makes a voltage, push a voltage into it and it flexes. AE2 imagines it can store the charge."
		"&eHow:&r the Charger is iron and copper (check JEI). The Inscriber is gated here: it needs an MI Turbo hull."
		"&eTip:&r a Crank on top of the Charger works too, slowly, if your power isn't up yet."
	]
	quest.2F15205AFC6F8614.title: "Dowsing Rod"
	quest.2F15205AFC6F8614.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a magical way to find things"
	quest.2F15205AFC6F8614.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Ars Nouveau's Dowsing Rod highlights nearby blocks of interest. It's a second way into the meteor hunt."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI (it needs source from Ars Nouveau)."
		"&eTip:&r the compass is faster for meteorites; the rod is handy for everything else."
	]
	quest.2D98A4A94ACD191C.title: "Meteorite Compass"
	quest.2D98A4A94ACD191C.quest_subtitle: "It points at fallen stars"
	quest.2D98A4A94ACD191C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the compass needle swings towards the nearest meteorite, where certus and the Inscriber presses wait."
		"&eHow:&r charged certus and iron (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r each meteorite holds one press in its mysterious cube. You need four."
	]
	quest.18BA0BAED4B065FB.title: "Certus Quartz"
	quest.18BA0BAED4B065FB.quest_subtitle: "The crystal every AE2 part starts from"
	quest.18BA0BAED4B065FB.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember crystals that sang when you touched them. These still hum, faintly.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r certus quartz goes into almost every AE2 recipe: processors, glass, cells and cards."
		"&eChemistry:&r certus is fictional, but it behaves like real quartz (SiO₂), which is piezoelectric: squeeze it and it makes a small voltage."
		"&eHow:&r mine certus from meteorite craters and budding certus. Grind crystals into dust in the Inscriber with no press."
		"&eTip:&r charged certus plus certus dust dropped in water makes two new crystals. Grow it once you have a little."
	]
	quest.3AA7CCC895AD04F0.title: "Fluix"
	quest.3AA7CCC895AD04F0.quest_subtitle: "Certus, quartz and redstone, in water"
	quest.3AA7CCC895AD04F0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fluix crystals carry AE2's channels: every cable, core and most parts need fluix."
		"&eChemistry:&r a reaction in solution: charged certus, nether quartz and redstone dropped together in water fuse into fluix. Real crystals also grow fastest from a seed in solution."
		"&eHow:&r throw charged certus, nether quartz and redstone into a water block: you get two fluix crystals. Grind fluix in the Inscriber for dust."
		"&eTip:&r four crystals make a fluix block, which is where ExtendedAE's entro grows (see its own page)."
	]
	quest.1DF011A9A8CA2618.title: "The Three Processors"
	quest.1DF011A9A8CA2618.quest_subtitle: "Logic, calculation and engineering"
	quest.1DF011A9A8CA2618.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r AE2's three processors: logic (gold), calculation (certus) and engineering (diamond). You'll want hundreds of each."
		"&eChemistry:&r gold barely reacts with air or water, so it never corrodes; real chips use it for contacts. Diamond spreads heat better than any metal."
		"&eHow:&r press the material with its press, press MI silicon with the Silicon Press, then inscribe the print, redstone and printed silicon together."
		"&eTip:&r one Inscriber per processor type, each fed by pipes, keeps all three in stock."
	]
	quest.4ACE8FFE618969CC.title: "Cables"
	quest.4ACE8FFE618969CC.quest_subtitle: "Glass, covered and dense"
	quest.4ACE8FFE618969CC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each ME device uses one channel. Glass and covered cables carry 8 channels, dense cables 32. Any colour counts."
		"&eHow:&r fluix crystals and quartz make glass cable; wool covers it; four covered cables and redstone make a dense one (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r build a dense-cable backbone from the controller and branch normal cables off it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive:&r if a device's light is off, it has no channel. Count devices on each normal cable (max 8). Drives, terminals, buses and interfaces all count. Plain cables, quartz fibre and energy cells don't."
	]
	quest.0D560DCA7C168A93.title: "Smart Cables"
	quest.0D560DCA7C168A93.quest_subtitle: "Cables that show their channels"
	quest.0D560DCA7C168A93.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r smart cables light up one stripe per channel in use, so you can see where a branch runs out."
		"&eHow:&r a covered cable plus redstone and glowstone (check JEI); the dense version from dense cable."
		"&eTip:&r use smart cable on the busy branches and plain cable everywhere else."
	]
	quest.2994AD22E14A7662.title: "Note: Count Your Channels"
	quest.2994AD22E14A7662.quest_subtitle: "Eight on a cable, thirty-two on a dense one"
	quest.2994AD22E14A7662.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a controller sends 32 channels out of each face. A normal cable carries 8 of them, a dense cable all 32."
		"&eHow:&r plan one dense line per face, then branch. Click to continue."
		"&eTip:&r a subnetwork behind an interface spends only one channel on the main network."
	]
	quest.41D5614938BB0331.title: "Knife, Anchor and Name Press"
	quest.41D5614938BB0331.quest_subtitle: "Small tools for tidy networks"
	quest.41D5614938BB0331.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the cutting knife makes Cable Anchors (they keep two neighbouring cables from joining) and the Inscriber Name Press, which labels items."
		"&eHow:&r a knife from certus or nether quartz and iron; cut any metal ingot for 4 anchors, or iron for the press (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r rename the press in an anvil, then press anything with it to give it that name. Every chemist labels their bottles."
	]
	quest.6E25945922874D1D.title: "Color Applicator"
	quest.6E25945922874D1D.quest_subtitle: "Paint your cables"
	quest.6E25945922874D1D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Color Applicator paints cables. Cables of different colours don't connect, so two networks can run side by side."
		"&eChemistry:&r dyes work by absorbing some wavelengths of light and reflecting the rest; the colour you see is what's left over."
		"&eHow:&r an energy cell, a 4k component and processors (check JEI). Load dye into it and charge it."
	]
	quest.586BC6690936D78A.title: "Sky Stone"
	quest.586BC6690936D78A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: stone that fell from the sky"
	quest.586BC6690936D78A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r sky stone is the rock of AE2 meteorites. The ME Controller in this pack needs smooth sky stone."
		"&eChemistry:&r real stony meteorites are mostly silicate minerals like olivine and pyroxene; iron meteorites are an iron-nickel alloy."
		"&eHow:&r mine the crater shell (iron pickaxe or better), then smelt sky stone into smooth sky stone."
		"&eTip:&r the Inscriber grinds sky stone into sky dust, which ExtendedAE and AdvancedAE recipes ask for."
	]
	quest.41F9E505FC3331BB.title: "All Four Presses"
	quest.41F9E505FC3331BB.quest_subtitle: "Optional: logic and calculation join the set"
	quest.41F9E505FC3331BB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Inscriber has four presses: silicon, logic, calculation and engineering. You need all four for the processors."
		"&eHow:&r each meteorite's mysterious cube holds one press. Keep finding meteorites until you have the set."
		"&eTip:&r never use your only copy in a long automation line. Make a spare in the Inscriber with an iron block first (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.353932F678CB4992.title: "Printed Silicon"
	quest.353932F678CB4992.quest_subtitle: "Optional: every processor sits on silicon"
	quest.353932F678CB4992.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r printed silicon is the base layer of every AE2 processor."
		"&eChemistry:&r industry makes silicon by heating quartz with carbon to about 2000 °C: SiO₂ + 2C → Si + 2CO. Chips need it purer than 99.9999999%."
		"&eHow:&r press MI silicon ingots in the Inscriber with the Silicon Press. They come from the Electric Blast Furnace (quartz dust + coke dust)."
		"&eTip:&r in this pack certus and sand don't smelt into silicon: carbothermic reduction is the only way, as in the real world."
	]
	quest.2BE1DBF6A42A1D60.title: "Calculation Prints"
	quest.2BE1DBF6A42A1D60.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a quartz heartbeat for the network"
	quest.2BE1DBF6A42A1D60.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r calculation processors go into crafting units, cards, bigger cell components and wireless parts."
		"&eChemistry:&r a real quartz crystal vibrates at a precise frequency when a voltage drives it. Watches count 32,768 vibrations a second to keep time."
		"&eHow:&r press a certus crystal with the Calculation Press, then combine it with redstone and printed silicon."
	]
	quest.201AD8AF75B2F90C.title: "Cell Housings"
	quest.201AD8AF75B2F90C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the case every storage cell needs"
	quest.201AD8AF75B2F90C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a storage cell is a housing plus a component. Item housings take iron; fluid housings take copper."
		"&eHow:&r quartz glass, redstone and metal in a crafting table (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r sneak-use an empty cell in the air to split it back into housing and component, for upgrading to a bigger one."
	]
	quest.69F4CBBE99F8800E.title: "Annihilation and Formation"
	quest.69F4CBBE99F8800E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the cores that move things in and out"
	quest.69F4CBBE99F8800E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r annihilation cores take things into the network; formation cores put things out. Interfaces, providers, planes and assemblers all need both."
		"&eHow:&r nether quartz (annihilation) or certus (formation), plus fluix dust and a logic processor, two at a time."
		"&eTip:&r make a stack of each. Autocrafting eats them fast."
	]
	quest.4EE0310E1069717A.title: "Budding Certus by Hand"
	quest.4EE0310E1069717A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: grow your own crystal farm"
	quest.4EE0310E1069717A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a certus quartz block dropped in water with charged certus becomes Damaged Budding Certus; repeat to climb to Chipped and better."
		"&eHow:&r throw a certus block and a charged crystal into water together (JEI's transform tab)."
		"&eTip:&r lower-grade budding blocks decay as they grow. Keep charged certus to remake them."
	]
	quest.31588D043F199E47.title: "Ender Dust"
	quest.31588D043F199E47.quest_subtitle: "Optional: ground pearls"
	quest.31588D043F199E47.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ender pearls ground into dust in the Inscriber. Entangled singularities, entro seeds and wireless parts use it."
		"&eHow:&r put an ender pearl in the Inscriber with no press."
		"&eTip:&r an enderman model in a Simulation Chamber keeps the pearls coming."
	]
	quest.3345DF7236466D75.title: "Fluix Sword"
	quest.3345DF7236466D75.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Fluix Sword"
	quest.3345DF7236466D75.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Fluix Sword\" on the Gear and Comfort page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.5A12756B50F4FE84.title: "Energy Acceptor"
	quest.5A12756B50F4FE84.quest_subtitle: "AE2 runs on its own energy, fed by FE"
	quest.5A12756B50F4FE84.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the ME network turns FE into its own AE energy. The Energy Acceptor does the converting."
		"&eHow:&r connect it to any FE source (an energy cube, a Powah cell, a Flux Point) and to your cables (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a controller face can't take power directly from FE; always go through an acceptor."
	]
	quest.56E785A27AA8ECF6.title: "Energy Cells"
	quest.56E785A27AA8ECF6.quest_subtitle: "A buffer for big jobs"
	quest.56E785A27AA8ECF6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Energy Cells store AE; a Dense Energy Cell stores eight times more."
		"&eHow:&r the dense cell is eight Energy Cells around a calculation processor (check JEI). Put them anywhere on the network."
		"&eTip:&r when a network flickers during autocrafting, more buffer is usually the cure, not more power input."
	]
	quest.66F0FE99872728C2.title: "Energy Card"
	quest.66F0FE99872728C2.quest_subtitle: "More charge in your portable tools"
	quest.66F0FE99872728C2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an Energy Card raises how much AE a portable terminal, cell or tool holds."
		"&eChemistry:&r a battery's capacity depends on how much reactant it holds; adding cells in parallel adds capacity, as this card does."
		"&eHow:&r an advanced card plus a dense energy cell (check JEI). Slot it into the item in a Cell Workbench."
	]
	quest.76110B693DBF6FF2.title: "Terminals"
	quest.76110B693DBF6FF2.quest_subtitle: "Your window into the archive"
	quest.76110B693DBF6FF2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the ME Terminal shows and searches everything the network stores. The Crafting Terminal adds a crafting grid that pulls from storage."
		"&eHow:&r an illuminated panel plus processors; the crafting version adds a crafting table (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r JEI's + button fills the crafting terminal's grid straight from the network."
	]
	quest.14F903B26956D603.title: "ME Controller"
	quest.14F903B26956D603.quest_subtitle: "The heart of the network"
	quest.14F903B26956D603.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Controller hands out channels: 32 from each face. Without one, a network is limited to 8 devices."
		"&eHow:&r in this pack it takes smooth sky stone, fluix, an engineering processor and an MI digital circuit (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r controller blocks can be joined into a bigger box, but never into a cross or a loop."
	]
	quest.162A48BA45345800.title: "Network Tool"
	quest.162A48BA45345800.quest_subtitle: "Read channels and power at a glance"
	quest.162A48BA45345800.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r right-click any cable or device with the Network Tool to see its channels, power use and status. It also holds spare upgrade cards."
		"&eHow:&r a quartz wrench, a chest and a calculation processor (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r when something's dark, this is the first tool to reach for."
	]
	quest.33690DED4CD25646.title: "ME Chest and Drive"
	quest.33690DED4CD25646.quest_subtitle: "Where the cells live"
	quest.33690DED4CD25646.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember a mind that held every name of every thing. The archive is waking.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the ME Chest is a one-cell drive with its own terminal. The ME Drive holds ten cells for the whole network."
		"&eHow:&r both from iron, quartz glass, fluix cable and processors (check JEI). Connect the drive to the controller with cable."
		"&eTip:&r keep power stable: an Energy Cell buffers the network."
	]
	quest.3038F3E8F86270FC.title: "Cell Workbench"
	quest.3038F3E8F86270FC.quest_subtitle: "Partition and upgrade cells"
	quest.3038F3E8F86270FC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Cell Workbench sets which items a cell accepts (partitioning) and adds cards to cells."
		"&eHow:&r wool, iron, a chest and a calculation processor (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a cell partitioned to one dust keeps that stock in one place."
	]
	quest.06B6E959227F5BB6.title: "IO Port"
	quest.06B6E959227F5BB6.quest_subtitle: "Move whole cells at once"
	quest.06B6E959227F5BB6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the IO Port empties a cell into the network, or fills a cell from it."
		"&eHow:&r glass, two drives, fluix cable, iron and a logic processor (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r upgrading 4k cells to 64k? Run the old cells through an IO Port first."
	]
	quest.5F3A3A91F04E760E.title: "Equal Distribution Card"
	quest.5F3A3A91F04E760E.quest_subtitle: "Spread items over a cell's partitions"
	quest.5F3A3A91F04E760E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r with this card a partitioned cell keeps the same room for each of its items, so one item can't crowd out the others."
		"&eHow:&r a basic card plus a few items (check JEI). Slot it in through the Cell Workbench."
	]
	quest.028EAB5670EA3CA4.title: "Overflow Destruction Card"
	quest.028EAB5670EA3CA4.quest_subtitle: "Delete what a full cell can't hold"
	quest.028EAB5670EA3CA4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a cell with this card destroys items of its partitioned types once it's full, instead of refusing them."
		"&eChemistry:&r real matter can't vanish: mass is conserved in every chemical reaction. In Minecraft it can."
		"&eHow:&r a basic card plus a few items (check JEI). Use it with a partition, or it will delete everything."
		"&eTip:&r a void card on a cobblestone cell stops a generator from filling your whole network."
	]
	quest.58932D295CE4DB3B.title: "1k Component"
	quest.58932D295CE4DB3B.quest_subtitle: "Bytes for your items"
	quest.58932D295CE4DB3B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r components are the memory inside every storage cell. The 1k is the smallest."
		"&eChemistry:&r certus and fluix are fictional, but the logic processors behind them echo real chips: doped silicon (Si)."
		"&eHow:&r certus, redstone and a logic processor (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.4AA0804D5C3521EA.title: "4k Component"
	quest.4AA0804D5C3521EA.quest_subtitle: "Four times the bytes"
	quest.4AA0804D5C3521EA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the first step up: a 4k component holds four times as many bytes as a 1k."
		"&eHow:&r three 1k components around quartz glass, with redstone and a calculation processor (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.7D7098581E0AE024.title: "16k Component"
	quest.7D7098581E0AE024.quest_subtitle: "Room for whole chemical stocks"
	quest.7D7098581E0AE024.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each tier combines three of the last with a calculation processor and quartz glass."
		"&eHow:&r 16k from three 4k (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a cell holds up to 63 item types whatever its size, so use small cells for odd items and big cells for bulk."
	]
	quest.02A16286559E58B6.title: "64k Component"
	quest.02A16286559E58B6.quest_subtitle: "Enough for a mine's worth of dust"
	quest.02A16286559E58B6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the 64k component, also what the Matter Condenser needs to make singularities."
		"&eHow:&r three 16k components around quartz glass, with a calculation processor (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.0D2DB0C5B5689C1A.title: "256k Component"
	quest.0D2DB0C5B5689C1A.quest_subtitle: "The biggest cell in base AE2"
	quest.0D2DB0C5B5689C1A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the top AE2 component: 256 kilobytes for a single cell."
		"&eHow:&r three 64k components around quartz glass, with sky stone dust and a calculation processor (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a cell spends bytes on every new item type, so put bulk stock here and rare items elsewhere."
	]
	quest.642DEBE4D8CDB237.title: "1M Component"
	quest.642DEBE4D8CDB237.quest_subtitle: "MEGA Cells: a million bytes"
	quest.642DEBE4D8CDB237.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MEGA Cells continues the ladder past 256k: 1M, 4M, 16M, 64M, 256M."
		"&eHow:&r 256k components, sky steel and accumulation processors (check JEI; the MEGA Cells section has both)."
		"&eTip:&r MEGA components need MEGA cell housings; AE2's won't take them."
	]
	quest.38EEABF9A5AA71CB.title: "4M Component"
	quest.38EEABF9A5AA71CB.quest_subtitle: "Four million bytes"
	quest.38EEABF9A5AA71CB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the 4M component, four times the 1M."
		"&eHow:&r 1M components, accumulation processors, ender dust and vibrant quartz glass (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.7360CDF6E6826C06.title: "16M Component"
	quest.7360CDF6E6826C06.quest_subtitle: "Sixteen million"
	quest.7360CDF6E6826C06.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the next MEGA step."
		"&eHow:&r three 4M components with accumulation processors (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.74259CDF279E1A53.title: "64M Component"
	quest.74259CDF279E1A53.quest_subtitle: "Sixty-four million"
	quest.74259CDF279E1A53.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one step from the top."
		"&eHow:&r three 16M components with accumulation processors (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.0E1219045D005E45.title: "256M Component"
	quest.0E1219045D005E45.quest_subtitle: "The largest component there is"
	quest.0E1219045D005E45.quest_desc: [
		"&6Every name of every thing, and room to spare. You remember this kind of memory.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the 256M MEGA component, the top of AE2 storage in this pack."
		"&eHow:&r three 64M components with accumulation processors (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.3B9ED29B7DF90798.title: "Item Storage Cell"
	quest.3B9ED29B7DF90798.quest_subtitle: "A component in a housing"
	quest.3B9ED29B7DF90798.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the 1k item cell: the thing you actually put in a drive."
		"&eHow:&r a 1k component in an item cell housing (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r sneak-use an empty cell in the air to split it back into housing and component."
	]
	quest.0553CB1F25E72491.title: "Fluid Storage Cell"
	quest.0553CB1F25E72491.quest_subtitle: "Acids and solvents as data"
	quest.0553CB1F25E72491.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fluid cells store fluids the same way item cells store items. Any size counts."
		"&eChemistry:&r H₂SO₄, HCl and HNO₃ each eat through different metals, so a real lab needs a different container for each. A fluid cell doesn't care."
		"&eHow:&r a component in a fluid cell housing (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.647BDAE4B7B8ECF3.title: "Portable Cell"
	quest.647BDAE4B7B8ECF3.quest_subtitle: "A drive in your pocket"
	quest.647BDAE4B7B8ECF3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a portable cell is a storage cell with its own terminal and battery. Any size, item or fluid."
		"&eHow:&r a component, a chest, a terminal and an energy cell (check JEI). Charge it in the Charger."
		"&eTip:&r a portable cell on a mining trip holds far more than a backpack."
	]
	quest.606F92F0A56293B8.title: "Bulk Item Cell"
	quest.606F92F0A56293B8.quest_subtitle: "One item, practically no limit"
	quest.606F92F0A56293B8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Bulk Item Cell holds a single item type in near-unlimited amounts."
		"&eHow:&r the bulk component needs a 1M component and accumulation processors (check JEI). Partition it in a Cell Workbench."
		"&eTip:&r perfect for cobblestone (condenser feed), salt dust or coal coke. A Compression Card stores nuggets, ingots and blocks as one pool."
	]
	quest.7257CA35618CA7BF.title: "AE2 Powered Tools"
	quest.7257CA35618CA7BF.quest_subtitle: "Zap, heat and cool, shoot"
	quest.7257CA35618CA7BF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Charged Staff zaps mobs; the Entropy Manipulator heats or cools blocks; the Matter Cannon fires matter balls or nuggets."
		"&eChemistry:&r the manipulator follows real phase changes: removing heat freezes water, and lava cools into obsidian when it loses heat too fast to crystallise."
		"&eHow:&r each uses an energy cell and processors; the cannon also takes a 4k component (check JEI). Charge them in the Charger."
	]
	quest.740C1D9B0EE26F7C.title: "Sky Steel"
	quest.740C1D9B0EE26F7C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the lava alloy behind MEGA's cells"
	quest.740C1D9B0EE26F7C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r sky steel goes into every MEGA part. The 1M item cell is the first MEGA cell you can put in a drive."
		"&eChemistry:&r sky steel is made by dropping charged certus, iron and sky stone into lava: heat drives the alloying, like a tiny smelter."
		"&eHow:&r throw the ingredients into a lava pool for sky steel, then build the 1M cell (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.096161FE28A839F6.title: "Sky Bronze and Sky Osmium"
	quest.096161FE28A839F6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: more lava alloys"
	quest.096161FE28A839F6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the same lava trick with copper gives sky bronze, and with osmium gives sky osmium. Both go into MEGA's larger parts."
		"&eChemistry:&r real bronze is copper plus tin (Cu + Sn); here the sky stone plays the tin. Osmium (Os) is the densest natural element, 22.6 g/cm³."
		"&eHow:&r drop charged certus, the ingot and a sky stone block into lava together."
	]
	quest.5160F2053D91D317.title: "Accumulation Processors"
	quest.5160F2053D91D317.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a press made from a singularity"
	quest.5160F2053D91D317.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the accumulation processor is MEGA's fourth processor, needed for every 1M+ part."
		"&eHow:&r inscribe a singularity between the calculation and engineering presses to make the Accumulation Press, then print sky steel with it (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r keep the press. The Inscriber can copy it with an iron block, like the other presses."
	]
	quest.1665F7B5F4B8CBDF.title: "MEGA Crafting CPU"
	quest.1665F7B5F4B8CBDF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: room for the biggest crafting jobs"
	quest.1665F7B5F4B8CBDF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r MEGA crafting storage and units build a separate, much larger crafting CPU."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. MEGA blocks only join other MEGA blocks, so build it as its own multiblock."
		"&eTip:&r the Seed of a New World chain is huge. One big CPU saves splitting the job by hand."
	]
	quest.6A29B228E6049846.title: "MEGA Pattern Provider"
	quest.6A29B228E6049846.quest_subtitle: "Optional: room for many more patterns"
	quest.6A29B228E6049846.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a pattern provider with many more pattern slots than the normal one."
		"&eHow:&r made as a cable part and turned into a block in the crafting grid (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r put one on each multi-input MI machine, like the Chemical Reactor."
	]
	quest.4E78EF5F2B0FEF48.title: "MEGA Energy"
	quest.4E78EF5F2B0FEF48.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a huge AE buffer and a stronger card"
	quest.4E78EF5F2B0FEF48.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the MEGA Energy Cell is eight dense cells around an accumulation processor. The Greater Energy Card gives portable tools far more charge."
		"&eHow:&r both in a crafting table (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.2EAE22CFCB5FBC80.title: "A Pocket Archive"
	quest.2EAE22CFCB5FBC80.quest_subtitle: "Optional: 256M in your inventory"
	quest.2EAE22CFCB5FBC80.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a portable cell with a 256M component: a whole storage network you carry, no drive needed."
		"&eHow:&r a 256M component in a portable cell housing with an energy cell (check JEI). Charge it first."
		"&eTip:&r perfect for a long trip to another planet."
	]
	quest.02D7A1418218250D.title: "ME Interface"
	quest.02D7A1418218250D.quest_subtitle: "Stock a machine, or join two networks"
	quest.02D7A1418218250D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an interface keeps chosen items stocked in itself for pipes and machines to pull. A storage bus on an interface lets one network see into another. Block or cable-part version."
		"&eHow:&r iron, glass, an annihilation core and a formation core (check JEI). Set the items to keep in its top row."
		"&eTip:&r a subnetwork for one chemical line, joined to the main network through an interface, keeps channels free."
	]
	quest.636E8714507A8D35.title: "Import Bus"
	quest.636E8714507A8D35.quest_subtitle: "Pull items into the network"
	quest.636E8714507A8D35.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an Import Bus pulls items out of the inventory it faces and into storage."
		"&eHow:&r an annihilation core, iron and a sticky piston (check JEI). Put it on a cable facing a machine's output."
		"&eTip:&r add a filter and Acceleration Cards to pull only products, faster."
	]
	quest.3B6C8D5CFF16EEC2.title: "Export Bus"
	quest.3B6C8D5CFF16EEC2.quest_subtitle: "Push items out to a machine"
	quest.3B6C8D5CFF16EEC2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an Export Bus pushes chosen items from storage into the inventory it faces."
		"&eHow:&r a formation core, iron and a piston (check JEI). Set what it exports in its slots."
		"&eTip:&r an export bus feeding coal coke to a boiler keeps it lit forever."
	]
	quest.14720B35A2C4785D.title: "Annihilation Plane"
	quest.14720B35A2C4785D.quest_subtitle: "Break blocks into the network"
	quest.14720B35A2C4785D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Annihilation Plane breaks the block in front of it, or picks up items that land there, and stores them."
		"&eHow:&r fluix crystals and an annihilation core (check JEI). It takes enchantments like a pickaxe."
		"&eTip:&r an annihilation plane in front of a cobblestone generator feeds the Matter Condenser with no pipes."
	]
	quest.614AA74634A8965A.title: "Formation Plane"
	quest.614AA74634A8965A.quest_subtitle: "Place blocks or drop items out"
	quest.614AA74634A8965A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Formation Plane places blocks (or drops items) from the network into the space in front of it."
		"&eHow:&r fluix crystals and a formation core (check JEI). Filter it, or it places anything you store."
	]
	quest.15163874C4379E91.title: "P2P Tunnels"
	quest.15163874C4379E91.quest_subtitle: "One cable, many channels"
	quest.15163874C4379E91.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a pair of P2P tunnels carries 32 channels (or items, fluids, FE and redstone) through a single cable."
		"&eHow:&r iron, an engineering processor and fluix (check JEI). Place both ends, then link them with a Memory Card."
		"&eTip:&r right-click a P2P tunnel with a bucket, redstone dust or an FE item to change what it carries."
	]
	quest.4F9BB43621109E32.title: "Storage Bus"
	quest.4F9BB43621109E32.quest_subtitle: "Treat any chest as network storage"
	quest.4F9BB43621109E32.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Storage Bus on a chest, drawer controller or tank lets the network read and fill it as if it were a cell."
		"&eHow:&r an interface, a piston and a sticky piston (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a storage bus on your Functional Storage controller gives AE2 the whole drawer wall, without spending cell types."
	]
	quest.4B75F7D88F4A9553.title: "Memory Card"
	quest.4B75F7D88F4A9553.quest_subtitle: "Copy settings from part to part"
	quest.4B75F7D88F4A9553.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Memory Card copies a part's settings and filters to another, and links P2P tunnels."
		"&eHow:&r a calculation processor, iron, gold and redstone (check JEI). Sneak-use it on the source, then use it on the target."
	]
	quest.3D1702FD08C4B831.title: "Capacity Card"
	quest.3D1702FD08C4B831.quest_subtitle: "More filter slots"
	quest.3D1702FD08C4B831.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Capacity Card adds filter slots to buses and other parts."
		"&eHow:&r a basic card plus certus (check JEI). Slot it into the part's upgrade slots."
	]
	quest.79201527AD910B0C.title: "Fuzzy and Inverter Cards"
	quest.79201527AD910B0C.quest_subtitle: "Looser matches, reversed filters"
	quest.79201527AD910B0C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Fuzzy matches items by damage or ignores their data; Inverter turns a whitelist into a blacklist."
		"&eHow:&r an advanced card plus one extra item each (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r an inverted storage bus on a junk chest takes everything except what you list."
	]
	quest.43D2CB1DCAE0ECF0.title: "Quartz Fiber"
	quest.43D2CB1DCAE0ECF0.quest_subtitle: "Share power, not channels"
	quest.43D2CB1DCAE0ECF0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Quartz Fiber passes power between two networks without joining them."
		"&eChemistry:&r glass made from pure SiO₂ (fused silica) is what real optical fibre is made of: so clear that light travels kilometres inside it."
		"&eHow:&r glass and quartz dust (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.72E2395F124F6C52.title: "Tunnels for Everything"
	quest.72E2395F124F6C52.quest_subtitle: "Optional: P2P for power and fluids"
	quest.72E2395F124F6C52.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r P2P tunnels can carry FE, fluids, items, light or redstone instead of channels."
		"&eHow:&r right-click an ME P2P tunnel with what it should carry, like a bucket or an FE item (check JEI for the full list)."
		"&eTip:&r FE tunnels move power through one cable instead of a bundle of power lines."
	]
	quest.4406D049ECD7E7BB.title: "Pattern Providers"
	quest.4406D049ECD7E7BB.quest_subtitle: "Where recipes meet machines"
	quest.4406D049ECD7E7BB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Pattern Provider holds crafting patterns and sends their inputs to the machine it faces. The Pattern Access Terminal shows every provider on one screen."
		"&eHow:&r iron, a crafting table and cores for the provider; an illuminated panel, an engineering processor and a provider for the terminal (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r processing patterns can drive MI machines too: send the inputs, wait for the outputs. The Automation and Logic page walks through a full sulfuric acid line."
	]
	quest.53E9E47DF10A9447.title: "Encoding Patterns"
	quest.53E9E47DF10A9447.quest_subtitle: "Write a recipe onto a pattern"
	quest.53E9E47DF10A9447.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Pattern Encoding Terminal writes crafting or processing recipes onto blank patterns."
		"&eHow:&r a crafting terminal plus an engineering processor; blank patterns from quartz glass, glowstone and iron (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r JEI's + button fills the encoder with any recipe you look up."
	]
	quest.55FA1AEAC65FBDE9.title: "Molecular Assembler"
	quest.55FA1AEAC65FBDE9.quest_subtitle: "A crafting table that runs itself"
	quest.55FA1AEAC65FBDE9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Molecular Assembler next to a pattern provider crafts crafting-table recipes for the network."
		"&eHow:&r iron, quartz glass, cores and a crafting table (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r one provider can feed up to six assemblers, one on each face."
	]
	quest.7B5A836AFA0968E6.title: "Acceleration Card"
	quest.7B5A836AFA0968E6.quest_subtitle: "Faster buses, Inscribers and assemblers"
	quest.7B5A836AFA0968E6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Acceleration Cards speed up buses, Inscribers and Molecular Assemblers."
		"&eHow:&r an advanced card plus fluix (check JEI). Up to five in an assembler."
	]
	quest.0E248F7AA8933C24.title: "Level Emitter"
	quest.0E248F7AA8933C24.quest_subtitle: "A redstone signal that counts"
	quest.0E248F7AA8933C24.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Level Emitter gives a redstone signal when the network holds more (or less) of an item than you set."
		"&eHow:&r a redstone torch and a calculation processor (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r wire one to an MI Electrolyzer so it only runs while hydrogen stock is low."
	]
	quest.4447903D72FA5B90.title: "Redstone Card and Toggle Bus"
	quest.4447903D72FA5B90.quest_subtitle: "Switch parts and branches by signal"
	quest.4447903D72FA5B90.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Redstone Card makes a bus work only with (or without) a signal. A Toggle Bus connects or cuts a cable branch by redstone."
		"&eHow:&r a basic card plus a redstone torch; the toggle bus is fluix cable, redstone and a lever (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r put a toggle bus in front of a subnetwork you only want running sometimes."
	]
	quest.1AED651855E02225.title: "Crafting Card"
	quest.1AED651855E02225.quest_subtitle: "A bus that orders what it lacks"
	quest.1AED651855E02225.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r with a Crafting Card, an export bus or interface asks autocrafting for items the network doesn't have."
		"&eHow:&r a basic card plus a crafting table (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a Crafting Card and a Redstone Card together make items only when a machine asks for them."
	]
	quest.2A7CE0F1602C61FA.title: "Growth Accelerator"
	quest.2A7CE0F1602C61FA.quest_subtitle: "Crystal farms at full speed"
	quest.2A7CE0F1602C61FA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Growth Accelerators speed up certus buds growing on budding certus blocks."
		"&eChemistry:&r real quartz crystals grow from silica-rich water over thousands of years. The idea of a seed crystal pulling material out of solution is real."
		"&eHow:&r iron, fluix cable, quartz glass and a fluix block (check JEI). Place them touching budding certus and power them."
		"&eTip:&r flawless budding certus never decays. Never break it with a normal pickaxe."
	]
	quest.416648248906CFC3.title: "Crafting Storage"
	quest.416648248906CFC3.quest_subtitle: "The memory of a crafting CPU"
	quest.416648248906CFC3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r crafting storage blocks make a crafting CPU: the bigger the storage, the bigger the job it can plan."
		"&eHow:&r a crafting unit plus a cell component of the matching size (check JEI). Build a solid box of crafting blocks."
		"&eTip:&r two CPUs beat one huge one: a long job then doesn't block a quick request."
	]
	quest.732A1D66682FA86D.title: "Co-Processor"
	quest.732A1D66682FA86D.quest_subtitle: "More steps at once"
	quest.732A1D66682FA86D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each Crafting Co-Processing Unit lets a CPU run one more step at the same time."
		"&eHow:&r a crafting unit plus an engineering processor (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r co-processors only help if the machines keep up. Ten acid patterns on one Chemical Reactor still run one at a time."
	]
	quest.4CC7CDE3DE6F7C67.title: "Crafting Monitor"
	quest.4CC7CDE3DE6F7C67.quest_subtitle: "See what the CPU is making"
	quest.4CC7CDE3DE6F7C67.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Crafting Monitor shows the item a CPU is working on, right on its face."
		"&eHow:&r a crafting unit plus a storage monitor (check JEI). Part of the CPU's box."
	]
	quest.15508397E54C44E6.title: "A Bigger Plan"
	quest.15508397E54C44E6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: crafting storage for long chains"
	quest.15508397E54C44E6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r long chemical chains need far more crafting storage than 1k."
		"&eHow:&r a crafting unit plus a 16k or 64k component (check JEI). Add them to the CPU's box."
	]
	quest.3E6BB0338E3344C9.title: "ME Requester"
	quest.3E6BB0338E3344C9.quest_subtitle: "Optional: keep stock topped up"
	quest.3E6BB0338E3344C9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the ME Requester keeps a set amount of an item in stock by ordering crafts automatically."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Set \"keep 64 HDPE\" and it never runs out."
		"&eTip:&r it needs autocrafting patterns for whatever it keeps in stock."
	]
	quest.0CC9A52C043BEE4C.title: "Requester Terminal"
	quest.0CC9A52C043BEE4C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: every stock rule on one screen"
	quest.0CC9A52C043BEE4C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Requester Terminal lists every ME Requester on the network."
		"&eHow:&r an illuminated panel, a logic processor and a Requester, shapeless (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r keep a stock rule for each acid: H₂SO₄, HCl and HNO₃ feed almost everything late game."
	]
	quest.0793BD80DC7ABE69.title: "Packaged Extended Crafting"
	quest.0793BD80DC7ABE69.quest_subtitle: "Optional: autocraft on the big tables"
	quest.0793BD80DC7ABE69.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Packaged ExCrafting adds crafters that run Extended Crafting recipes from packages."
		"&eHow:&r an auto table of the right size, an ME package component, crystaltine components, black iron and a redstone catalyst (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r encode the recipe in the Packaged Auto encoder, just like normal packages."
	]
	quest.24D6EC7D3175543C.title: "The Ultimate Crafter"
	quest.24D6EC7D3175543C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: 9x9 recipes on demand"
	quest.24D6EC7D3175543C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Ultimate Crafter runs 9x9 Ultimate Table recipes automatically from the network."
		"&eHow:&r same recipe as the basic crafter, with an Ultimate Auto Table in the middle (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the Seed of a New World is a 9x9 recipe. Feed it from the network and the capstone crafts itself."
	]
	quest.29DF6C2F77C3462E.title: "Matter Condenser"
	quest.29DF6C2F77C3462E.quest_subtitle: "Crush items into matter"
	quest.29DF6C2F77C3462E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Matter Condenser destroys items. With a component inside, it squeezes them into Matter Balls (or, with a 64k, a Singularity)."
		"&eHow:&r craft it (check JEI), put a component in, set the mode and feed it cobblestone from a pipe."
		"&eTip:&r matter balls are Matter Cannon ammo; singularities unlock MEGA's press and every AdvancedAE machine."
	]
	quest.6DB07A0E0C18A4CB.title: "Singularity, Dust and a Small Bang"
	quest.6DB07A0E0C18A4CB.quest_subtitle: "The ingredients of entanglement"
	quest.6DB07A0E0C18A4CB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a singularity from the condenser, ender dust from the Inscriber and Tiny TNT: together they make entangled singularities."
		"&eChemistry:&r gunpowder is potassium nitrate, charcoal and sulfur: 2KNO₃ + S + 3C → K₂S + N₂ + 3CO₂. The gases expanding all at once are the bang."
		"&eHow:&r drop a singularity and ender dust together, then set off Tiny TNT next to them: you get a pair of Quantum Entangled Singularities."
		"&eTip:&r set it off away from anything you care about. It is still TNT."
	]
	quest.12502172FFC387E5.title: "Quantum Bridge"
	quest.12502172FFC387E5.quest_subtitle: "Link networks across dimensions"
	quest.12502172FFC387E5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r two Quantum Network Bridges joined by entangled singularities act like one cable, even across dimensions."
		"&eHow:&r build a 3x3 ring of 8 Quantum Rings around a Quantum Link Chamber at each end, then put one of a pair of entangled singularities in each chamber."
		"&eTip:&r both ends must be chunk-loaded. Use FTB Chunks to force-load them."
	]
	quest.2DC9FE73876C2216.title: "Spooky Action"
	quest.2DC9FE73876C2216.quest_subtitle: "Secret: two particles, one fate"
	quest.2DC9FE73876C2216.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember being in two places at once. It felt exactly like this.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r you made a pair of Quantum Entangled Singularities by blowing up a singularity with ender dust."
		"&eChemistry:&r real entangled particles share one quantum state: measure one and you know the other, however far apart. Sadly it can't send messages faster than light; AE2 is kinder."
	]
	quest.67C615814E0346D9.title: "Loaded Cannon"
	quest.67C615814E0346D9.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the heavier the atom, the harder it hits"
	quest.67C615814E0346D9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Matter Cannon fires matter balls or metal nuggets from a cell inside it."
		"&eChemistry:&r AE2 rates each nugget by its element's real atomic mass: iron 55.8, osmium 190.2, uranium 238. Heavier atoms carry more momentum at the same speed."
		"&eHow:&r a condenser on Matter Ball mode makes ammo; the cannon's tooltip shows how to load it."
		"&eTip:&r osmium and uranium nuggets are the best ammo you'll have spare."
	]
	quest.45E7618F9628A70D.title: "Wireless Access Point"
	quest.45E7618F9628A70D.quest_subtitle: "Where every wireless terminal connects"
	quest.45E7618F9628A70D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Wireless Access Point sends your network a short distance through the air. Boosters raise its range."
		"&eHow:&r a wireless receiver over a calculation processor and fluix cable; boosters from fluix dust, certus, ender dust and iron (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r put the access point near the middle of your base for the best coverage."
	]
	quest.72A62F77A5D7C0CE.title: "Wireless Terminals"
	quest.72A62F77A5D7C0CE.quest_subtitle: "Your network in your pocket"
	quest.72A62F77A5D7C0CE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r reach your ME network from anywhere in range of a Wireless Access Point. The crafting version has a grid too."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Link the terminal by putting it in the access point, and charge it in the Charger."
	]
	quest.5F84732A701D2559.title: "Infinite Range"
	quest.5F84732A701D2559.quest_subtitle: "No range limit, in any dimension"
	quest.5F84732A701D2559.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Infinity Booster Card removes the access point's range limit in one dimension; the Dimension Card reaches every dimension."
		"&eHow:&r both need Nether Stars, so the Wither comes first (check JEI). The dimension card takes four infinity cards."
		"&eTip:&r put the card in the Wireless Access Point, not the terminal, and keep that chunk loaded."
	]
	quest.26BA1E4C00A29726.title: "Quantum Bridge Card"
	quest.26BA1E4C00A29726.quest_subtitle: "Your terminal, through an entangled pair"
	quest.26BA1E4C00A29726.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r this AE2 Wireless Terminals card lets a terminal reach the network through quantum entanglement, from any distance or dimension."
		"&eHow:&r quantum rings, a Quantum Link Chamber and an advanced card (check JEI). Its tooltip explains how to pair it."
		"&eTip:&r the network's end must stay chunk-loaded."
	]
	quest.07860310FF05CBD6.title: "Universal Terminal"
	quest.07860310FF05CBD6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: one terminal to rule them all"
	quest.07860310FF05CBD6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r AE2 Wireless Terminals merges the crafting, pattern access and pattern encoding terminals into one Universal Terminal."
		"&eHow:&r combine two wireless terminals in a crafting grid (check JEI); add more by crafting them in again."
		"&eTip:&r a Magnet Card from the same mod pulls nearby drops straight into your network."
	]
	quest.0ADD4DC8D8127357.title: "A Spare Dimension Card"
	quest.0ADD4DC8D8127357.quest_subtitle: "Optional: one for every base"
	quest.0ADD4DC8D8127357.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a second Dimension Card, for a second network or an outpost's access point."
		"&eHow:&r four Infinity Cards, four Nether Stars and an eye of ender (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.56AC603AD4E1D10D.title: "Import and Export Cards"
	quest.56AC603AD4E1D10D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: your inventory, auto-sorted"
	quest.56AC603AD4E1D10D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r these cards go in a wireless terminal. The Import Card pushes chosen items from your inventory into the network; the Export Card keeps chosen items stocked in your inventory."
		"&eHow:&r an import (or export) bus, redstone blocks, an advanced card and processors (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r set the Import Card to cobblestone, dirt and raw ores, and mining trips never fill your inventory."
	]
	quest.41E4A1BAA00E0A6E.title: "Spatial IO Port"
	quest.41E4A1BAA00E0A6E.quest_subtitle: "Cut a room out of the world"
	quest.41E4A1BAA00E0A6E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Spatial IO Port stores everything inside a frame of Spatial Pylons in a spatial cell, and can put it back elsewhere."
		"&eHow:&r glass, an IO Port and an engineering processor (check JEI and the AE2 guide)."
		"&eTip:&r the stored room becomes a real dimension you can visit. Ask before you move someone else's base."
	]
	quest.19998927D7814BD9.title: "Spatial Pylon"
	quest.19998927D7814BD9.quest_subtitle: "The frame of the box"
	quest.19998927D7814BD9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r pylons outline the space to be stored, along three edges of a box."
		"&eHow:&r fluix and quartz glass (check JEI). Each pylon row also takes a channel."
	]
	quest.3CEFA211E8DB8054.title: "Spatial Anchor"
	quest.3CEFA211E8DB8054.quest_subtitle: "Optional: keep a network's chunks loaded"
	quest.3CEFA211E8DB8054.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Spatial Anchor keeps every chunk its network touches loaded."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI."
		"&eTip:&r one anchor keeps both ends of a quantum bridge alive."
	]
	quest.69975626027FAAC7.title: "Spatial Cell"
	quest.69975626027FAAC7.quest_subtitle: "A room in a cell"
	quest.69975626027FAAC7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r spatial cells hold the stored space: 2, 16 or 128 blocks to a side."
		"&eHow:&r a spatial component in a housing (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.6ABB15806114CC83.title: "Gas in the Network"
	quest.6ABB15806114CC83.quest_subtitle: "Optional: store Mekanism chemicals in AE2"
	quest.6ABB15806114CC83.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Applied Mekanistics lets AE2 store and move Mekanism chemicals: H₂, O₂, Cl₂, HCl, SO₂ and the rest."
		"&eChemistry:&r a 1k cell holds a lot of gas because the network stores amounts, not tanks. Real gases need pressure vessels."
		"&eHow:&r a chemical cell housing (osmium, quartz glass, redstone) + a 1k component. Import buses on chemical tanks fill it."
		"&eTip:&r processing patterns can pull stored SO₂ and O₂ straight from the cell to feed your sulfuric acid line."
	]
	quest.52CB2FB63C5C2051.title: "A Tank Farm in a Cell"
	quest.52CB2FB63C5C2051.quest_subtitle: "Optional: 64k of chemicals"
	quest.52CB2FB63C5C2051.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a 64k chemical cell replaces a room full of chemical tanks."
		"&eChemistry:&r one mole of any ideal gas fills about 22.4 L at 0 °C and 1 atm. Stored as data, it fills nothing at all."
		"&eHow:&r chemical housing plus a 64k component (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.049F324F4DE92733.title: "Shielded Storage"
	quest.049F324F4DE92733.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a cell for hot chemicals"
	quest.049F324F4DE92733.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r normal chemical cells refuse radioactive chemicals. MEGA's Radioactive Chemical Cell holds one, like nuclear waste or plutonium."
		"&eChemistry:&r spent fuel stays dangerous because unstable nuclei keep decaying, giving off α, β and γ radiation for years."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the radioactive component and cell."
	]
	quest.4B1B2296A5EDEB45.title: "Energy in a Cell"
	quest.4B1B2296A5EDEB45.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Applied Flux stores FE in AE2"
	quest.4B1B2296A5EDEB45.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Applied Flux stores FE in AE2 cells and moves it through the network with Flux Accessors."
		"&eHow:&r redstone crystal (redstone block, fluix and glowstone dropped in water) → charge it in the Charger → FE cell core and housing (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the housing needs insulating resin, which needs silicon: a little chemistry even here."
	]
	quest.136207F7A3DC6A3C.title: "Flux Accessor"
	quest.136207F7A3DC6A3C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: power machines from the network"
	quest.136207F7A3DC6A3C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Flux Accessor pushes FE from your FE cells into any machine it touches. An Induction Card lets an I/O bus or interface do the same."
		"&eHow:&r an energy acceptor, energy processors, copper and glowstone (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r one FE cell plus accessors can replace a tangle of power cables."
	]
	chapter.289AD3164561F6B2.title: "Extended and Advanced AE"
	chapter.289AD3164561F6B2.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Bigger providers, faster crafters, and a computer that thinks in parallel."
	]
	quest.72672D38B08444F2.title: "Beyond the Basics"
	quest.72672D38B08444F2.quest_subtitle: "Two addons that grow AE2 up"
	quest.72672D38B08444F2.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember the archive was never big enough. It can grow.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r ExtendedAE adds bigger versions of AE2's blocks and a new crystal, entro. AdvancedAE adds a reaction chamber, quantum alloy and a multiblock crafting computer."
		"&eHow:&r any fluix crystal opens this page. Both halves start from it."
		"&eTip:&r the Assembler Matrix and the Quantum Computer are the two big builds here; everything else feeds them."
	]
	quest.164CEEB154CFCC2C.title: "Note: Two Mods, One Page"
	quest.164CEEB154CFCC2C.quest_subtitle: "Which half is which"
	quest.164CEEB154CFCC2C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the top half of this page is ExtendedAE (entro, the Crystal Assembler, extended blocks). The bottom half is AdvancedAE (the Reaction Chamber and everything quantum)."
		"&eTip:&r ExtendedAE changes a few AdvancedAE recipes to use its own parts, so check JEI rather than an online wiki."
	]
	quest.32EB70759DD2D747.title: "Fluix Block"
	quest.32EB70759DD2D747.quest_subtitle: "The soil entro grows in"
	quest.32EB70759DD2D747.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r four fluix crystals make a fluix block. Planted with an entro seed, it becomes budding entro."
		"&eHow:&r four fluix crystals in a square (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.68089090A4D213E6.title: "Entro Crystals"
	quest.68089090A4D213E6.quest_subtitle: "ExtendedAE's own budding crystal"
	quest.68089090A4D213E6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r entro crystals feed every ExtendedAE machine. They grow like certus, from Budding Entroized Fluix."
		"&eHow:&r craft Entro Seeds (sand, ender dust, redstone, glowstone, sky dust), then right-click a placed Fluix Block with a seed to make it budding. Harvest the clusters."
		"&eTip:&r Growth Accelerators work on budding entro too."
	]
	quest.7C665ABE9D83ED81.title: "Note: Cells That Aren't Storage"
	quest.7C665ABE9D83ED81.quest_subtitle: "Some cells delete, some never run dry"
	quest.7C665ABE9D83ED81.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ExtendedAE has cells that don't store anything: one that destroys what it's sent, and ones that supply water or cobblestone without end."
		"&eHow:&r both go in an ordinary ME Drive. Click to continue."
	]
	quest.7EF291158B90A46F.title: "ME Void Cell"
	quest.7EF291158B90A46F.quest_subtitle: "Trash, matter balls or singularities"
	quest.7EF291158B90A46F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a cell that destroys what you send it. Its modes delete items, turn them into Matter Balls, or compress them into Singularities."
		"&eChemistry:&r in the real world matter is never destroyed in a chemical reaction; it only rearranges. This cell ignores that law."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Partition it to cobblestone in a Cell Workbench and put it in a drive."
		"&eTip:&r on Singularity mode it replaces the Matter Condenser for AdvancedAE and MEGA's singularity needs."
	]
	quest.5980872F288762DC.title: "Infinity Cell"
	quest.5980872F288762DC.quest_subtitle: "Water or cobblestone, forever"
	quest.5980872F288762DC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an infinity cell reports an endless stock of water or cobblestone to the network. Either one counts."
		"&eChemistry:&r water (H₂O) is the most-used solvent in this pack: electrolysis, the Bayer process, acid dilution. Never running out of it is a quiet luxury."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Put it in a drive; autocrafting pulls from it like any cell."
	]
	quest.66ED4FE9373A352B.title: "Crystal Assembler"
	quest.66ED4FE9373A352B.quest_subtitle: "A crafting machine for AE2 parts"
	quest.66ED4FE9373A352B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Crystal Assembler makes ExtendedAE's blocks from several items (and sometimes a fluid) at once."
		"&eHow:&r crush entro to dust in the Inscriber, drop it in water with a gold ingot and lapis for an entro ingot, then build a Machine Frame and the Assembler (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r it accepts pipes and patterns, so the network can drive it like any other machine."
	]
	quest.33967F89E0530A95.title: "Extended Blocks"
	quest.33967F89E0530A95.quest_subtitle: "Any one bigger version of an AE2 block"
	quest.33967F89E0530A95.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ExtendedAE's 'Ex' blocks are larger versions of AE2's: the Extended Pattern Provider holds many more patterns, the Extended Drive many more cells, and so on."
		"&eHow:&r made in the Crystal Assembler from the normal block plus concurrent processors (check JEI). Any one of them counts."
		"&eTip:&r one extended provider can feed a whole row of chemical reactors."
	]
	quest.261AE8C2C2D39AC5.title: "Extended Pattern Access"
	quest.261AE8C2C2D39AC5.quest_subtitle: "Every pattern, searchable"
	quest.261AE8C2C2D39AC5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Extended Pattern Access Terminal lists every pattern provider on the network with search and filters."
		"&eHow:&r a Pattern Access Terminal upgraded in the Crystal Assembler (check JEI). A wireless version exists too."
		"&eTip:&r name your pattern providers in an anvil (Sulfuric Acid, Polyethylene) and the terminal groups them by name."
	]
	quest.6A53C98F6B5D669D.title: "Circuit Slicer"
	quest.6A53C98F6B5D669D.quest_subtitle: "A storage block into nine prints"
	quest.6A53C98F6B5D669D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Circuit Slicer cuts a whole block (gold, diamond, silicon, certus) into nine printed circuits at once."
		"&eHow:&r made in the Crystal Assembler (check JEI). Put the matching press in and feed it blocks."
		"&eTip:&r a silicon block becomes nine printed silicon. That's an MI ingot line feeding AE2 nine at a time."
	]
	quest.61E774E4778CD356.title: "ME Canner"
	quest.61E774E4778CD356.quest_subtitle: "Fill and empty containers for autocrafting"
	quest.61E774E4778CD356.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the ME Canner fills buckets, cells and other containers from the network, or empties them back in."
		"&eChemistry:&r many recipes still ask for a bucket of acid. The canner means the network can hand over 1,000 mB of H₂SO₄ in a bucket without you."
		"&eHow:&r made in the Crystal Assembler (check JEI). Set Fill or Empty mode in its GUI and give it patterns through a provider."
	]
	quest.671135248AAD6760.title: "Wireless Connectors"
	quest.671135248AAD6760.quest_subtitle: "Cables through thin air"
	quest.671135248AAD6760.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a pair of Wireless Connectors links two parts of your network without a cable between them. The Setup Kit binds them."
		"&eHow:&r connectors come two at a time from the Crystal Assembler; the kit too (check JEI). Use the kit on one end, then the other."
		"&eTip:&r great for reaching a reactor room behind thick shielding."
	]
	quest.3785AD22B4BFBE03.title: "Wireless Hub"
	quest.3785AD22B4BFBE03.quest_subtitle: "Many wireless links, one block"
	quest.3785AD22B4BFBE03.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the ME Wireless Hub takes many wireless links at one point."
		"&eHow:&r from the Crystal Assembler (check JEI). Bind each connector to it with the Setup Kit."
		"&eTip:&r one hub in the middle of your base, linked out to every outpost room."
	]
	quest.3F280E221B8CB5BE.title: "Crystal Fixer"
	quest.3F280E221B8CB5BE.quest_subtitle: "Keep budding crystals budding"
	quest.3F280E221B8CB5BE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r budding entro and certus decay as they grow clusters. The Crystal Fixer restores them with fresh material."
		"&eHow:&r from the Crystal Assembler (check JEI). Put it next to a budding block and give it what its GUI asks for."
		"&eTip:&r one fixer keeps both farms alive."
	]
	quest.5D65AF6211578AC7.title: "Active Formation Plane"
	quest.5D65AF6211578AC7.quest_subtitle: "Push items into whatever is in front"
	quest.5D65AF6211578AC7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r ExtendedAE's plane inserts items straight into the inventory it faces instead of dropping them."
		"&eHow:&r a formation plane upgraded with ExtendedAE parts (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r handy for filling machines that don't accept a storage bus."
	]
	quest.7A9D33953F39D9E9.title: "Concurrent Processors"
	quest.7A9D33953F39D9E9.quest_subtitle: "Optional: ExtendedAE's own processor"
	quest.7A9D33953F39D9E9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r concurrent processors go into nearly every Extended block: drives, providers, interfaces, inscribers and chargers."
		"&eHow:&r build the Concurrent Press in the Crystal Assembler, inscribe entro crystals with it, then assemble the prints with printed silicon and redstone (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the Crystal Assembler can also make AE2's normal processors from their prints."
	]
	quest.3A03AD5658BF5053.title: "Extended Inscriber and Charger"
	quest.3A03AD5658BF5053.quest_subtitle: "Optional: process several stacks at once"
	quest.3A03AD5658BF5053.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Extended Inscriber and Extended Charger work on several items in parallel, so processors and charged certus stop being a bottleneck."
		"&eHow:&r a normal Inscriber or Charger plus capacity cards and a concurrent processor, in the Crystal Assembler (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.64B349EC2D6CA5B6.title: "Extended Interface and IO Port"
	quest.64B349EC2D6CA5B6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: more slots, faster cell transfers"
	quest.64B349EC2D6CA5B6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Extended Interface stocks many more item types than a normal one. The Extended IO Port empties and fills cells far faster."
		"&eHow:&r both from the Crystal Assembler (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r an Extended Interface next to an MI machine can hold every input that machine needs."
	]
	quest.7231154AB582EF98.title: "Smarter Buses"
	quest.7231154AB582EF98.quest_subtitle: "Optional: filter by tag, switch with a margin"
	quest.7231154AB582EF98.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Tag Storage Bus filters by item tag, so one bus can accept every dust or every ingot. The Threshold Level Emitter turns on at one amount and off at another."
		"&eHow:&r a storage bus or level emitter plus processors (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a threshold emitter on an MI Electrolyzer stops it flickering: on below 10,000 mB of hydrogen, off above 50,000 mB."
	]
	quest.3770AEAFDC83097B.title: "Assembler Matrix Shell"
	quest.3770AEAFDC83097B.quest_subtitle: "The box around a thousand crafters"
	quest.3770AEAFDC83097B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Assembler Matrix is a multiblock that replaces walls of molecular assemblers. This is its shell: frames on the edges, walls or glass on the faces."
		"&eHow:&r both from the Crystal Assembler (check JEI). The counts here are enough for a full-size shell."
		"&eTip:&r glass faces let you watch the crafters work; walls are cheaper."
	]
	quest.167FA55B833918AF.title: "Filling the Matrix"
	quest.167FA55B833918AF.quest_subtitle: "Patterns, crafters and speed cores"
	quest.167FA55B833918AF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Thirty-five hands working as one. You remember having more, but this is a start.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r pattern cores hold the patterns, crafter cores do the work in parallel, and speed cores make each job finish sooner."
		"&eHow:&r all from the Crystal Assembler with concurrent processors and entro (check JEI). They go inside the shell."
		"&eTip:&r it's for crafting-table recipes only. Processing patterns for MI machines still need pattern providers."
	]
	quest.0F4FABC8FB5268DF.title: "Into AdvancedAE"
	quest.0F4FABC8FB5268DF.quest_subtitle: "It starts with a logic processor"
	quest.0F4FABC8FB5268DF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r AdvancedAE's first machines and its pattern provider all need logic processors. Bring one to begin."
		"&eHow:&r the Inscriber, as on the Applied Energistics page."
	]
	quest.7FFFA15128FCBD88.title: "Reaction Chamber"
	quest.7FFFA15128FCBD88.quest_subtitle: "AdvancedAE's powered reactor"
	quest.7FFFA15128FCBD88.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r AdvancedAE's Reaction Chamber combines items and a fluid with lots of energy. Its first job: shattering singularities."
		"&eHow:&r a matter condenser, a vibration chamber, fluix dust, glowstone and a bucket (check JEI). Feed it a singularity, ender dust, sky dust and lava."
		"&eTip:&r it uses a lot of power per craft. Put it on its own Energy Acceptor."
	]
	quest.4FBB5D1C1A7FC218.title: "Directional Providers"
	quest.4FBB5D1C1A7FC218.quest_subtitle: "Send each ingredient to the right face"
	quest.4FBB5D1C1A7FC218.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Advanced Pattern Provider lets a processing pattern send each input to a chosen side of the machine. The Advanced Pattern Encoder writes the sides onto the pattern."
		"&eHow:&r an Extended Pattern Provider, a logic processor, an ender pearl and redstone for the provider (check JEI for both)."
		"&eTip:&r a Mekanism PRC takes items, a fluid and a gas on different sides: perfect for this."
	]
	quest.43A72FAC8EB012CB.title: "Quantum Materials"
	quest.43A72FAC8EB012CB.quest_subtitle: "Shattered singularity, quantum alloy, quantum processor"
	quest.43A72FAC8EB012CB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the three materials behind everything quantum: a shattered singularity, quantum alloy, and the quantum processor printed on it."
		"&eChemistry:&r copper is the alloy's base for a reason: after silver it's the best electrical conductor of any metal."
		"&eHow:&r shatter a singularity in the Reaction Chamber; react quantum infusion with copper ingots and singularities for the alloy; press it with the Quantum Press (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r copy the Quantum Press before you use it in automation, like the other presses."
	]
	quest.7090BF1A6ACCFCD5.title: "Encoding Directions"
	quest.7090BF1A6ACCFCD5.quest_subtitle: "Optional: pick a face for each ingredient"
	quest.7090BF1A6ACCFCD5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the encoder adds side information to a processing pattern."
		"&eHow:&r put a pattern in, set each input's side, and take it out. Click JEI for the recipe."
		"&eTip:&r keep one next to your Pattern Encoding Terminal."
	]
	quest.39E28A8F48D7260F.title: "A Stack of Quantum Processors"
	quest.39E28A8F48D7260F.quest_subtitle: "Optional: you'll need more than one"
	quest.39E28A8F48D7260F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r quantum processors go into the Quantum Computer's parts, quantum gear and AdvancedAE's best buses."
		"&eHow:&r inscribe quantum alloy with the Quantum Press, then add redstone and printed silicon (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.6DD6D25D57D8A0BA.title: "Quantum Unit and Structure"
	quest.6DD6D25D57D8A0BA.quest_subtitle: "The bricks of the computer"
	quest.6DD6D25D57D8A0BA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Quantum Structure blocks make the computer's shell; Quantum Crafting Units fill its inside."
		"&eHow:&r both need quantum alloy and shattered singularities (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.4A0F9E21A373D41D.title: "Quantum Storage"
	quest.4A0F9E21A373D41D.quest_subtitle: "How big a job it can plan"
	quest.4A0F9E21A373D41D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r quantum storage blocks set how big a crafting job the computer can hold in mind."
		"&eHow:&r a quantum unit plus storage components (check JEI; ExtendedAE changes a few recipes)."
		"&eTip:&r storage first: a long chemical chain fails to plan long before it runs short of threads."
	]
	quest.67E3FD336B87FEF7.title: "Quantum Accelerator"
	quest.67E3FD336B87FEF7.quest_subtitle: "More jobs in parallel"
	quest.67E3FD336B87FEF7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each Quantum Accelerator lets the computer run more crafting steps at once."
		"&eHow:&r a quantum unit, quantum processors and shattered singularities (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.423E95AFA4363CFD.title: "Quantum Core"
	quest.423E95AFA4363CFD.quest_subtitle: "The archive learns to think"
	quest.423E95AFA4363CFD.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember thinking a thousand thoughts at once. The machine remembers how, too.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the Quantum Core is the heart of the Quantum Computer: a multiblock crafting CPU with huge storage and many parallel jobs."
		"&eHow:&r the core goes inside a shell of Quantum Structure, with units, accelerators and storage around it (check JEI for size limits)."
		"&eTip:&r build it next to your main pattern providers so every chemical line can run at once."
	]
	quest.364796E1E2BDF89E.title: "Multi-Threader"
	quest.364796E1E2BDF89E.quest_subtitle: "Multiply the accelerators"
	quest.364796E1E2BDF89E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Multi-Threader multiplies what each accelerator in the computer adds."
		"&eHow:&r quantum parts and ExtendedAE's components (check JEI). Only a few fit in one computer."
	]
	quest.45B43718DAF8FF7C.title: "Data Entangler"
	quest.45B43718DAF8FF7C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: multiply the computer's memory"
	quest.45B43718DAF8FF7C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Quantum Data Entangler multiplies the whole computer's storage. Only a few fit in one multiblock."
		"&eHow:&r quantum storage, quantum units and shattered singularities (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r one entangler is usually enough for the Seed of a New World chain."
	]
	quest.641030E10A5328A9.title: "Quantum Crafter"
	quest.641030E10A5328A9.quest_subtitle: "An assembler that keeps stock"
	quest.641030E10A5328A9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Quantum Crafter crafts patterns over and over with no CPU, keeping a set amount in stock."
		"&eHow:&r quantum accelerators, a quantum unit, 64k components and shattered singularities (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r set it to keep plates and wires in stock; the CPU stays free for the long chains."
	]
	quest.3A886C92BDB18F98.title: "The Full Quantum Computer"
	quest.3A886C92BDB18F98.quest_subtitle: "Challenge: the largest computer the mod allows"
	quest.3A886C92BDB18F98.quest_desc: [
		"&6Every reaction you ever learned, planned at once. You remember being this.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r the materials for a maximum-size Quantum Computer: a full shell, a hundred accelerators, the core and a multi-threader."
		"&eHow:&r it's a lot of shattered singularities. Automate the Reaction Chamber and the Condenser (or a Void Cell on Singularity mode) first."
		"&eTip:&r you don't need the full size to finish the pack. This is for the archive's own sake."
	]
	quest.007EDC75C12A0DBE.title: "Quantum Armour"
	quest.007EDC75C12A0DBE.quest_subtitle: "Armour wired into the network"
	quest.007EDC75C12A0DBE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r quantum armour is netherite armour rebuilt around quantum processors, with slots for AdvancedAE's armour cards."
		"&eHow:&r each piece needs its netherite piece, quantum alloy plates, quantum processors and a quantum storage component (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r flight in this pack comes from chemistry (pylons, jetpacks, the Angel Ring), not from AE2, so no quest asks for the Flight Card."
	]
	quest.139AEA4F1FC0C461.title: "Quantum Upgrade Base"
	quest.139AEA4F1FC0C461.quest_subtitle: "The blank behind every armour card"
	quest.139AEA4F1FC0C461.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the blank card that every Quantum Armour card is built on."
		"&eHow:&r a quantum alloy plate surrounded by quantum processors (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.396979F7EE253206.title: "Walk Speed Card"
	quest.396979F7EE253206.quest_subtitle: "Faster on your feet"
	quest.396979F7EE253206.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r you walk faster while wearing the armour."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
		"&eTip:&r stack it with Sprint Speed for crossing big bases."
	]
	quest.04286565C91F3DD1.title: "Sprint Speed Card"
	quest.04286565C91F3DD1.quest_subtitle: "Faster when you run"
	quest.04286565C91F3DD1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r sprinting is faster again."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
	]
	quest.737C2EC52786A3EF.title: "Step Assist Card"
	quest.737C2EC52786A3EF.quest_subtitle: "Walk up blocks"
	quest.737C2EC52786A3EF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r you step up full blocks without jumping, like a horse."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
	]
	quest.79C3F069718302D8.title: "Jump Height Card"
	quest.79C3F069718302D8.quest_subtitle: "Higher jumps"
	quest.79C3F069718302D8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r you jump higher."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
	]
	quest.6B8A805FA8C7C36A.title: "Lava Immunity Card"
	quest.6B8A805FA8C7C36A.quest_subtitle: "Swim in the Nether's oceans"
	quest.6B8A805FA8C7C36A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r lava doesn't burn you."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
		"&eTip:&r it doesn't stop fall damage into a lava lake. Look before you leap."
	]
	quest.391861EB18907448.title: "Water Breathing Card"
	quest.391861EB18907448.quest_subtitle: "No more air bar"
	quest.391861EB18907448.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r you breathe underwater."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
	]
	quest.723C700E1EB65325.title: "Auto Feeding Card"
	quest.723C700E1EB65325.quest_subtitle: "Eat from the network"
	quest.723C700E1EB65325.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r when you're hungry the armour feeds you from the ME network."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
		"&eTip:&r stock a farm's output in the network."
	]
	quest.73F370C7AE3B8E6E.title: "Auto Stock Card"
	quest.73F370C7AE3B8E6E.quest_subtitle: "Your inventory refills itself"
	quest.73F370C7AE3B8E6E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r keeps chosen items stocked in your inventory from the network."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
		"&eTip:&r torches, scaffolding and food, forever."
	]
	quest.6E6993C23E508954.title: "Magnet Card"
	quest.6E6993C23E508954.quest_subtitle: "Pull in nearby drops"
	quest.6E6993C23E508954.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r nearby dropped items fly to you."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
		"&eTip:&r pair it with Auto Stock and you rarely visit storage at all."
	]
	quest.149697C62123CCCA.title: "HP Buffer Card"
	quest.149697C62123CCCA.quest_subtitle: "Extra health"
	quest.149697C62123CCCA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r adds extra health while worn."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
	]
	quest.2197066315C2C358.title: "Evasion Card"
	quest.2197066315C2C358.quest_subtitle: "A chance to dodge"
	quest.2197066315C2C358.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r gives a chance to dodge an attack entirely."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
	]
	quest.6C886D3146E602CC.title: "Regeneration Card"
	quest.6C886D3146E602CC.quest_subtitle: "Heal over time"
	quest.6C886D3146E602CC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r you slowly regenerate health."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
	]
	quest.2E8BFCC6100A35E9.title: "Strength Card"
	quest.2E8BFCC6100A35E9.quest_subtitle: "Hit harder"
	quest.2E8BFCC6100A35E9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r your attacks deal more damage."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
	]
	quest.02D1F277E62BD8BE.title: "Attack Speed Card"
	quest.02D1F277E62BD8BE.quest_subtitle: "Swing faster"
	quest.02D1F277E62BD8BE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r your weapon recovers faster between swings."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
	]
	quest.36DD71A1A6D46CB4.title: "Luck Card"
	quest.36DD71A1A6D46CB4.quest_subtitle: "Better loot"
	quest.36DD71A1A6D46CB4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r adds luck, which improves loot rolls and fishing."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
	]
	quest.2651676FFBA9363C.title: "Reach Card"
	quest.2651676FFBA9363C.quest_subtitle: "Longer arms"
	quest.2651676FFBA9363C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r you can reach blocks and entities further away."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
	]
	quest.361D54C23901F38C.title: "Swim Speed Card"
	quest.361D54C23901F38C.quest_subtitle: "Faster in water"
	quest.361D54C23901F38C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r you swim faster."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
	]
	quest.427BBF7D63793D17.title: "Night Vision Card"
	quest.427BBF7D63793D17.quest_subtitle: "See in the dark"
	quest.427BBF7D63793D17.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r permanent night vision while worn."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
	]
	quest.23B449C618C4A120.title: "ME Recharging Card"
	quest.23B449C618C4A120.quest_subtitle: "Charge from the network"
	quest.23B449C618C4A120.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the armour recharges itself from the ME network's energy."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
	]
	quest.15777B39559E9C54.title: "Portable Workbench Card"
	quest.15777B39559E9C54.quest_subtitle: "A crafting grid on the go"
	quest.15777B39559E9C54.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r opens a crafting grid from the armour."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
	]
	quest.5A6453F596488595.title: "Pick Craft Card"
	quest.5A6453F596488595.quest_subtitle: "Order what you look at"
	quest.5A6453F596488595.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r middle-clicking a block you don't have orders it from your autocrafting."
		"&eHow:&r a Quantum Upgrade Base plus a few items (check JEI). Install it in a quantum armour piece's GUI."
	]
	chapter.6A576761B258CEBA.title: "Automation and Logic"
	chapter.6A576761B258CEBA.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Make the factory run itself."
	]
	quest.0FAEFFEE3AF43096.title: "Moving Things Around"
	quest.0FAEFFEE3AF43096.quest_subtitle: "Any wrench opens the logistics page"
	quest.0FAEFFEE3AF43096.quest_desc: [
		"&6You never carried your own buckets. You remember things flowing to where you wanted them.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r this page is every way the pack moves items, fluids, gases and power: Pipez, Mekanism transmitters, Integrated Dynamics, LaserIO, and a few extras."
		"&eHow:&r any of the logistics wrenches counts: Pipez, Integrated Dynamics, LaserIO, the Mekanism Configurator, Powah or Modern Industrialization."
		"&eTip:&r start with Pipez. It is cheap, it works early, and you can swap it for something cleverer later."
	]
	quest.0C721CC0F004F7C2.title: "Pipez"
	quest.0C721CC0F004F7C2.quest_subtitle: "Simple pipes, one for each job"
	quest.0C721CC0F004F7C2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Pipez has a pipe for each thing that moves, and the Pipe Wrench to cut and rejoin pipe sides."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the wrench. Sneak-click where a pipe meets a machine to make that end extract."
		"&eTip:&r Pipez only pulls from ends you set to extract, so connecting a pipe to a machine never drains it by accident."
	]
	quest.634FAF5A40A5A4C3.title: "Item Pipes"
	quest.634FAF5A40A5A4C3.quest_subtitle: "Ore in one end, ingots out the other"
	quest.634FAF5A40A5A4C3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the item pipe moves stacks between inventories."
		"&eHow:&r iron and redstone (check JEI). Set the machine end to extract with the wrench or by sneak-clicking."
		"&eTip:&r one pipe line can feed a whole row of furnaces; items go to the nearest free one first."
	]
	quest.1BD7920FD8476E10.title: "Fluid Pipes"
	quest.1BD7920FD8476E10.quest_subtitle: "Water, acids and fuels"
	quest.1BD7920FD8476E10.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the fluid pipe moves liquids: water to boilers, acid to reactors, fuel to generators."
		"&eChemistry:&r a pipe of sulfuric acid in real life is lined with PTFE or glass, because H₂SO₄ eats most metals. Pipez is kinder."
		"&eHow:&r iron and redstone with a bucket (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r keep one fluid per pipe line, or the first fluid in blocks the rest."
	]
	quest.640DFFA9810B358A.title: "Energy Pipes"
	quest.640DFFA9810B358A.quest_subtitle: "FE from generator to machine"
	quest.640DFFA9810B358A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the energy pipe carries FE (Forge Energy), the power most mods share."
		"&eHow:&r iron and redstone with a redstone block (check JEI). Extract from the generator side."
		"&eTip:&r MI machines run on EU, not FE. Use MI cables for those."
	]
	quest.787F558E65CB4582.title: "Universal Pipe"
	quest.787F558E65CB4582.quest_subtitle: "One pipe, all the jobs"
	quest.787F558E65CB4582.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Universal Pipe carries several kinds of thing at once in one line (its tooltip lists which)."
		"&eHow:&r item, fluid and energy pipes with iron and a redstone block (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r set each side's mode per type in its GUI, so one pipe can feed a machine items and power together."
	]
	quest.52A98D42EC341D44.title: "Gas Pipes"
	quest.52A98D42EC341D44.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism chemicals by pipe"
	quest.52A98D42EC341D44.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the gas pipe moves Mekanism chemicals: hydrogen, oxygen, chlorine, SO₂ and the rest."
		"&eChemistry:&r keep H₂ and Cl₂ in separate lines: mixed and lit, they react explosively (H₂ + Cl₂ → 2HCl)."
		"&eHow:&r iron and redstone with infused alloy (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.63CD285F0798C754.title: "Filter Destination Tool"
	quest.63CD285F0798C754.quest_subtitle: "Aim a filter at one inventory"
	quest.63CD285F0798C754.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r this tool picks the one inventory a filter sends its items to."
		"&eHow:&r right-click the target block with the tool, then click the filter entry in the pipe's GUI (check JEI for the recipe)."
		"&eTip:&r useful when two furnaces sit on one line but only one should get the coal."
	]
	quest.1C06634BCA2F3595.title: "Pipe Upgrades"
	quest.1C06634BCA2F3595.quest_subtitle: "Faster pipes with filters and modes"
	quest.1C06634BCA2F3595.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r upgrades raise a pipe end's speed and unlock filters, redstone modes and round-robin. Any tier counts."
		"&eHow:&r each tier is the one before plus better materials (check JEI). Put it in the extracting end."
		"&eTip:&r round-robin spreads ore evenly across a row of machines."
	]
	quest.5FCCF59FEB0822A1.title: "Mekanism Transport"
	quest.5FCCF59FEB0822A1.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Configurator"
	quest.5FCCF59FEB0822A1.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Configurator\" on the Mekanism page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.3310B1BAFA7C7EAB.title: "Mechanical Pipes"
	quest.3310B1BAFA7C7EAB.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Mechanical Pipes"
	quest.3310B1BAFA7C7EAB.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Mechanical Pipes\" on the Mekanism page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.364DBD9E21BAEB32.title: "Universal Cables"
	quest.364DBD9E21BAEB32.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Universal Cable"
	quest.364DBD9E21BAEB32.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Universal Cable\" on the Mekanism page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.13C80C7E7AB60184.title: "Logistical Transporters"
	quest.13C80C7E7AB60184.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Logistical Transporters"
	quest.13C80C7E7AB60184.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Logistical Transporters\" on the Mekanism page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.1855FB6EDE874D50.title: "Thermodynamic Conductors"
	quest.1855FB6EDE874D50.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Thermodynamic Conductors"
	quest.1855FB6EDE874D50.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Thermodynamic Conductors\" on the Mekanism page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.23D69B0EA35D99A6.title: "Pressurized Tubes"
	quest.23D69B0EA35D99A6.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Pressurized Tubes"
	quest.23D69B0EA35D99A6.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Pressurized Tubes\" on the Mekanism page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.656CCB48225718F9.title: "Integrated Dynamics"
	quest.656CCB48225718F9.quest_subtitle: "Logic networks built from resin"
	quest.656CCB48225718F9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Integrated Dynamics reads values from the world (tank levels, item counts), applies logic, and acts on them. Integrated Tunnels uses the same cables to move things. The Menril wrench rotates and removes ID blocks and parts."
		"&eHow:&r Menril chunks and redstone (check JEI). The mod's own book, On the Dynamics of Integration, has worked examples."
		"&eTip:&r the resin line that makes Menril chunks is on the Integrated Dynamics page."
	]
	quest.53D012374749B94D.title: "Logic Cables"
	quest.53D012374749B94D.quest_subtitle: "The wiring for every part"
	quest.53D012374749B94D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r logic cables join readers, writers, importers and exporters into one network."
		"&eHow:&r crystalized Menril chunks and redstone (check JEI). Parts go on the side of a cable."
		"&eTip:&r use the wrench on a cable side to cut it, so two networks next to each other stay apart."
	]
	quest.26C77FC1CE6AC1B7.title: "Variable Cards"
	quest.26C77FC1CE6AC1B7.quest_subtitle: "A card that holds a value or a rule"
	quest.26C77FC1CE6AC1B7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a variable card stores one thing: a number, a yes/no, an item, or a rule built in the Logic Programmer."
		"&eHow:&r Menril chunks around redstone (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r make a stack. Every reader value and every exporter rule wants its own card."
	]
	quest.2D9AFA2141A6E02F.title: "Items by Logic"
	quest.2D9AFA2141A6E02F.quest_subtitle: "Importer in, interface out"
	quest.2D9AFA2141A6E02F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an Item Importer pulls items into the network; an Item Interface lets the network's items be reached from a chest or machine."
		"&eHow:&r put both on cables (check JEI for the parts). The importer takes a variable card that says what to move."
		"&eTip:&r with no card, an importer moves everything. Add a card when you want it picky."
	]
	quest.1C556EC0AD6B56D0.title: "Fluids by Logic"
	quest.1C556EC0AD6B56D0.quest_subtitle: "Tanks joined by cable"
	quest.1C556EC0AD6B56D0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the fluid versions of the importer and interface."
		"&eChemistry:&r an exporter that only runs while a tank reader says 'below 50%' is a simple feedback loop, the same idea as a float valve in a cistern."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for both parts; place them on cables against tanks and machines."
	]
	quest.28C9F3C3697312D2.title: "Energy by Logic"
	quest.28C9F3C3697312D2.quest_subtitle: "Power along the same cables"
	quest.28C9F3C3697312D2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r energy importers and interfaces move FE through logic cables."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Pull from a generator or battery, push out at a machine."
		"&eTip:&r a redstone variable can switch power to a whole wing of the base on and off."
	]
	quest.51734E649209B091.title: "LaserIO"
	quest.51734E649209B091.quest_subtitle: "Move things through the air"
	quest.51734E649209B091.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r LaserIO nodes sit on machines and pass items, fluids, chemicals, power and redstone along lasers. Logic chips go into every node and card."
		"&eHow:&r raw logic chips are a quartz block, clay, gold nuggets and redstone (4 at a time); smelt them."
		"&eTip:&r one node can serve all six sides of the block it touches."
	]
	quest.7E444AD0C3399678.title: "Laser Wrench"
	quest.7E444AD0C3399678.quest_subtitle: "Click one node, then the other"
	quest.7E444AD0C3399678.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Laser Wrench links nodes together."
		"&eHow:&r iron and a logic chip (check JEI). Click the first node, then the second."
		"&eTip:&r sneak-click a node with the wrench to unlink it."
	]
	quest.5607D234E6EF1000.title: "Laser Nodes"
	quest.5607D234E6EF1000.quest_subtitle: "One per machine"
	quest.5607D234E6EF1000.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a node sits against a machine and holds the cards for each of its sides."
		"&eHow:&r glass, iron, redstone and a logic chip (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r right-click a node to open its six side slots."
	]
	quest.6912F21E0B5211B5.title: "Basic Filter"
	quest.6912F21E0B5211B5.quest_subtitle: "Only these items, please"
	quest.6912F21E0B5211B5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r filters go inside cards. The basic filter matches the items you list."
		"&eHow:&r put the filter in a card's filter slot and set it up."
		"&eTip:&r flip it to deny mode to send everything except the listed items."
	]
	quest.408A259A993527E2.title: "Item Cards"
	quest.408A259A993527E2.quest_subtitle: "Configure what each node moves"
	quest.408A259A993527E2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r cards tell each node what to move and in which direction."
		"&eHow:&r put a card in a node's side slot. Set it to Extract on the source and Insert on the destination."
		"&eTip:&r right-click with a card in your hand to open its settings."
	]
	quest.441C3C6BBF44735C.title: "Fluid Cards"
	quest.441C3C6BBF44735C.quest_subtitle: "Move acids without pipes"
	quest.441C3C6BBF44735C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fluid cards move liquids between nodes."
		"&eHow:&r same as item cards: Extract on the tank, Insert on the machine."
		"&eTip:&r one node can run several cards on one side."
	]
	quest.54D4BBC0F664CD9C.title: "Energy Cards"
	quest.54D4BBC0F664CD9C.quest_subtitle: "Power by laser"
	quest.54D4BBC0F664CD9C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r energy cards move FE between nodes."
		"&eHow:&r a logic chip with quartz, gold nuggets and a redstone block (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a node on your battery and one on each machine replaces a whole cable run."
	]
	quest.159509C240B9CCA6.title: "Redstone Cards"
	quest.159509C240B9CCA6.quest_subtitle: "Signals along the laser network"
	quest.159509C240B9CCA6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r redstone cards read a signal at one node and send it out at another."
		"&eHow:&r a logic chip with redstone (check JEI). Set channels to pair senders and receivers."
		"&eTip:&r switch a separator on only while the sulfur chest has stock."
	]
	quest.2B63B37E93792141.title: "Chemical Cards"
	quest.2B63B37E93792141.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism gases by laser"
	quest.2B63B37E93792141.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r chemical cards move Mekanism chemicals: hydrogen, oxygen, SO₂, slurries."
		"&eChemistry:&r a separator splits water 2H₂O → 2H₂ + O₂. Two chemical cards on one node carry both gases off to different machines."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the recipe; set Extract and Insert like any card."
	]
	quest.13955ABB5B1AFAB1.title: "Card Holder"
	quest.13955ABB5B1AFAB1.quest_subtitle: "Optional: spare cards on your belt"
	quest.13955ABB5B1AFAB1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Card Holder carries spare cards and filters and fills nodes from your inventory."
		"&eHow:&r a logic chip in iron with a chest (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r keep one of each card type in it while you wire a new line."
	]
	quest.04F765422F690B3A.title: "Card Cloner"
	quest.04F765422F690B3A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: copy one card's settings"
	quest.04F765422F690B3A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Card Cloner copies one card's settings onto others."
		"&eHow:&r a logic chip in iron with paper (check JEI). Sneak-click a card to copy, click another to paste."
		"&eTip:&r clone one tuned acid card to every reactor in the line."
	]
	quest.04A637B2AB0653E9.title: "Laser Connector"
	quest.04A637B2AB0653E9.quest_subtitle: "Optional: relay lasers round corners"
	quest.04A637B2AB0653E9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a connector relays lasers between nodes without holding cards."
		"&eHow:&r glass, redstone, iron and a logic chip (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r nodes link up to a set range; connectors let you go round corners and through walls."
	]
	quest.4FD8CA290EB68642.title: "Count Filter"
	quest.4FD8CA290EB68642.quest_subtitle: "Keep exactly this many in stock"
	quest.4FD8CA290EB68642.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the count filter tops a machine up to a set number and stops."
		"&eHow:&r a basic filter with a comparator (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r 64 sulfur in the oxidizer and no more: the rest stays in storage for other lines."
	]
	quest.78D4B87EDD7C898D.title: "Tag Filter"
	quest.78D4B87EDD7C898D.quest_subtitle: "Every dust, every ingot"
	quest.78D4B87EDD7C898D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the tag filter matches whole tags, like c:dusts or c:ores."
		"&eHow:&r a basic filter with a name tag or paper (check JEI). Type the tag in its screen."
		"&eTip:&r one tag filter on c:raw_materials sends every raw ore to your processing line."
	]
	quest.73D64B4A0CA4BB01.title: "Mod Filter"
	quest.73D64B4A0CA4BB01.quest_subtitle: "Everything from one mod"
	quest.73D64B4A0CA4BB01.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the mod filter matches every item from the mod of the item you show it."
		"&eHow:&r a basic filter plus a book (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r route all ChemLib items to the lab store with one card."
	]
	quest.43C31D71C7FEB6D8.title: "Card Overclocker"
	quest.43C31D71C7FEB6D8.quest_subtitle: "Optional: bigger batches per card"
	quest.43C31D71C7FEB6D8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r card overclockers raise how much one card moves per trip."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI; it goes in a card's upgrade slot."
		"&eTip:&r most lines don't need it. Add it when a machine starves."
	]
	quest.4B7800B2F32F2DD9.title: "Node Overclocker"
	quest.4B7800B2F32F2DD9.quest_subtitle: "Optional: faster nodes"
	quest.4B7800B2F32F2DD9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r node overclockers make a node act more often."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI; it goes in the node's upgrade slot."
		"&eTip:&r pair a fast node with an overclocked card for the busiest machine in a line."
	]
	quest.140C58A0A3A11DB7.title: "A Computer"
	quest.140C58A0A3A11DB7.quest_subtitle: "Optional: Lua, in a box"
	quest.140C58A0A3A11DB7.quest_desc: [
		"&6You never did your own chores. You remember having things that did them for you.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r CC: Tweaked computers run Lua programs: monitor tanks, balance chemical lines, build a base dashboard."
		"&eHow:&r place it and right-click. Type &ehelp&r, or &eedit startup&r to write a program that runs on boot."
		"&eTip:&r Mekanism machines can be read by computers directly. Put a computer next to one and try &eperipheral.getNames()&r."
	]
	quest.5860D80382B926CC.title: "Monitors"
	quest.5860D80382B926CC.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a screen for your numbers"
	quest.5860D80382B926CC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r monitors show program output on a wall. Placed together, they join into one big screen."
		"&eHow:&r put monitors next to the computer and run &emonitor <side> <program>&r to send output to them."
		"&eTip:&r advanced monitors show colour and accept clicks, so you can make touch buttons."
	]
	quest.1DC5FA34C818F32E.title: "Wired Networks"
	quest.1DC5FA34C818F32E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: reach machines across the room"
	quest.1DC5FA34C818F32E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r wired modems and networking cable connect a computer to machines that aren't touching it."
		"&eHow:&r put a modem on the machine, run cable back to a modem on the computer, and right-click the machine's modem to attach it."
		"&eTip:&r each attached peripheral gets a name. List them with &eperipheral.getNames()&r."
	]
	quest.67691356C2B16C8D.title: "Ender Modem"
	quest.67691356C2B16C8D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: talk across dimensions"
	quest.67691356C2B16C8D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Ender Modem sends messages with no range limit, even between dimensions. A pocket computer carries a terminal with you."
		"&eHow:&r use &erednet&r on both ends: one computer broadcasts tank levels, your pocket computer reads them."
		"&eTip:&r a remote alarm for your reactor is a very good idea."
	]
	quest.5B44262E5F932D07.title: "Turtles"
	quest.5B44262E5F932D07.quest_subtitle: "Optional: robots you program"
	quest.5B44262E5F932D07.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r turtles are programmable robots that mine, build and farm."
		"&eHow:&r craft one with a tool (a pickaxe makes a mining turtle) and fuel it with coal."
		"&eTip:&r try the built-in &eexcavate&r and &etunnel&r programs first."
	]
	quest.02AEF5F6A8349814.title: "Advanced Peripherals"
	quest.02AEF5F6A8349814.quest_subtitle: "Optional: read power flow and your ME network"
	quest.02AEF5F6A8349814.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r extra peripherals: the Energy Detector measures power flow; the ME Bridge reads (and requests crafts from) your whole AE2 network."
		"&eHow:&r place them on your wired network like any other peripheral."
		"&eTip:&r an ME Bridge program can keep your stock of every intermediate topped up."
	]
	quest.34D7444D271541A3.title: "Base Dashboard"
	quest.34D7444D271541A3.quest_subtitle: "Optional: every tank on one screen"
	quest.34D7444D271541A3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a wall screen that shows your chemical stocks, power and flow rates at a glance."
		"&eHow:&r the Fluid Detector measures flow through a pipe. Combine it with tank readings and the energy detector in one program."
		"&eTip:&r colour lines red when a tank drops below 20%. You'll spot problems from across the room."
	]
	quest.5A5E16639EDFAC93.title: "Printers and Disks"
	quest.5A5E16639EDFAC93.quest_subtitle: "Optional: save programs, print lab notes"
	quest.5A5E16639EDFAC93.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Disk Drive lets you save programs on floppy disks and carry them between computers. A Printer prints text onto paper."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Put a disk in the drive and it appears as &edisk/&r in the computer's files."
		"&eTip:&r print a list of your reactions and their inputs and bind the pages into a book: a real lab notebook."
	]
	quest.6BDC8F1C446B5D65.title: "Advanced Turtle"
	quest.6BDC8F1C446B5D65.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a golden robot with a colour screen"
	quest.6BDC8F1C446B5D65.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r advanced turtles have colour screens and can be clicked, which makes menus easy."
		"&eHow:&r an advanced computer with gold instead of iron around it (check JEI). Give it a pickaxe to make a Mining Turtle."
		"&eTip:&r run &eexcavate 16&r on a mining turtle and it digs a 16x16 hole down to bedrock, bringing everything back."
	]
	quest.7D39CBFAE0AE3E52.title: "Geo Scanner"
	quest.7D39CBFAE0AE3E52.quest_subtitle: "Optional: find ores with a program"
	quest.7D39CBFAE0AE3E52.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Geo Scanner lists every block around it within a radius, including ores, for your computer to read."
		"&eChemistry:&r real geologists find ore bodies by measuring gravity, magnetism and how rocks conduct electricity, rather than digging blind."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Put it next to a computer (or in a pocket computer) and call &escan(8)&r."
		"&eTip:&r write a program that counts ore blocks by type: it's a quick way to check a deposit before setting up a mine."
	]
	quest.6CC389628C143887.title: "Chat Box and Player Detector"
	quest.6CC389628C143887.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a base that talks back"
	quest.6CC389628C143887.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Chat Box lets a computer send chat messages; the Player Detector tells it who is nearby."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Place them next to a computer."
		"&eTip:&r have the base warn everyone in chat when a tank of hydrogen is nearly full or an induction matrix is running low."
	]
	quest.41E9EE7CC03DE9F3.title: "Inventory Manager"
	quest.41E9EE7CC03DE9F3.quest_subtitle: "Optional: programs that use your inventory"
	quest.41E9EE7CC03DE9F3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Inventory Manager lets a computer move items into and out of your own inventory, once you bind it with a Memory Card."
		"&eHow:&r right-click the Memory Card to bind it to yourself, then put it in the manager (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a button that refills your hotbar with torches and food from storage is a classic first program."
	]
	quest.6192AD314EA01958.title: "Buses"
	quest.6192AD314EA01958.quest_subtitle: "AE2 pulls, pushes and reads"
	quest.6192AD314EA01958.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an import bus pulls items out of a machine, an export bus pushes them in, and a storage bus lets ME see inside a chest or tank."
		"&eHow:&r place them on cable facing the machine. Set filters in each bus's GUI."
		"&eTip:&r Applied Mekanistics is in the pack, so buses and storage also handle Mekanism gases like hydrogen and SO₂."
	]
	quest.573035DFFD4A529E.title: "Crafting CPU"
	quest.573035DFFD4A529E.quest_subtitle: "The part of AE2 that plans"
	quest.573035DFFD4A529E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a crafting CPU is a multiblock that works out and tracks autocrafting jobs."
		"&eHow:&r build a solid box of crafting units with at least one crafting storage, and connect it to your network."
		"&eTip:&r more storage lets it plan bigger jobs; co-processing units run more steps at once."
	]
	quest.43797C9ECEA77DF3.title: "Encoding Patterns"
	quest.43797C9ECEA77DF3.quest_subtitle: "Teach AE2 a recipe"
	quest.43797C9ECEA77DF3.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a pattern is a recipe card: these inputs make that output."
		"&eHow:&r in the Pattern Encoding Terminal, switch to Processing mode for machine recipes and fill in the inputs and outputs."
		"&eTip:&r processing patterns work for any machine: MI, Mekanism or the Combiner."
	]
	quest.21A977445D70545D.title: "Autocraft a Chemical Line"
	quest.21A977445D70545D.quest_subtitle: "Pattern providers drive your machines"
	quest.21A977445D70545D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r pattern providers push ingredients into machines; molecular assemblers do crafting-table recipes."
		"&eHow:&r put a provider against an MI or Mekanism machine, load a processing pattern, and send the output back into the network."
		"&eTip:&r chain patterns (sulfur → SO₂ → SO₃ → H₂SO₄) and one request runs the whole line."
	]
	quest.3FEB19A4A1E0D8A4.title: "Level Emitters"
	quest.3FEB19A4A1E0D8A4.quest_subtitle: "Moved: see Level Emitter"
	quest.3FEB19A4A1E0D8A4.quest_desc: [
		"&eMoved:&r this step is now \"Level Emitter\" on the Applied Energistics page. Click to dismiss."
	]
	quest.44221BA2292D178B.title: "Fully Automated Sulfuric Acid"
	quest.44221BA2292D178B.quest_subtitle: "Optional: sulfur in, acid out, no hands"
	quest.44221BA2292D178B.quest_desc: [
		"&6The factory hums without you. You remember this kind of quiet.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r a line that makes sulfuric acid on its own and stops when the tanks are full."
		"&eChemistry:&r 2SO₂ + O₂ → 2SO₃ (industry uses a vanadium oxide catalyst), then SO₃ + H₂O → H₂SO₄."
		"&eHow:&r Separator (O₂) → Oxidizer (S → SO₂) → Infuser (SO₃) → Rotary Condensentrator (water vapour) → Infuser (H₂SO₄). Feed sulfur with a bus or LaserIO and gate it with a level emitter."
		"&eTip:&r when it runs a full day with no help, fill 16 buckets and click the checkmark."
	]
	quest.34D0F3A6001E73F8.title: "Super Factory Manager"
	quest.34D0F3A6001E73F8.quest_subtitle: "Optional: one block scripts the whole factory"
	quest.34D0F3A6001E73F8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r one Manager block runs a short program that moves items, fluids and energy between everything on its cables."
		"&eHow:&r put the disk in the Manager and write a program, e.g. &eEVERY 20 TICKS DO INPUT FROM a OUTPUT TO b END&r."
		"&eTip:&r the in-game editor has examples. Start with one input and one output."
	]
	quest.6DFD0C0EE913BF88.title: "Labels"
	quest.6DFD0C0EE913BF88.quest_subtitle: "Optional: name every machine"
	quest.6DFD0C0EE913BF88.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Label Gun tags inventories with names (like &ea&r and &eb&r above) for your programs."
		"&eHow:&r set a label in the gun, then right-click each machine. The Network Tool shows what's connected."
		"&eTip:&r label by job ('sulfur_in', 'acid_out'), not by machine type."
	]
	quest.648179C70EA53466.title: "Your First SFM Program"
	quest.648179C70EA53466.quest_subtitle: "Optional: four lines that move items"
	quest.648179C70EA53466.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Super Factory Manager runs small text programs written on a disk. Labels name the blocks it talks to."
		"&eHow:&r label a chest &ea&r and a furnace &eb&r with the Label Gun, then write this program on the disk and put it in the manager. Click the checkmark when items start moving."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eProgram:&r"
		"EVERY 20 TICKS DO"
		"    INPUT FROM a"
		"    OUTPUT TO b"
		"END"
		"&eTip:&r add a side, like &eOUTPUT TO b TOP SIDE&r, to choose which face of the block is used. The manager's built-in examples cover fluids and energy too."
	]
	quest.0239845B19FBECF7.title: "Logistics Network"
	quest.0239845B19FBECF7.quest_subtitle: "Optional: nodes that route by rules"
	quest.0239845B19FBECF7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Logistics Network nodes sit on machines and chests and move items, fluids and energy between every node in the same named network, with no cables."
		"&eHow:&r obsidian, a redstone block, hoppers, an eye of ender and a redstone torch for a node (check JEI). Open a node to create or join a network, then set what it imports and exports."
		"&eTip:&r the Wrench has a copy-paste mode: set up one node, then paste its settings onto the rest."
	]
	quest.06ECD076BD8BC6DA.title: "Logistics Filters"
	quest.06ECD076BD8BC6DA.quest_subtitle: "Optional: move only what you mean to"
	quest.06ECD076BD8BC6DA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r filters narrow what a node moves: by tag, by amount and more."
		"&eHow:&r put a filter in a node's slot and set it up in its GUI (check JEI for all the filter types)."
		"&eTip:&r a tag filter for 'c:dusts' sends every dust to one chest."
	]
	quest.489B2F9C72693B10.title: "Node Upgrades"
	quest.489B2F9C72693B10.quest_subtitle: "Optional: bigger batches, shorter delays"
	quest.489B2F9C72693B10.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r upgrades raise how much a node moves per batch and how often. Iron, gold, diamond and netherite tiers each do more."
		"&eHow:&r the tier's metal, hoppers, chests and smooth stone (check JEI). Put them in the node's upgrade slots."
		"&eTip:&r the upgrade's tooltip lists its exact items, fluid and energy per batch."
	]
	quest.1256F17F8027B0DF.title: "Moving Chemicals"
	quest.1256F17F8027B0DF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: nodes that carry Mekanism gases"
	quest.1256F17F8027B0DF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Mekanism Chemical Upgrade lets nodes move Mekanism chemicals: H₂, O₂, Cl₂, SO₂ and the rest."
		"&eChemistry:&r the contact process needs SO₂ and O₂ in the same place: 2SO₂ + O₂ → 2SO₃. Nodes can bring both to one Chemical Infuser."
		"&eHow:&r basic chemical tanks, infused alloy, chests and an Iron Upgrade (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r one network for gases and another for items keeps the settings easy to read."
	]
	quest.4AAFFDC37F0E4EE8.title: "Network Manager"
	quest.4AAFFDC37F0E4EE8.quest_subtitle: "Optional: see every node and its flow"
	quest.4AAFFDC37F0E4EE8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Computer opens a Network Manager that lists your networks, their nodes and how much each channel moves."
		"&eHow:&r iron, glass and a comparator (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r when a line stops, look here first: a channel with no flow shows where the jam is."
	]
	chapter.0B070594762C61D3.title: "Integrated Dynamics"
	chapter.0B070594762C61D3.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Logic networks grown from resin."
	]
	quest.1F1E66B35278C2F3.title: "Menril Trees"
	quest.1F1E66B35278C2F3.quest_subtitle: "Blue-grey wood full of resin"
	quest.1F1E66B35278C2F3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Thought made solid, growing on a tree. You remember building minds out of stranger things.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Menril trees are where Integrated Dynamics starts: logs for resin, and berries from the leaves."
		"&eChemistry:&r real tree resins are mixtures of terpenes, small hydrocarbons that plants build from isoprene units (C₅H₈). Amber is resin that hardened over millions of years."
		"&eHow:&r find a Menril tree in the Overworld (Jade names it) and plant its saplings near your base."
	]
	quest.2006C6B640CAAFF4.title: "Menril Berries"
	quest.2006C6B640CAAFF4.quest_subtitle: "A snack with side effects"
	quest.2006C6B640CAAFF4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r berries drop from Menril leaves."
		"&eHow:&r break or wait for Menril leaves to decay."
		"&eTip:&r read the berries' tooltip before you eat a stack."
	]
	quest.352C13A0AB00A5FD.title: "Menril Seeds"
	quest.352C13A0AB00A5FD.quest_subtitle: "Optional: grow Menril as a crop"
	quest.352C13A0AB00A5FD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mystical Agriculture can grow Menril essence, which crafts into Menril logs, so you never chase trees again."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for the seed; its tier sets which Mystical Agriculture essence and circuit it needs."
		"&eTip:&r the Mystical Agriculture page covers seed tiers."
	]
	quest.64796471E388C36C.title: "Squeezer"
	quest.64796471E388C36C.quest_subtitle: "Press the resin out"
	quest.64796471E388C36C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Squeezer presses Menril logs into liquid resin."
		"&eHow:&r an iron block, iron, planks and sticks (check JEI). Put a Menril log in and jump on it a few times."
		"&eTip:&r it presses other things too. Ores give 2 raw ores in this pack, like every early processor."
	]
	quest.51AA7365BFEED033.title: "Drying Basin"
	quest.51AA7365BFEED033.quest_subtitle: "Leave the resin to set"
	quest.51AA7365BFEED033.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Drying Basin dries Menril resin into crystalized Menril chunks."
		"&eChemistry:&r drying is evaporation: the solvent leaves and the dissolved solids stay, just as salt is left when brine dries."
		"&eHow:&r logs, iron and black dye (check JEI). Place the Squeezer on top of the basin and the resin flows straight in."
	]
	quest.27ED21A2DD1FDA38.title: "Crystalized Menril"
	quest.27ED21A2DD1FDA38.quest_subtitle: "The building block of logic"
	quest.27ED21A2DD1FDA38.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r crystalized Menril chunks make every cable, card and part of Integrated Dynamics."
		"&eHow:&r dry resin in the basin, a bucket at a time."
		"&eTip:&r nine chunks make a block, and some recipes want the block."
	]
	quest.42F2E8F1D04D046D.title: "Energy Battery"
	quest.42F2E8F1D04D046D.quest_subtitle: "Power for a logic network"
	quest.42F2E8F1D04D046D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Energy Battery stores FE and can feed a network through its cables."
		"&eHow:&r crystalized Menril chunks and blocks around a redstone block (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r any FE source works; link a cable to your main grid instead if you have one."
	]
	quest.389B2529EE0F1417.title: "ID Generator"
	quest.389B2529EE0F1417.quest_subtitle: "Optional: burn fuel for the network"
	quest.389B2529EE0F1417.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Integrated Dynamics' own Generator burns furnace fuel for FE."
		"&eChemistry:&r burning charcoal is C + O₂ → CO₂, about 33 kJ of heat for every gram of carbon."
		"&eHow:&r an Energy Battery plus a furnace (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.0B8712079F22304F.title: "Mechanical Squeezer"
	quest.0B8712079F22304F.quest_subtitle: "Optional: no more jumping"
	quest.0B8712079F22304F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the powered Squeezer: faster and pipe-friendly."
		"&eHow:&r the Squeezer with Energy Batteries, a diamond and obsidian (check JEI). Feed it FE."
		"&eTip:&r ore output is capped at 2 raw ores in this pack, the same as the hand-powered one."
	]
	quest.6D023B5C96AD4D9C.title: "Mechanical Drying Basin"
	quest.6D023B5C96AD4D9C.quest_subtitle: "Optional: drying on power"
	quest.6D023B5C96AD4D9C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the powered Drying Basin: it dries resin much faster."
		"&eHow:&r the Drying Basin with Energy Batteries and more (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r press U on it in JEI to see what else it dries."
	]
	quest.4FFA7DD5BC94074C.title: "Input Transformer"
	quest.4FFA7DD5BC94074C.quest_subtitle: "The part inside every importer"
	quest.4FFA7DD5BC94074C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r input variable transformers are the crafting parts of readers and importers."
		"&eHow:&r variable cards, Menril chunks and a sticky piston (check JEI). Craft extra before a big build."
		"&eTip:&r one transformer per part, so a dozen goes quickly."
	]
	quest.7D824BBA6C0895AA.title: "Output Transformer"
	quest.7D824BBA6C0895AA.quest_subtitle: "The part inside every exporter"
	quest.7D824BBA6C0895AA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r output variable transformers are the crafting parts of writers and exporters."
		"&eHow:&r like the input one, mirrored (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r keep both kinds in a chest next to your crafting table."
	]
	quest.2A2D0EBC86F0D3DA.title: "Importers"
	quest.2A2D0EBC86F0D3DA.quest_subtitle: "Pull things into the network"
	quest.2A2D0EBC86F0D3DA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r importers pull items, fluids or energy into the network. World importers take straight from the world: they break blocks, pick up items, or drain fluid."
		"&eHow:&r an input transformer and a few extras per part (check JEI). Any importer counts."
		"&eTip:&r a world block importer with a filter is a tidy quarry face."
	]
	quest.1216DA8041FBAB86.title: "Exporters"
	quest.1216DA8041FBAB86.quest_subtitle: "Push things out where you want them"
	quest.1216DA8041FBAB86.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r exporters push items, fluids or energy out of the network. World exporters place blocks, drop items or pour fluid."
		"&eHow:&r an output transformer and a few extras per part (check JEI). Any exporter counts."
		"&eTip:&r a world block exporter is an automatic block placer for a cobble or basalt generator."
	]
	quest.5B66E9C98951DF71.title: "Integrated Tunnels"
	quest.5B66E9C98951DF71.quest_subtitle: "Move items, fluids and energy with logic"
	quest.5B66E9C98951DF71.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r importers, exporters and interfaces together move anything along the logic cables, controlled by variables."
		"&eHow:&r put an Item Importer on a chest and an Item Exporter on a machine, and give the exporter a variable card that says what to move. Click the checkmark when it works."
		"&eTip:&r a fluid exporter with a yes/no variable from a tank reader only fills the reactor when it's below half."
	]
	quest.00C7FF03D1B02894.title: "Logic Programmer"
	quest.00C7FF03D1B02894.quest_subtitle: "Write rules onto cards"
	quest.00C7FF03D1B02894.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Logic Programmer writes values and rules onto variable cards: 'tank above 90%', 'more than 64 sulfur', and so on."
		"&eHow:&r Menril chunks and a few extras (check JEI). Pick an operator on the left, fill in its inputs, and write it onto a blank card."
		"&eTip:&r a Redstone Writer turns a yes/no card into a signal: perfect for stopping a separator when its tank is full."
	]
	quest.45734051C5E266FD.title: "Portable Programmer"
	quest.45734051C5E266FD.quest_subtitle: "The programmer in your pocket"
	quest.45734051C5E266FD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the same Logic Programmer, as an item."
		"&eHow:&r a Logic Programmer and Menril chunks (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r carry it while wiring up a factory, so you can fix a card on the spot."
	]
	quest.00A54A06239849EA.title: "Challenge: The Self-Stopping Separator"
	quest.00A54A06239849EA.quest_subtitle: "Your first closed loop"
	quest.00A54A06239849EA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r make a Mekanism Electrolytic Separator turn itself off when its hydrogen tank is 90% full, and back on below 50%."
		"&eHow:&r a Reader on the tank → a comparison in the Logic Programmer → a Redstone Writer on the separator (set it to redstone control in its GUI)."
		"&eTip:&r the gap between 50% and 90% (hysteresis) stops it flickering on and off."
		"Click the checkmark once it works."
	]
	quest.41D0A370BD0CCEFC.title: "Note: Readers and Aspects"
	quest.41D0A370BD0CCEFC.quest_subtitle: "What a reader can tell you"
	quest.41D0A370BD0CCEFC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every Reader part (inventory, fluid, energy, redstone, world and more) offers a list of aspects: single values it can read, like 'fill ratio' or 'item count'."
		"&eHow:&r right-click a placed reader to see its aspects, and drag one onto a blank card to save it. Display Panels show a card's value live."
		"&eTip:&r a Display Panel on every main tank is a cheap base dashboard. Click the checkmark when you've read one value."
	]
	quest.698304026FBC82C1.title: "Integrated Crafting"
	quest.698304026FBC82C1.quest_subtitle: "Autocrafting without AE2"
	quest.698304026FBC82C1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Crafting Interface crafts on demand through the ID network, much like AE2 patterns."
		"&eHow:&r write recipes onto variable cards with the Logic Programmer and put them in the interface on a machine (check JEI for the part)."
		"&eTip:&r it's a cheaper autocrafter than AE2 for small chains, like rubber sheets or redstone batteries."
	]
	quest.0B6B6A7EEDAF93D8.title: "Variable Store"
	quest.0B6B6A7EEDAF93D8.quest_subtitle: "Keep your logic in one place"
	quest.0B6B6A7EEDAF93D8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Variable Store holds variable cards so the whole network can use them."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI. Put cards in the store and reference them from any writer or display panel on the network."
		"&eTip:&r name cards with the Labeller after what they measure ('H2 tank %'). You'll thank yourself later."
	]
	quest.132AB0ACC55773F4.title: "Crafting Job Terminal"
	quest.132AB0ACC55773F4.quest_subtitle: "Watch the network craft"
	quest.132AB0ACC55773F4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Integrated Terminals' Crafting Job Terminal shows what Integrated Crafting is working on and what it's waiting for."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI; it's a part, so it goes on a cable."
		"&eTip:&r the Storage Terminal part (and its portable version) shows everything on the network, like an ME terminal."
	]
	chapter.6F5A0E5EF3B9E1BF.title: "Pylons"
	chapter.6F5A0E5EF3B9E1BF.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Standing stones that bend the rules of a chunk."
	]
	quest.60BA26548880FCDF.title: "Pylons"
	quest.60BA26548880FCDF.quest_subtitle: "Polished blackstone is where every pylon starts"
	quest.60BA26548880FCDF.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember marking ground as yours with a single stone. These are close enough.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Pylons are blocks that change the rules in an area: give you an effect, farm for you, keep mobs out, keep players out, or protect what you've built."
		"&eHow:&r every pylon is the pylon frame (quartz slabs, iron bars and polished blackstone) around a core block. Most take a filter to tell them what to act on."
		"&eTip:&r polished blackstone comes from the Nether: smelt or stonecut blackstone, then polish it."
	]
	quest.60D349276513B2BE.title: "Expulsion Pylon"
	quest.60D349276513B2BE.quest_subtitle: "Uninvited guests leave"
	quest.60D349276513B2BE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Expulsion Pylon sends other players out of the chunks around it. Whitelist friends with a Player Filter."
		"&eHow:&r the pylon frame (quartz slabs, iron bars and polished blackstone) around a diamond block (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r with FTB Teams, your team is whitelisted automatically."
	]
	quest.51BEBD7764209CA7.title: "Interdiction Pylon"
	quest.51BEBD7764209CA7.quest_subtitle: "Not that mob, not here"
	quest.51BEBD7764209CA7.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r stops chosen mobs spawning around it. A Mob Filter names the mob; a Lifeless Filter blocks all natural spawns."
		"&eHow:&r the pylon frame (quartz slabs, iron bars and polished blackstone) around a netherite block (check JEI). Put the filter inside."
		"&eTip:&r a phantom filter over your base means sleepless nights are only a figure of speech."
	]
	quest.0EEBD82F0B57E5EF.title: "Harvester Pylon"
	quest.0EEBD82F0B57E5EF.quest_subtitle: "A pylon that farms for you"
	quest.0EEBD82F0B57E5EF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r harvests ripe crops in a square around it and puts them in a chest above it, wearing down a hoe as it goes."
		"&eChemistry:&r every harvest carries nitrogen, phosphorus and potassium out of the soil. Real farms put it back with fertiliser; this one forgives you."
		"&eHow:&r the pylon frame (quartz slabs, iron bars and polished blackstone) around a hay bale. Put it level with the crops, a hoe inside and a chest on top."
		"&eTip:&r an Unbreaking hoe lasts far longer; a Mending one never runs out."
	]
	quest.147F437F62E7C586.title: "Infusion Pylon"
	quest.147F437F62E7C586.quest_subtitle: "An effect that follows you everywhere"
	quest.147F437F62E7C586.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Infusion Pylon applies a potion filter's effect to its owner, anywhere. With a Flying filter, that's flight."
		"&eChemistry:&r its core needs hydrogen, the lightest element: the gas that lifted the first balloons."
		"&eHow:&r in this pack: 2 quartz slabs, 2 iron bars, a block of emerald, 3 polished blackstone and 1 &ehydrogen&r from your Dissolver (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the main path's Wings of a God quest walks through the flight filter step by step."
	]
	quest.35BBCCB16F699629.title: "Protection Pylon"
	quest.35BBCCB16F699629.quest_subtitle: "Keep your own hands off your best work"
	quest.35BBCCB16F699629.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r stops chosen blocks being broken, or chosen mobs being hurt, in its range. A pet or a showpiece is safe even from your own sword."
		"&eHow:&r the pylon frame (quartz slabs, iron bars and polished blackstone) around a honeycomb block (check JEI). Add a Block Filter or a Mob Filter."
		"&eTip:&r protect the glass of your evaporation tower before the first creeper finds it."
	]
	quest.1C0254F397D306D0.title: "Player Filter"
	quest.1C0254F397D306D0.quest_subtitle: "Names the friends who may stay"
	quest.1C0254F397D306D0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Player Filter lists players for the Expulsion Pylon to let through."
		"&eHow:&r cyan terracotta, green dye and glass around a diamond (check JEI). Right-click a player with it to add them."
		"&eTip:&r one filter holds several names."
	]
	quest.0A13A4B12CEEADEC.title: "Mob Filter"
	quest.0A13A4B12CEEADEC.quest_subtitle: "Names one kind of mob"
	quest.0A13A4B12CEEADEC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Mob Filter names a mob type for the Interdiction or Protection Pylon."
		"&eHow:&r cyan terracotta, green dye and glass around netherite (check JEI). Use it on the mob to set it."
		"&eTip:&r one filter per mob type; a pylon takes several."
	]
	quest.5D3BBE0974D5D537.title: "Potion Filter"
	quest.5D3BBE0974D5D537.quest_subtitle: "Store an effect in glass"
	quest.5D3BBE0974D5D537.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Potion Filter stores a potion effect for the Infusion Pylon."
		"&eHow:&r 2 cyan terracotta, green dye, an emerald and 5 glass. Drink a potion, then right-click the filter to store the effect."
		"&eTip:&r it only works once it holds an hour of the effect, so brew Long or Extra Long potions."
	]
	quest.303BE5FCB4509058.title: "A Spare Hoe"
	quest.303BE5FCB4509058.quest_subtitle: "Any hoe, for the Harvester"
	quest.303BE5FCB4509058.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Harvester Pylon needs a hoe to work, and wears it down by one point per harvest."
		"&eHow:&r any hoe counts: wood, iron, diamond or a modded one."
		"&eTip:&r the better the hoe, the longer between refills."
	]
	quest.542F34211E348C1A.title: "Lifeless Filter"
	quest.542F34211E348C1A.quest_subtitle: "No natural spawns at all"
	quest.542F34211E348C1A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Lifeless Filter makes an Interdiction Pylon block every natural spawn over a much larger area."
		"&eHow:&r cyan terracotta, green dye and glass around a Nether Star (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r spawners and breeding still work, so farms inside the area keep running."
	]
	quest.746432B234EE074D.title: "Block Filter"
	quest.746432B234EE074D.quest_subtitle: "Names the blocks to protect"
	quest.746432B234EE074D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a Block Filter lists blocks the Protection Pylon keeps from being broken."
		"&eHow:&r cyan terracotta, green dye and glass around a honeycomb (check JEI). Use it on a block to add it."
		"&eTip:&r list the glass and casings of a multiblock so a slip of the pickaxe can't break it."
	]
	chapter.355E4A964218121E.title: "Farming and Food"
	chapter.355E4A964218121E.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Grow what you need, cook it well, feed it back to the soil."
	]
	quest.61BB360C973E0F7F.title: "Knife and Board"
	quest.61BB360C973E0F7F.quest_subtitle: "Farmer's Delight starts with a cut"
	quest.61BB360C973E0F7F.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember feasts that lasted a week. Start with something smaller.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Farmer's Delight adds crops, meals and kitchen blocks. The knife harvests straw and cuts ingredients."
		"&eHow:&r craft a knife (flint is the cheapest; any knife counts) and a Cutting Board. Place items on the board and use the knife on them."
		"&eTip:&r a knife on tall grass gives straw; wild crops (tomatoes, onions, cabbage, rice) grow in the wild."
	]
	quest.1CD576F80AC49B5F.title: "Cooking Pot"
	quest.1CD576F80AC49B5F.quest_subtitle: "Heat, ingredients, and a meal"
	quest.1CD576F80AC49B5F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Cooking Pot turns several ingredients into one meal. It needs heat underneath."
		"&eChemistry:&r browning meat is the Maillard reaction: amino acids and sugars react above about 140 °C, making hundreds of flavour compounds."
		"&eHow:&r iron, bricks, a wooden shovel and a water bucket (check JEI). Place it over a fire, campfire or Stove."
	]
	quest.2CFFEDC4683607CF.title: "A Proper Meal"
	quest.2CFFEDC4683607CF.quest_subtitle: "Food that keeps you full"
	quest.2CFFEDC4683607CF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Farmer's Delight meals restore a lot of hunger and give long effects like Nourishment (hunger stops dropping) and Comfort."
		"&eHow:&r cook vegetable soup in the Cooking Pot (check JEI), then bowl it."
		"&eTip:&r a Feeding Upgrade in your backpack eats these for you."
	]
	quest.6AAF559710229117.title: "Pasta with Meatballs"
	quest.6AAF559710229117.quest_subtitle: "Optional: four ingredients, three of them cooked first"
	quest.6AAF559710229117.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hearty meal that chains every kitchen tool: knife (minced beef), board (raw pasta from dough) and pot (tomato sauce)."
		"&eChemistry:&r dough is starch and gluten proteins; water lets gluten chains cross-link into the stretchy network that holds pasta together."
		"&eHow:&r follow the tree in JEI: wheat dough → raw pasta, beef → minced beef, tomatoes → tomato sauce, then the pot."
		"&eTip:&r press U on any ingredient in JEI to see every meal that uses it."
	]
	quest.6E91CE0ADEA5ADA6.title: "A Varied Diet"
	quest.6E91CE0ADEA5ADA6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: any six Farmer's Delight meals"
	quest.6E91CE0ADEA5ADA6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r collect six bowls or plates of any Farmer's Delight meal: stews, soups, rice dishes, ratatouille, you choose."
		"&eHow:&r anything in the 'meals' tag counts. Mix and match, they don't have to be different."
		"&eTip:&r meals stack to 16; keep a stack in the backpack for long mining trips."
	]
	quest.26CA44769AF76A9D.title: "Rich Soil"
	quest.26CA44769AF76A9D.quest_subtitle: "Optional: compost into the best dirt"
	quest.26CA44769AF76A9D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r organic compost slowly turns into Rich Soil, which grows crops faster and mushrooms into colonies."
		"&eChemistry:&r composting is microbes breaking down organic matter with oxygen. They release CO₂ and heat, and leave humus rich in nitrogen."
		"&eHow:&r craft compost from dirt, straw and bone meal plus rotten flesh or tree bark (check JEI), place it and wait."
		"&eTip:&r till Rich Soil with a hoe to get rich farmland for crops."
	]
	quest.2FB463350074B333.title: "The Stove"
	quest.2FB463350074B333.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a heat source that never burns out"
	quest.2FB463350074B333.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Stove heats a Cooking Pot or Skillet on top and can grill up to six items on its own surface."
		"&eHow:&r iron ingots, bricks and a campfire (check JEI). Light it with flint and steel."
		"&eTip:&r unlike a campfire it doesn't need logs, and it looks right in a kitchen."
	]
	quest.1DF7F1133046DEB1.title: "A Feast"
	quest.1DF7F1133046DEB1.quest_subtitle: "Optional: one block feeds the whole team"
	quest.1DF7F1133046DEB1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r feasts are placed as blocks and served with a bowl, several portions each."
		"&eHow:&r cook a Honey Glazed Ham (check JEI). Place it on a table and right-click with bowls."
		"&eTip:&r a feast is the easiest way to feed a whole team before a boss fight."
	]
	quest.188A4BC2D2682264.title: "Banquet"
	quest.188A4BC2D2682264.quest_subtitle: "Optional: roast chicken and shepherd's pie"
	quest.188A4BC2D2682264.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r two more feasts for the table: a whole Roast Chicken and a Shepherd's Pie."
		"&eHow:&r both come from the Cooking Pot (check JEI). Each needs a container, often a bowl, to serve."
		"&eTip:&r place feasts where everyone passes, like next to the team's waystone."
	]
	quest.68C63D9C708CAB99.title: "Mushroom Colonies"
	quest.68C63D9C708CAB99.quest_subtitle: "Optional: mushrooms that keep growing"
	quest.68C63D9C708CAB99.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a mushroom on Rich Soil grows into a colony that you can harvest again and again."
		"&eChemistry:&r fungi don't photosynthesise. They digest organic matter with enzymes, which is why rich, dark soil suits them."
		"&eHow:&r plant a brown or red mushroom on Rich Soil in low light, wait, then harvest it with shears; the colony stays and regrows."
		"&eTip:&r mushroom colonies are the steady source of mushrooms for stews and rice dishes."
	]
	quest.05CA20DAF3D6CE4E.title: "Skillet"
	quest.05CA20DAF3D6CE4E.quest_subtitle: "Optional: fry it, or hit something with it"
	quest.05CA20DAF3D6CE4E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a frying pan that cooks one item at a time over heat, and doubles as a surprisingly good weapon."
		"&eHow:&r iron ingots and a brick (check JEI). Place it on the Stove or a campfire, or check its tooltip for cooking in hand."
		"&eTip:&r Fire Aspect on a skillet sounds silly; it works."
	]
	quest.056B1AE78D5B1CCF.title: "Breakfast"
	quest.056B1AE78D5B1CCF.quest_subtitle: "Optional: eggs and bacon from the skillet"
	quest.056B1AE78D5B1CCF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the start of most Farmer's Delight breakfasts: fried eggs and cooked bacon."
		"&eChemistry:&r egg white turns opaque as heat unfolds its proteins (denaturation) and they tangle together; it can't go back."
		"&eHow:&r cut raw porkchop into bacon on the Cutting Board, then fry it and the eggs on the Skillet or Stove."
		"&eTip:&r combine them into Bacon and Eggs in the Cooking Pot (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.6D7BCF15F3CF7687.title: "The New Crops"
	quest.6D7BCF15F3CF7687.quest_subtitle: "Tomatoes, onions, cabbage and rice"
	quest.6D7BCF15F3CF7687.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Farmer's Delight crops are the base of nearly every meal."
		"&eHow:&r find wild tomatoes, onions, cabbages and rice in the world (rice grows in shallow water). Break them for seeds and replant."
		"&eTip:&r rice must be planted in water one block deep, like in a real paddy."
	]
	quest.2D35837B42389FD6.title: "Tomatoes on a Rope"
	quest.2D35837B42389FD6.quest_subtitle: "Optional: grow upward"
	quest.2D35837B42389FD6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tomato vines climb rope, so a single plant grows several blocks tall and fruits all the way up."
		"&eHow:&r craft rope from straw (check JEI), hang it above a tomato plant, and let the vine climb."
		"&eTip:&r rope also lets you climb down mineshafts; right-click a placed rope to extend it downward."
	]
	quest.726507D0921F20DA.title: "Harvest Festival"
	quest.726507D0921F20DA.quest_subtitle: "Optional: 128 crops of any kind"
	quest.726507D0921F20DA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a full harvest: any 128 items from the shared crops tag (wheat, carrots, potatoes, tomatoes, rice and more)."
		"&eHow:&r a large field, Hopper Botany Pots, or an MI Farmer all count. Carry them in one go."
		"&eTip:&r crop storage blocks (crates and bags) pack 9 crops each; you need the loose crops here."
	]
	quest.3890E7B5FA9CA044.title: "Hopper Botany Pots"
	quest.3890E7B5FA9CA044.quest_subtitle: "A farm in one block"
	quest.3890E7B5FA9CA044.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Hopper Botany Pots grow crops and push the harvest into the container below."
		"&eHow:&r place one on a chest, add soil (dirt) and a seed."
		"&eTip:&r Rich Soil or farmland grows faster than dirt, and Mystical Agriculture seeds work in pots too."
	]
	quest.1449CF00D49726FD.title: "Animal Husbandry"
	quest.1449CF00D49726FD.quest_subtitle: "A lead, and the animals at the end of it"
	quest.1449CF00D49726FD.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r cows, sheep, pigs and chickens give food, leather, wool and eggs. Two adults fed their favourite food make a baby."
		"&eHow:&r lead two animals into a pen and feed them. Just Enough Breeding adds a JEI page per animal: look up any mob egg or food to see what it eats and what it drops."
		"&eTip:&r babies take about 20 minutes to grow; feeding them their breeding food speeds that up."
	]
	quest.797F266229BD1FB2.title: "Pet Food"
	quest.797F266229BD1FB2.quest_subtitle: "Optional: feed for horses and wolves"
	quest.797F266229BD1FB2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Horse Feed heals and speeds up horses; Dog Food heals tamed wolves and gives them buffs."
		"&eHow:&r both are Farmer's Delight crafting recipes (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a well-fed wolf is a decent bodyguard in the early Twilight Forest."
	]
	quest.383BB756C9C76954.title: "N, P and K"
	quest.383BB756C9C76954.quest_subtitle: "The three numbers on every fertiliser bag"
	quest.383BB756C9C76954.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r plants need nitrogen (N), phosphorus (P) and potassium (K) more than anything else from the soil. These three compounds deliver them."
		"&eChemistry:&r urea CO(NH₂)₂ is 46% nitrogen; diammonium phosphate (NH₄)₂HPO₄ carries N and P; potassium nitrate KNO₃ carries K and N."
		"&eHow:&r make all three in the Alchemistry Combiner (check JEI for the element recipe of each)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: why nitrogen is the hard one.&r"
		"Air is 78% nitrogen, but N₂ has a triple bond that plants can't break. Only some soil bacteria (and lightning) can 'fix' it."
		"In 1909 Fritz Haber found how to force N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃ with a metal catalyst, high pressure and heat; Carl Bosch scaled it up."
		"Today about half the nitrogen in your body passed through a Haber-Bosch plant. Ammonia is turned into urea, ammonium nitrate and phosphates."
		"You'll build that same reaction in the main quests (Haber-Bosch, HV tier). Phosphorus comes from mined phosphate rock, and potassium from potash salts like KCl."
	]
	quest.201E746EF18C024B.title: "NPK Fertilizer"
	quest.201E746EF18C024B.quest_subtitle: "Liquid fertiliser from the Chemical Reactor"
	quest.201E746EF18C024B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Extended Industrialization's NPK Fertilizer is a fluid the MI Farmer can spread to grow crops faster."
		"&eChemistry:&r bone meal is calcium phosphate; sulfuric acid frees phosphoric acid, H₃PO₄, just like the real 'wet process' for phosphate rock."
		"&eHow:&r Chemical Reactor, three steps (check JEI): bone meal + H₂SO₄ → phosphoric acid; potato/carrot/beetroot + water + HCl → potassium chloride, then KCl + H₂ + O₂ → potassium hydroxide; finally nitrogen + phosphoric acid + KOH → NPK Fertilizer."
		"&eTip:&r real NPK plants start from ammonia, not raw nitrogen. Here the recipe takes the shortcut."
	]
	quest.42489EAAE4800867.title: "The Steam Farmer"
	quest.42489EAAE4800867.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a multiblock that plants and harvests"
	quest.42489EAAE4800867.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Extended Industrialization's Farmer is a multiblock that tills, plants, harvests and (with fertiliser) speeds up a whole field."
		"&eHow:&r analog circuits, a motor, bronze plated bricks, a steel combine and a bronze pipe casing (check JEI). Its layout is in JEI and the MI guidebook."
		"&eTip:&r the Electric Farmer is the upgrade. JEI has a fertiliser page that shows which fluids speed up a Farmer."
	]
	quest.4388A334EC12570D.title: "Food Fight"
	quest.4388A334EC12570D.quest_subtitle: "Secret: ammunition, not dinner"
	quest.4388A334EC12570D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r you found a use for spoiled tomatoes: rotten tomatoes can be thrown."
		"&eChemistry:&r rotting is bacteria and fungi breaking sugars into acids, alcohols and gases. Don't eat it."
		"&eTip:&r they're also good compost material. Probably better than throwing them at the team."
	]
	quest.795662BF85103267.title: "Kitchen Garden"
	quest.795662BF85103267.quest_subtitle: "Optional: seeds, roots, melons and berries"
	quest.795662BF85103267.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the vanilla crops beyond wheat: potatoes and carrots from village farms, melons from jungles, sweet berries from taiga."
		"&eChemistry:&r a potato is mostly starch, long chains of glucose packed into grains. Cooking swells and bursts the grains (gelatinisation), which is why a baked potato is soft."
		"&eHow:&r break grass for seeds, raid a village farm for potatoes and carrots, and replant everything."
		"&eTip:&r sweet berry bushes hurt to walk through. Plant a row as a mob fence."
	]
	quest.707EBA33CCE0C439.title: "Barnyard Goods"
	quest.707EBA33CCE0C439.quest_subtitle: "Optional: everything a pen of animals gives"
	quest.707EBA33CCE0C439.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r 16 raw meat of any kind, plus leather, feathers and eggs: the steady output of a few animal pens."
		"&eChemistry:&r an eggshell is about 95% calcium carbonate, CaCO₃: the same compound as chalk and limestone. Drop one in vinegar and it fizzes away as CO₂."
		"&eHow:&r breed cows, pigs, sheep, chickens or rabbits and harvest the adults. Chickens lay eggs on their own."
		"&eTip:&r cook meat before eating; raw chicken can give you Hunger."
	]
	quest.19B3E12AC6512111.title: "Milk"
	quest.19B3E12AC6512111.quest_subtitle: "The cure for most status effects"
	quest.19B3E12AC6512111.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r drinking milk clears every potion effect, good and bad. It's also a baking ingredient."
		"&eChemistry:&r milk is an emulsion: fat droplets held in water by proteins (casein). Add acid and the casein clumps into curds, which is the first step of every cheese."
		"&eHow:&r use an empty bucket on a cow (or a goat)."
		"&eTip:&r carry one into the Deep Dark or the Wither fight to wipe Darkness or Wither in one gulp."
	]
	quest.4001ABEC58F9F590.title: "Sugar"
	quest.4001ABEC58F9F590.quest_subtitle: "Crystallised sucrose"
	quest.4001ABEC58F9F590.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r sugar goes into cakes, pies, fermented spider eyes and speed potions."
		"&eChemistry:&r table sugar is sucrose, C₁₂H₂₂O₁₁: a glucose and a fructose joined together. Heat it past about 160 °C and it breaks down into hundreds of brown, bitter-sweet compounds: caramel."
		"&eHow:&r one sugar cane makes one sugar. A row of cane on Snad (Quality of Life page) grows fast."
		"&eTip:&r the Alchemistry Dissolver splits sucrose into carbon, hydrogen and oxygen if you need the elements."
	]
	quest.4859615A20A98EB3.title: "Bake Sale"
	quest.4859615A20A98EB3.quest_subtitle: "A whole cake"
	quest.4859615A20A98EB3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Wheat, sugar, milk and eggs from your own field and pasture. You remember feasts; this is a good start.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r a cake, placed and eaten a slice at a time. It needs something from every part of this page."
		"&eChemistry:&r baking is chemistry you can eat: egg proteins set the structure, sugar caramelises, and the Maillard reaction between sugars and proteins browns the crust."
		"&eHow:&r 3 milk buckets, 2 sugar, an egg and 3 wheat (you keep the buckets)."
		"&eTip:&r a cake on the table in your base means nobody ever starves between trips."
	]
	quest.0CEEB0EF247AFEE1.title: "Honey and Wax"
	quest.0CEEB0EF247AFEE1.quest_subtitle: "Optional: rob a hive without being stung"
	quest.0CEEB0EF247AFEE1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r shears on a full bee nest give honeycomb; a glass bottle gives honey. Honeycomb waxes copper so it never tarnishes."
		"&eChemistry:&r beeswax is mostly long esters (fatty acids joined to long alcohols). Wax on copper keeps out the air and water that would turn it green."
		"&eHow:&r put a campfire under the nest first: the smoke keeps the bees calm. Then shear it or bottle it when it's dripping."
		"&eTip:&r honey bottles cure poison and can be crafted into sugar."
	]
	quest.5B3831A5F122F274.title: "An Apiary"
	quest.5B3831A5F122F274.quest_subtitle: "Optional: your own hive and its blocks"
	quest.5B3831A5F122F274.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a beehive you can place where you like, plus the two honey blocks: sticky honey blocks and decorative honeycomb blocks."
		"&eChemistry:&r honey is a supersaturated sugar solution, about 80% sugar in 17% water. That's why it slowly crystallises, and why bacteria can't live in it: the sugar pulls the water out of them."
		"&eHow:&r a beehive is planks and honeycomb. A honey block is 4 honey bottles; a honeycomb block is 4 honeycomb. Lead bees home with flowers."
		"&eTip:&r honey blocks slow anything on them and stop pistons pulling other blocks; great for flying machines."
	]
	quest.5008B9812B5F38D8.title: "Wildflowers"
	quest.5008B9812B5F38D8.quest_subtitle: "Optional: 16 flowers of any kind"
	quest.5008B9812B5F38D8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r flowers make dyes, feed bees and decorate. Any 16 count."
		"&eChemistry:&r many flower colours are anthocyanins, pigments that change colour with pH: the same molecule is red in acid and blue in alkali, like red cabbage indicator."
		"&eHow:&r pick them in meadows and flower forests, or bone meal grass to grow more."
		"&eTip:&r cornflower gives blue dye without lapis."
	]
	quest.2C27F6E0A24ECFCC.title: "Bone Meal"
	quest.2C27F6E0A24ECFCC.quest_subtitle: "Optional: phosphate for your crops"
	quest.2C27F6E0A24ECFCC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r bone meal makes crops, saplings and flowers grow instantly."
		"&eChemistry:&r bone is mostly hydroxyapatite, Ca₅(PO₄)₃(OH). Ground bone was one of the first phosphate fertilisers, before mined phosphate rock took over."
		"&eHow:&r one bone makes 3 bone meal; a composter also turns plant scraps into it."
		"&eTip:&r the NPK quests further along this page start from bone meal."
	]
	quest.4F51D89D9F8829D4.title: "Hay Bales"
	quest.4F51D89D9F8829D4.quest_subtitle: "Optional: wheat in bulk"
	quest.4F51D89D9F8829D4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hay bale is 9 wheat. Horses and llamas eat it, and landing on one cuts fall damage by 80%."
		"&eHow:&r 9 wheat in the crafting grid."
		"&eTip:&r a hay bale under a campfire makes the smoke rise much higher: a signal for friends."
	]
	quest.18F6CFCBB960E126.title: "Crates and Bags"
	quest.18F6CFCBB960E126.quest_subtitle: "Optional: store a harvest in a block"
	quest.18F6CFCBB960E126.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Farmer's Delight crates and bags hold 9 crops each and look good in a pantry. Any four."
		"&eHow:&r 9 of the crop in the crafting grid (check JEI). Break one back into crops any time."
		"&eTip:&r a wall of crates is a kitchen store that doubles as decoration."
	]
	quest.10DB0AD9FC683E4A.title: "From the Sea"
	quest.10DB0AD9FC683E4A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: kelp, and a bright fish"
	quest.10DB0AD9FC683E4A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r kelp grows fast underwater; dried, it's a snack and (as a block) a good furnace fuel. Tropical fish come from fishing or warm oceans."
		"&eChemistry:&r burnt kelp ash was the world's first source of iodine: Bernard Courtois found it in 1811 when sulfuric acid on seaweed ash gave off violet I₂ vapour. The ash was also a source of soda for glass."
		"&eHow:&r harvest kelp, smelt it into dried kelp, and catch or bucket a tropical fish."
		"&eTip:&r 9 dried kelp make a block that burns for 20 items in a furnace."
	]
	quest.0E68D7AE1C7DBBA0.title: "Nether Fungi"
	quest.0E68D7AE1C7DBBA0.quest_subtitle: "Optional: farm the Nether's forests"
	quest.0E68D7AE1C7DBBA0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r crimson and warped fungi grow into huge Nether trees when bone-mealed on matching nylium. Warped fungus on a stick steers a strider."
		"&eChemistry:&r real fungi aren't plants: their cell walls are chitin, the same polymer as insect shells, not cellulose."
		"&eHow:&r pick them in the crimson and warped forests. Bone meal on nylium grows more."
		"&eTip:&r hoglins run from warped fungus. Plant some around your Nether base."
	]
	quest.15F725E5C01D018A.title: "Chorus Orchard"
	quest.15F725E5C01D018A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: the End's only crop"
	quest.15F725E5C01D018A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r chorus fruit teleports you a short way when eaten. Smelted, it becomes popped chorus fruit for purpur blocks, end rods and Silent Gear's glittery dust."
		"&eHow:&r break chorus plants on the outer End islands, or plant a chorus flower on end stone and grow your own."
		"&eTip:&r in this pack the Potion of Flying uses hydrogen, not chorus, so this crop is for building and Silent Gear."
	]
	quest.37E826F1EDD6F372.title: "Flax String"
	quest.37E826F1EDD6F372.quest_subtitle: "String without spiders"
	quest.37E826F1EDD6F372.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Silent Gear's flax gives fibre for string, so bows and bindings don't depend on spider hunts."
		"&eChemistry:&r flax fibre is nearly pure cellulose. Linen, made from it, is one of the oldest textiles, woven for over 30,000 years."
		"&eHow:&r grow flax and craft its fibre into flax string (check JEI for the recipe)."
		"&eTip:&r flax flowers make blue dye too."
	]
	quest.6E4CBAC1961181AC.title: "Overqualified"
	quest.6E4CBAC1961181AC.quest_subtitle: "Secret: the most expensive way to till dirt"
	quest.6E4CBAC1961181AC.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember making forests grow with a word. Now you're upgrading a hoe with netherite. Priorities.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r a netherite hoe. It tills, it harvests leaves and sculk fast, and it cost you a netherite ingot."
		"&eTip:&r hoes are the fastest tool for leaves, hay, moss and sculk. So it isn't entirely a joke."
	]
	quest.608361B36B4CBB56.title: "Something That Grows"
	quest.608361B36B4CBB56.quest_subtitle: "Any crop at all"
	quest.608361B36B4CBB56.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember fields that ripened when you walked past them. Now you'll have to wait for the sun, like everyone else.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r this page covers food: the vanilla field and pasture, Farmer's Delight's kitchen, fertiliser chemistry and the sea."
		"&eChemistry:&r every crop is stored sunlight: 6CO₂ + 6H₂O → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂, powered by light and run by chlorophyll."
		"&eHow:&r pick up any crop (wheat, carrots, potatoes, beetroot, Farmer's Delight crops and more all count)."
		"&eTip:&r village farms are a free first harvest."
	]
	quest.0C3B5911C3CE83E1.title: "A Hoe"
	quest.0C3B5911C3CE83E1.quest_subtitle: "Turn dirt into farmland"
	quest.0C3B5911C3CE83E1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a hoe tills dirt and grass into farmland, the only block most crops grow on."
		"&eHow:&r 2 of any tool material and 2 sticks. Any hoe counts."
		"&eTip:&r farmland within 4 blocks of water stays wet and grows crops faster."
	]
	quest.3D16238345D145F0.title: "Seeds"
	quest.3D16238345D145F0.quest_subtitle: "Eight seeds to start a field"
	quest.3D16238345D145F0.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r wheat seeds come from breaking grass, and every harvest gives more back."
		"&eHow:&r break tall grass, then plant on tilled farmland."
		"&eTip:&r seeds also feed chickens; keep a few spare."
	]
	quest.7F61136246AB9DEA.title: "Wheat"
	quest.7F61136246AB9DEA.quest_subtitle: "The first harvest"
	quest.7F61136246AB9DEA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r wheat is bread, cake and animal feed."
		"&eChemistry:&r a wheat grain is mostly starch plus gluten proteins, the proteins that make dough stretch."
		"&eHow:&r grow seeds until the stalks turn gold, then break them."
		"&eTip:&r a composter turns spare seeds into bone meal."
	]
	quest.02FACAB9BA3E93D6.title: "Bread"
	quest.02FACAB9BA3E93D6.quest_subtitle: "Three loaves"
	quest.02FACAB9BA3E93D6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the simplest real meal: three wheat make a loaf."
		"&eChemistry:&r real bread rises because yeast ferments sugar into CO₂ and ethanol; the gas gets trapped in the gluten network."
		"&eHow:&r 3 wheat in a row on a crafting table."
		"&eTip:&r bread stacks to 64 and never spoils. Carry a stack."
	]
	quest.20AF2159674A0643.title: "Sugar Cane"
	quest.20AF2159674A0643.quest_subtitle: "A reed that grows by water"
	quest.20AF2159674A0643.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r sugar cane gives sugar and paper."
		"&eHow:&r find it on sand or dirt next to water and replant it by water."
		"&eTip:&r break the top blocks and leave the bottom one: it regrows."
	]
	quest.316D014140DCB5D8.title: "Flax Seeds"
	quest.316D014140DCB5D8.quest_subtitle: "A crop for fibre, not food"
	quest.316D014140DCB5D8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Silent Gear's flax is grown for its fibre, which becomes string."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for where flax seeds drop, then plant them on farmland."
		"&eTip:&r one seed is enough to start; replant the extras."
	]
	quest.0C68E65A5DB2B595.title: "Fishing Rod"
	quest.0C68E65A5DB2B595.quest_subtitle: "Food from any water"
	quest.0C68E65A5DB2B595.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fishing gives fish, and sometimes treasure: saddles, name tags, enchanted books."
		"&eHow:&r 3 sticks and 2 string."
		"&eTip:&r Luck of the Sea and Lure enchantments make it far better."
	]
	quest.01058B56E9F9B012.title: "Shears"
	quest.01058B56E9F9B012.quest_subtitle: "Wool without killing the sheep"
	quest.01058B56E9F9B012.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r shears take wool from sheep (they regrow it by eating grass), and collect leaves, vines and cobwebs."
		"&eHow:&r 2 iron ingots diagonally. Any shears count."
		"&eTip:&r dye a sheep and it grows coloured wool forever."
	]
	quest.3A5F859955CE1AFF.title: "Wool"
	quest.3A5F859955CE1AFF.quest_subtitle: "Three blocks of any colour"
	quest.3A5F859955CE1AFF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r wool makes beds, carpets and banners."
		"&eChemistry:&r wool is keratin, a protein held together by sulfur bridges between its chains."
		"&eHow:&r shear sheep; each one gives 1 to 3 wool."
		"&eTip:&r three wool and three planks make a bed: set your spawn early."
	]
	quest.2CCBE2A708D00AC2.title: "Leather"
	quest.2CCBE2A708D00AC2.quest_subtitle: "From cows and horses"
	quest.2CCBE2A708D00AC2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r leather goes into books, item frames, armour and backpacks."
		"&eChemistry:&r tanning cross-links the collagen in hide so it stops rotting; plant tannins or chromium salts do the job."
		"&eHow:&r cows drop 0 to 2 leather each."
		"&eTip:&r rabbit hide also crafts into leather (4 hides make 1)."
	]
	quest.5E684E56447BABBB.title: "Eggs"
	quest.5E684E56447BABBB.quest_subtitle: "Three eggs"
	quest.5E684E56447BABBB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r chickens lay eggs by themselves about every 5 to 10 minutes."
		"&eChemistry:&r the shell is about 95% calcium carbonate, CaCO₃, the same compound as limestone."
		"&eHow:&r keep a few chickens penned and pick up what they drop."
		"&eTip:&r throwing an egg sometimes hatches a chick."
	]
	quest.45BD8886E1236F2B.title: "Feathers and Chicken"
	quest.45BD8886E1236F2B.quest_subtitle: "A full coop's worth"
	quest.45BD8886E1236F2B.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r feathers make arrows and quills; raw chicken cooks into a decent meal."
		"&eHow:&r breed chickens with seeds, then harvest the adults."
		"&eTip:&r cook the chicken; raw chicken can make you hungry."
	]
	chapter.1C9E9D35BDB125AE.title: "Mystical Agriculture"
	chapter.1C9E9D35BDB125AE.chapter_subtitle: [
		"Resource crops, within the rules of chemistry."
	]
	quest.7592FE8784DA7D0E.title: "Mystical Agriculture"
	quest.7592FE8784DA7D0E.quest_subtitle: "Resource crops, made on an altar"
	quest.7592FE8784DA7D0E.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember coaxing metal out of the ground like wheat. Some of that still works.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r resource crops grow essence that crafts into real materials. Seeds are made on the Infusion Altar with Infusion Pedestals around it."
		"&eHow:&r the altar is gold, stone and red wool; 8 Infusion Pedestals stand around it (check JEI for both and the layout)."
		"&eTip:&r &eTier 3/4/5 seeds need MI LV/MV/HV circuits&r, and crops for chemistry milestones can't be grown at all. Farming is a convenience here, not a shortcut."
	]
	quest.476972F4A69AE2B6.title: "Prosperity"
	quest.476972F4A69AE2B6.quest_subtitle: "Shards for seed bases and crystals"
	quest.476972F4A69AE2B6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r prosperity shards come from prosperity ore. They make seed bases (the core of every resource seed) and infusion crystals."
		"&eHow:&r mine prosperity ore (an iron pick is enough)."
		"&eTip:&r Ultimine the veins; you'll want a lot of shards."
	]
	quest.53DFFD39635750E6.title: "Infusion Crystal"
	quest.53DFFD39635750E6.quest_subtitle: "The tool that upgrades essence"
	quest.53DFFD39635750E6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a crystal that combines lower essence into higher tiers. It wears out with use."
		"&eHow:&r a diamond, prosperity shards and inferium essence (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the Master Infusion Crystal never wears out; it comes much later, from supremium."
	]
	quest.05F6FABCA51A5D27.title: "Prudentium"
	quest.05F6FABCA51A5D27.quest_subtitle: "Tier 2 essence"
	quest.05F6FABCA51A5D27.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the second essence tier, for tier 2 seeds (JEI lists every crop and its tier)."
		"&eHow:&r 4 inferium essence around an infusion crystal make 1 prudentium (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r it uncrafts back to inferium if you overshoot (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.63BC9482303C7949.title: "Tertium: LV Seeds"
	quest.63BC9482303C7949.quest_subtitle: "Tier 3 seeds need an analog circuit"
	quest.63BC9482303C7949.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tier 3 seeds (iron, copper, redstone, nether quartz, tin, lead and more) need Tertium essence and an &eMI analog circuit&r."
		"&eChemistry:&r the analog circuit stands on steel, and steel stands on coke: coal baked without air until only carbon is left."
		"&eHow:&r 4 prudentium around an infusion crystal make 1 tertium. Each seed type costs its circuit once; planted seeds multiply."
	]
	quest.429B4A2ABF9C8710.title: "Imperium: MV Seeds"
	quest.429B4A2ABF9C8710.quest_subtitle: "Tier 4 seeds need an electronic circuit"
	quest.429B4A2ABF9C8710.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r tier 4 seeds (gold, lapis, nickel, blaze, enderman and more) need Imperium essence and an &eMI electronic circuit&r."
		"&eChemistry:&r the electronic circuit needs aluminum, which only electrolysis can free from its oxide: 2Al₂O₃ → 4Al + 3O₂."
		"&eHow:&r 4 tertium around an infusion crystal make 1 imperium."
	]
	quest.329417D2B6B5EF41.title: "Supremium: HV Seeds"
	quest.329417D2B6B5EF41.quest_subtitle: "Tier 5 seeds need a digital circuit"
	quest.329417D2B6B5EF41.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember gardens that grew gold. These come close, and they still answer to chemistry.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r tier 5 seeds (diamond, emerald, netherite and more) need Supremium essence and an &eMI digital circuit&r."
		"&eChemistry:&r the digital circuit needs polyethylene: thousands of ethylene units, C₂H₄, linked into one chain."
		"&eHow:&r 4 imperium around an infusion crystal make 1 supremium."
	]
	quest.12AA4108F02395E9.title: "Growth Accelerators"
	quest.12AA4108F02395E9.quest_subtitle: "Crops grow faster above them"
	quest.12AA4108F02395E9.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r growth accelerators placed below farmland speed up the crops above them. Stack several for more effect."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI for each tier's recipe."
		"&eTip:&r put them under the floor of your crop room so they're out of the way."
	]
	quest.4D32DDE3DA6B6767.title: "Awakening"
	quest.4D32DDE3DA6B6767.quest_subtitle: "Beyond supremium"
	quest.4D32DDE3DA6B6767.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Awakening Altar turns supremium into awakened supremium for the strongest Mystical Agriculture gear."
		"&eHow:&r JEI shows the altar, its Awakening Pedestals, the Essence Vessels and the awakening recipe."
		"&eTip:&r awakened supremium makes the best Mystical Agriculture tools and armour."
	]
	quest.7B1B5EF67E8690E8.title: "Master Infusion Crystal"
	quest.7B1B5EF67E8690E8.quest_subtitle: "A crystal that never breaks"
	quest.7B1B5EF67E8690E8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r an infusion crystal with no durability, so essence upgrades stop costing crystals."
		"&eHow:&r a supremium gemstone, supremium essence and prosperity shards (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r worth it once you are mass-producing tertium and imperium for seeds."
	]
	quest.08D5A196E95B09AF.title: "Inferium Seeds"
	quest.08D5A196E95B09AF.quest_subtitle: "The crop that grows more essence"
	quest.08D5A196E95B09AF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Inferium Seeds grow inferium essence, the fuel for every higher tier. Any 4 Mystical Agriculture seeds complete this."
		"&eHow:&r 8 inferium essence around wheat seeds in a crafting grid (no altar needed). Plant them on farmland and replant the extra seeds."
		"&eTip:&r every other resource seed starts from a seed base on the altar, so build a big inferium field first."
	]
	quest.05CAB1D55ED3D024.title: "Essence Farmland"
	quest.05CAB1D55ED3D024.quest_subtitle: "Better soil, and the first seeds"
	quest.05CAB1D55ED3D024.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r farmland infused with essence. Inferium crops drop more essence on higher-tier farmland."
		"&eHow:&r one inferium essence plus one farmland, shapeless (check JEI). Higher tiers use their own essence."
		"&eTip:&r upgrade the farmland under your inferium field as each new essence tier arrives."
	]
	quest.54A29771FF1DDF78.title: "Mystical Fertilizer"
	quest.54A29771FF1DDF78.quest_subtitle: "Optional: grow a crop instantly"
	quest.54A29771FF1DDF78.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r instantly grows a crop or sapling, including resource crops that bone meal can't push."
		"&eHow:&r bone meal, inferium essence and a diamond make 4 (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r save it for slow, expensive crops rather than wheat."
	]
	quest.5839B7784C096EED.title: "Agglomeratio"
	quest.5839B7784C096EED.quest_subtitle: "Optional: materials for crops with no single item"
	quest.5839B7784C096EED.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r some crops (nature, the four elements, dye, nether, coral and others) don't map to one item. Their seed recipes use an agglomeratio instead."
		"&eHow:&r Nature Agglomeratio is pumpkin, potato, cactus and sugar cane; JEI shows the rest."
		"&eTip:&r the elemental crops (air, earth, water, fire) feed many other recipes, so they're good early picks."
	]
	quest.24AE5486AE474342.title: "Why Chemistry Won't Grow"
	quest.24AE5486AE474342.quest_subtitle: "Some seeds were removed on purpose"
	quest.24AE5486AE474342.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r seeds for uranium, uraninite, osmium, fluorite, silicon, steel, aluminum, graphite, platinum, iridium, refined obsidian and refined glowstone don't exist in this pack. Click the checkmark when you've read why."
		"&eHow:&r if JEI shows no altar recipe for a crop, it's one of these. Get them from ore processing and the reactors in the main quests."
		"&eTip:&r iron, copper, tin, lead, gold and other everyday metals are still farmable, behind their circuit gates."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&eDeep dive: why these metals?&r"
		"Each blocked resource is the reason a tier exists. Steel needs carbon from coke and an oxygen-controlled furnace; aluminum needs electrolysis of molten alumina (Hall-Héroult, 2Al₂O₃ → 4Al + 3O₂)."
		"Silicon is reduced from quartz with carbon at about 2000 °C (SiO₂ + 2C → Si + 2CO). Fluorite is the fluorine source for uranium enrichment; uranium and uraninite are the nuclear chain."
		"Platinum and iridium come from the PGM line: anode sludge, aqua regia, ammonium hexachloroplatinate, calcining. Graphite and osmium gate Mekanism and MI steps."
		"Growing them on a plant would skip the chemistry those tiers teach. Everything else stays farmable, so farming saves time without replacing a single reaction."
	]
	quest.31B95BF1B78FC771.title: "Watering Can"
	quest.31B95BF1B78FC771.quest_subtitle: "Water speeds up growth"
	quest.31B95BF1B78FC771.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r right-click to water crops in an area, which makes them grow faster while you hold it."
		"&eHow:&r iron ingots, a bowl and bone meal (check JEI). Fill it from any water source."
		"&eTip:&r stand in the middle of the field and hold right-click."
	]
	quest.2AE6F05324BA2C59.title: "Inferium Ingots"
	quest.2AE6F05324BA2C59.quest_subtitle: "The metal for Mystical Agriculture gear"
	quest.2AE6F05324BA2C59.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r essence-infused ingots for tools, armour and the better watering cans."
		"&eHow:&r a prosperity ingot plus 2 inferium essence (check JEI for the prosperity ingot)."
		"&eTip:&r each essence tier has its own ingot; JEI shows the upgrade path."
	]
	quest.3BC7002FEB68725F.title: "Inferium Watering Can"
	quest.3BC7002FEB68725F.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a bigger watering area"
	quest.3BC7002FEB68725F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a tiered watering can covers a larger area and works faster."
		"&eHow:&r your watering can, inferium ingots and mystical fertilizer (check JEI). The higher tiers repeat the pattern."
		"&eTip:&r the can keeps its contents when upgraded."
	]
	quest.08F7E833C88C6704.title: "A Lucky Harvest"
	quest.08F7E833C88C6704.quest_subtitle: "Secret: a rare drop from the field"
	quest.08F7E833C88C6704.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r crops sometimes drop Fertilized Essence. You found one."
		"&eHow:&r it crafts into mystical fertilizer (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r more crops means more chances; a big inferium field pays for itself."
	]
	quest.1A6616EA3169DE4E.title: "Soulstone"
	quest.1A6616EA3169DE4E.quest_subtitle: "A Nether stone with something inside"
	quest.1A6616EA3169DE4E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r soulstone clusters generate in the Nether. A few of their blocks are soulium ore, the source of soulium dust."
		"&eHow:&r mine soulstone in the Nether and watch for soulium ore (check JEI for its drops)."
		"&eTip:&r a soulium ingot is a prosperity ingot plus 2 soulium dust; soul dust (for soul glass) comes from smelting smooth soulstone."
	]
	quest.0A1E76D6BAED16FB.title: "Soulium Dagger"
	quest.0A1E76D6BAED16FB.quest_subtitle: "A blade that collects souls"
	quest.0A1E76D6BAED16FB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r kills with this dagger capture the mob's soul into a Soul Jar in your inventory."
		"&eHow:&r a golden sword, soulium ingots and soulium dust (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r carry 4 Soul Jars for four mob types; the Soul Extractor fills jars from drops instead of kills."
	]
	quest.428E72DF157C0E84.title: "Soul Jars"
	quest.428E72DF157C0E84.quest_subtitle: "Glass that holds a mob's essence"
	quest.428E72DF157C0E84.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r each jar stores souls of one mob type. Full jars are the material for mob seeds."
		"&eHow:&r soul glass (soul dust around glass) and a soulium ingot (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r carry one empty jar per mob type you're hunting."
	]
	quest.26B2F788E44A88FF.title: "Fill a Jar"
	quest.26B2F788E44A88FF.quest_subtitle: "Kill 20 zombies with the dagger"
	quest.26B2F788E44A88FF.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fill a Soul Jar with zombie souls for zombie seeds (rotten flesh)."
		"&eHow:&r keep an empty Soul Jar in your inventory and kill zombies with the Soulium Dagger."
		"&eTip:&r the Soul Extractor can also pull souls out of mob drops like rotten flesh (check JEI)."
	]
	quest.7BF7865AB438BD4F.title: "Mob Seeds"
	quest.7BF7865AB438BD4F.quest_subtitle: "Grow mob drops without the mobs"
	quest.7BF7865AB438BD4F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r mob seeds start from a Soulium Seed Base and grow drops like rotten flesh, bones and string."
		"&eHow:&r a prosperity seed base plus 2 soulium dust. On the altar, put it in the middle and the full jars and essence on the pedestals (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r zombie, skeleton, spider and creeper are tier 3, so they also need an analog circuit."
	]
	quest.0D456A2E999CC4F8.title: "Machine Frame"
	quest.0D456A2E999CC4F8.quest_subtitle: "The base of Mystical Agriculture machines"
	quest.0D456A2E999CC4F8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the shared frame for the Harvester, Soul Extractor, Seed Reprocessor and other MA machines."
		"&eHow:&r iron, redstone and stone (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r MA machines run on Forge Energy, so they plug into any FE cable."
	]
	quest.4E7A8526103C06DE.title: "Harvester"
	quest.4E7A8526103C06DE.quest_subtitle: "Harvests and replants a field"
	quest.4E7A8526103C06DE.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Harvester picks mature crops in an area in front of it and replants them, pushing drops into its inventory."
		"&eHow:&r machine frame, soulium ingots, iron and two diamond scythes (check JEI). Power it with FE."
		"&eTip:&r pipe its output into storage and the field runs itself."
	]
	quest.1AB94C1A78E23821.title: "Soul Extractor"
	quest.1AB94C1A78E23821.quest_subtitle: "Souls from mob drops"
	quest.1AB94C1A78E23821.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r fills Soul Jars from mob drops (rotten flesh, bones, string and more) instead of kills."
		"&eHow:&r machine frame, soulium ingots, iron and a soulium dagger (check JEI). Power it with FE."
		"&eTip:&r feed it drops from an HNN Simulation Chamber for a fully passive soul supply."
	]
	quest.2E34A7CBAE7C47D5.title: "A Pot Farm"
	quest.2E34A7CBAE7C47D5.quest_subtitle: "Eight hopper pots of resource crops"
	quest.2E34A7CBAE7C47D5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mystical Agriculture seeds grow in Hopper Botany Pots, which harvest by themselves into a chest below."
		"&eHow:&r put each pot on a hopper, pipe or chest, add dirt or farmland and a seed. Hold any MA seed in JEI to see its pot growth time."
		"&eTip:&r a column of pots over one shared item pipe is a compact essence farm for every tier."
	]
	quest.65BFEDF064434795.title: "Infusion Pedestals"
	quest.65BFEDF064434795.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a full ring around the altar"
	quest.65BFEDF064434795.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the altar takes its eight side ingredients from the pedestals around it. Every seed recipe uses all eight."
		"&eHow:&r each pedestal is gold, red wool and stone (check JEI). Place them as JEI shows around the altar."
		"&eTip:&r a hopper or pipe into the altar's centre makes repeat seeds easier."
	]
	quest.6950DD2DF950738A.title: "Better Farmland"
	quest.6950DD2DF950738A.quest_subtitle: "Upgrade the soil under your inferium"
	quest.6950DD2DF950738A.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r higher-tier farmland makes inferium crops drop more essence: prudentium, tertium, imperium or supremium."
		"&eHow:&r one essence of the tier plus farmland (shapeless), or till dirt with a hoe and the essence."
		"&eTip:&r it only boosts inferium crops; resource crops grow the same on any farmland."
	]
	quest.7FD7ED0A2D0B0532.title: "Stronger Accelerators"
	quest.7FD7ED0A2D0B0532.quest_subtitle: "Faster growth from below"
	quest.7FD7ED0A2D0B0532.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r higher-tier growth accelerators reach further and tick crops more often."
		"&eHow:&r essence of the tier around stone and that tier's gemstone (makes 3; check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r stack them in a column under the crop; each tier adds range."
	]
	quest.62D1ADC312A36564.title: "Inferium Armour"
	quest.62D1ADC312A36564.quest_subtitle: "Armor grown from a field"
	quest.62D1ADC312A36564.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r Mystical Agriculture armor in six tiers, from inferium to awakened supremium. Higher tiers hold augments."
		"&eHow:&r a diamond armor piece with two ingots and two gemstones of the tier (it keeps the item's enchantments). Each tier upgrades the last."
		"&eTip:&r higher tiers also take augments; see the Augments quest."
	]
	quest.118A7C8F362C4A22.title: "Inferium Tools"
	quest.118A7C8F362C4A22.quest_subtitle: "Swords, bows and a fishing rod"
	quest.118A7C8F362C4A22.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r essence swords, bows, crossbows and fishing rods, upgraded tier by tier like the armor."
		"&eHow:&r the diamond (or plain) item with two ingots and two gemstones of the tier (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r a sword with the Mystical Enlightenment enchantment can collect Cognizant Dust from bosses."
	]
	quest.74CC190A40E105C8.title: "Augments"
	quest.74CC190A40E105C8.quest_subtitle: "Add powers to essence gear"
	quest.74CC190A40E105C8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r augments add effects to essence tools and armor (speed, night vision, mining area and more). The Tinkering Table fits them."
		"&eHow:&r an Unattuned Augment is prosperity shards and iron; attune it on the altar (check JEI). The Tinkering Table fits it."
		"&eTip:&r higher gear tiers have more augment slots."
	]
	quest.36C94540F248019D.title: "Seed Reprocessor"
	quest.36C94540F248019D.quest_subtitle: "Spare seeds back into essence"
	quest.36C94540F248019D.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r grinds surplus resource seeds back into the essence they're made of, powered by FE."
		"&eHow:&r a machine frame with soulium ingots, iron and 2 iron hoes."
		"&eTip:&r feed it the extra seeds from a pot farm and nothing goes to waste."
	]
	quest.15A2839EEA20814E.title: "Essence Furnace"
	quest.15A2839EEA20814E.quest_subtitle: "An electric furnace"
	quest.15A2839EEA20814E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a powered furnace that smelts with FE instead of burning fuel."
		"&eChemistry:&r an electric furnace heats by resistance: current through a wire, P = I²R. No combustion, no CO₂ at the furnace."
		"&eHow:&r a machine frame with iron, prosperity ingots and 2 furnaces."
	]
	quest.04376C3B679506E2.title: "Essence Enchanter"
	quest.04376C3B679506E2.quest_subtitle: "Optional: enchant with essence, not luck"
	quest.04376C3B679506E2.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r applies the enchantment you pick, paid for with experience essence plus an item for each enchantment (check JEI for the costs)."
		"&eHow:&r an enchanting table on a soulium ingot over 3 soulstone."
		"&eTip:&r it's the easy way to put Mystical Enlightenment on a sword."
	]
	quest.4CFD3DC3D0DD7BAA.title: "Experience Capsule"
	quest.4CFD3DC3D0DD7BAA.quest_subtitle: "Optional: bottle your levels"
	quest.4CFD3DC3D0DD7BAA.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r stores experience points picked up while it's in your inventory, to spend later."
		"&eHow:&r 2 soulium ingots and 2 soul glass."
	]
	quest.16715B6E6324D65F.title: "Soulium Spawner"
	quest.16715B6E6324D65F.quest_subtitle: "Mobs from essence"
	quest.16715B6E6324D65F.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a powered spawner that turns mob essence into living mobs (JEI's Soulium Spawner page lists what each costs)."
		"&eHow:&r a machine frame with iron, soulium ingots and 2 wither skeleton skulls."
		"&eTip:&r pair it with a mob grinder for drops crops can't grow, like XP."
	]
	quest.5CA7AAE7C8DAE7C6.title: "Awakening Rig"
	quest.5CA7AAE7C8DAE7C6.quest_subtitle: "Pedestals and vessels for the altar"
	quest.5CA7AAE7C8DAE7C6.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Awakening Altar is fed by 4 Awakening Pedestals and 4 Essence Vessels holding air, earth, water and fire essence."
		"&eHow:&r both are gold and soulstone, with orange wool (pedestal) or glass (vessel). JEI shows the layout."
		"&eTip:&r fill the vessels before you start; awakening drains a lot of elemental essence."
	]
	quest.4449C276C65D5AC5.title: "Witherproof Bricks"
	quest.4449C276C65D5AC5.quest_subtitle: "Optional: an arena the Wither can't break"
	quest.4449C276C65D5AC5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r bricks the Wither's skulls can't destroy: build a box and fight it on your terms."
		"&eHow:&r a witherproof block is soulstone in wither skeleton essence (a tier 5 crop); 4 blocks make 4 bricks."
		"&eTip:&r the Seed of a New World needs Nether Stars, so a safe Wither arena pays for itself."
	]
	quest.79AB7DDCFF409FB4.title: "Cognizant Dust"
	quest.79AB7DDCFF409FB4.quest_subtitle: "Knowledge from a boss"
	quest.79AB7DDCFF409FB4.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember learning from the strongest things you fought. Some of it is still on the floor.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Cognizant Dust drops from the Wither and the Ender Dragon when they die to an essence weapon with Mystical Enlightenment."
		"&eHow:&r enchant an essence sword in the Essence Enchanter, then land the last hit on a boss with it."
		"&eTip:&r it goes into awakened supremium: JEI shows the awakening recipe."
	]
	quest.15FA433BAA48EBD5.title: "Seeds of Something"
	quest.15FA433BAA48EBD5.quest_subtitle: "Any seed: the start of every crop"
	quest.15FA433BAA48EBD5.quest_desc: [
		"&6You remember coaxing metal out of the ground like wheat. Some of that still works.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r Mystical Agriculture grows resources as crops. This page climbs its five essence tiers and lists every seed this pack allows."
		"&eChemistry:&r a real plant only builds itself from CO₂, water and a few soil minerals. Growing iron from a seed is the magic part; the circuit gates are the chemistry part."
		"&eHow:&r pick up any seed. Wheat seeds from grass are fine."
		"&eTip:&r seeds for uranium, osmium, fluorite and the other chemistry milestones don't exist here, by design."
	]
	quest.45E0631479F7028C.title: "Prosperity Seed Base"
	quest.45E0631479F7028C.quest_subtitle: "The core of every resource seed"
	quest.45E0631479F7028C.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r every resource seed is crafted around a seed base on the Infusion Altar."
		"&eHow:&r 4 prosperity shards around wheat seeds."
		"&eTip:&r make a stack; each new seed type costs one."
	]
	quest.01B64DF2B4F90172.title: "Inferium Essence"
	quest.01B64DF2B4F90172.quest_subtitle: "Tier 1 essence"
	quest.01B64DF2B4F90172.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the first essence. Everything on this page is built from it, and every higher essence is made from four of the tier below."
		"&eHow:&r mine inferium ore (or kill mobs, which drop a little). 8 essence around wheat seeds make Inferium Seeds."
		"&eTip:&r a big inferium field is the engine of the whole page."
	]
	quest.52DDF7E1181D8095.title: "The Wand"
	quest.52DDF7E1181D8095.quest_subtitle: "Optional: start the altar's crafting"
	quest.52DDF7E1181D8095.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the wand activates the Infusion and Awakening Altars when the ingredients are in place."
		"&eHow:&r check JEI; it's cheap."
		"&eTip:&r a redstone signal on the altar also starts it, which is handy for automation."
	]
	quest.31AB68F6A9DF88E1.title: "A Sickle"
	quest.31AB68F6A9DF88E1.quest_subtitle: "Harvest crops and leaves in an area"
	quest.31AB68F6A9DF88E1.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a sickle breaks plants, leaves and grass in a radius around the block you hit."
		"&eHow:&r any sickle counts: wood up to diamond, or the essence ones (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r great for clearing a jungle canopy."
	]
	quest.52DFA7A5E92C41FB.title: "A Scythe"
	quest.52DFA7A5E92C41FB.quest_subtitle: "Harvest and replant a field"
	quest.52DFA7A5E92C41FB.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a scythe harvests mature crops in an area and replants them in one swing."
		"&eHow:&r any scythe counts (check JEI). Two diamond scythes also go into the Harvester."
		"&eTip:&r right-click a mature crop to harvest just that one and replant it."
	]
	quest.74E64D307110C738.title: "Machine Upgrades"
	quest.74E64D307110C738.quest_subtitle: "Faster machines, one tier at a time"
	quest.74E64D307110C738.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r machine upgrades make the MA machines (furnace, harvester, reprocessor, spawner, extractor) faster and wider-reaching."
		"&eHow:&r essence of the tier around a prosperity ingot or the previous upgrade (check JEI). Any tier counts."
		"&eTip:&r one upgrade slot per machine: put your best one where the bottleneck is."
	]
	quest.5A5636B64B51BFC8.title: "Tinkering Table"
	quest.5A5636B64B51BFC8.quest_subtitle: "Fit augments to essence gear"
	quest.5A5636B64B51BFC8.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the Tinkering Table puts augments into essence tools and armour."
		"&eHow:&r stone and soulium dust (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r higher gear tiers have more augment slots."
	]
	quest.552E759FEEB78088.title: "A Block of Awakened Supremium"
	quest.552E759FEEB78088.quest_subtitle: "Nine of the best ingots"
	quest.552E759FEEB78088.quest_desc: [
		"&6The garden answers you fully now. You remember this: patience, then plenty.&r"
		"&eWhat:&r a storage block of awakened supremium ingots: proof you've run the whole essence ladder."
		"&eHow:&r 9 awakened supremium ingots."
		"&eTip:&r the ingots also upgrade gear to the awakened tier, so only block your spares."
	]
	quest.779DCC201D370F42.title: "Prudentium Armour"
	quest.779DCC201D370F42.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a full essence set"
	quest.779DCC201D370F42.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the prudentium armour set. Each tier adds protection and augment slots."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade the previous tier's pieces with this tier's ingots and gemstones (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r augments go in at the Tinkering Table."
	]
	quest.430D372C1DC73DA5.title: "Prudentium Tools"
	quest.430D372C1DC73DA5.quest_subtitle: "Any one essence tool of this tier"
	quest.430D372C1DC73DA5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r any prudentium tool: sword, pick, axe, shovel, hoe, sickle, scythe, shears, bow, crossbow, fishing rod or watering can."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade the previous tier's tool with this tier's ingots and gemstones (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the sickle and scythe harvest crops in an area and replant them."
	]
	quest.7F020261C90E336E.title: "Tertium Farmland"
	quest.7F020261C90E336E.quest_subtitle: "Soil for tier 3 crops"
	quest.7F020261C90E336E.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r farmland infused with tertium essence. Inferium crops on it drop more essence, and the tier 3 seeds on this page hang off it."
		"&eHow:&r tertium essence and farmland, shapeless (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r convert the soil under your inferium field first; that's where it pays."
	]
	quest.184BB321A7001B55.title: "Tertium Growth Accelerator"
	quest.184BB321A7001B55.quest_subtitle: "Faster crops from below"
	quest.184BB321A7001B55.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r a growth accelerator placed under farmland ticks the crops above it; higher tiers reach further."
		"&eHow:&r tertium essence around stone and the tier's gemstone (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r stack them in a column under the crop."
	]
	quest.281B06EAD9BED5D4.title: "Tertium Armour"
	quest.281B06EAD9BED5D4.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a full essence set"
	quest.281B06EAD9BED5D4.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r the tertium armour set. Each tier adds protection and augment slots."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade the previous tier's pieces with this tier's ingots and gemstones (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r augments go in at the Tinkering Table."
	]
	quest.6DC7CB8F240C93CC.title: "Tertium Tools"
	quest.6DC7CB8F240C93CC.quest_subtitle: "Any one essence tool of this tier"
	quest.6DC7CB8F240C93CC.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r any tertium tool: sword, pick, axe, shovel, hoe, sickle, scythe, shears, bow, crossbow, fishing rod or watering can."
		"&eHow:&r upgrade the previous tier's tool with this tier's ingots and gemstones (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r the sickle and scythe harvest crops in an area and replant them."
	]
	quest.38F46E6A1DC59E74.title: "Imperium Farmland"
	quest.38F46E6A1DC59E74.quest_subtitle: "Soil for tier 4 crops"
	quest.38F46E6A1DC59E74.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhat:&r farmland infused with imperium essence. Inferium crops on it drop more essence, and the tier 4 seeds on this page hang off it."
		"&eHow:&r imperium essence and farmland, shapeless (check JEI)."
		"&eTip:&r convert the soil under your inferium field first; that's where it pays."
	]
	quest.7355A556382039F6.title: "Imperium Growth Accelerator"
	quest.7355A556382039F6.quest_subtitle: "Faster crops from below"
